PVD("malaysia_ndp_2011-2015",{"docs":["","Malaysia NDP 2011 15"],"s":{"1":[[1,"146","2","Oil and Gas Industry Development and Local Capacity Building","PETRONAS, the national oil corporation, plays a major role in driving the industry growth through its development of oil and gas resources as well as creation of opportunities for local companies to build up their capacity and capability across the value chain.",""],[1,"146","3","Petrochemical Industry Investment and Export Target","During the Plan period, the investment target in petrochemical industry has been set at RM11.3 billion annually and exports from this industry are expected to reach RM27.7 billion in 2015.",""],[1,"146","4","Domestic Resource and Infrastructure Development Acceleration","Malaysia will accelerate and optimise the development of remaining domestic reserves and existing infrastructure",""],[1,"146","4","Regional and Global Champion Development in Business Sectors","support the formation of regional and global champions in contiguous business sectors",""],[1,"146","8","Downstream Petrochemical Linkage Enhancement","Enhancing linkages in the downstream industries to optimise resources, facilities and services available at the integrated petrochemical complex;",""],[1,"146","10","Oil and Gas Professional Services Strengthening and International Champion Development","Strengthening oil and gas related professional services and creating international champions such as in OFSE, those related to deep water extraction and integrated service providers.",""]],"2":[[1,"52","2","Government Transformation Based on Four Core Principles","the Government of Malaysia will undertake a transformation on the basis of four key principles, namely a culture of creativity and innovation, speed of decision making and execution, value for money and integrity.",""],[1,"52","9","Public Service Delivery Competitiveness Enhancement","Therefore, the efficiency and timeliness of Government procedures will be benchmarked to international comparisons.",""],[1,"53","7","Public Sector Talent Attraction Initiative","During the Plan period, a special focus will be given towards attracting top talent for the public sector.",""],[1,"88","8","Government Transformation for Economic Facilitation and Quality Service Delivery","The role of government will evolve to become an effective facilitator in the transformation of the economy and provide quality services to the rakyat.",""]],"3":[[1,"337","4","Whole-of-Government Coordination Approach","A whole-of-government approach will be adopted to ensure cross-cutting issues are addressed with a focus on the people as customers.",""],[1,"345","1","Consultative Policy Development Approach","The Government will adopt a more consultative approach and proactively seek input and feedback from multiple stakeholders from within government, the private sector and non-government organisations (NGOs) in the development of government policies, plans and programmes.",""],[1,"345","2","Government Transformation Programme","Developing the Government Trans- formation Programme (GTP).",""],[1,"345","4","Tenth Malaysia Plan Development Process","Developing the Tenth Malaysia Plan.",""],[1,"352","4","Technical Working Groups for Strategy and Implementation Plan Development","technical working groups are formed to develop strategies and plans to deliver the outcomes identified for all priorities.",""],[1,"353","6","Integrated Planning and Cross-Agency Coordination Approach","Greater coordination across agencies at an earlier stage will ensure more effective use of resources.",""],[1,"365","8","Inter-Agency and Multi-Level Government Coordination Strengthening","Collaboration across agencies and between federal, state and local governments will also be strengthened particularly on national priorities.",""],[1,"365","8","Prime Minister-Led Delivery Taskforces for NKRAs","Lean, dynamic governance structures with representation from all constituents, such as the Prime Minister-led delivery taskforces for NKRAs will be used to drive the delivery of high priority",""],[1,"366","17","Cross-Agency Working Teams for National Priorities","Labs consisting of cross-agency working teams will be more frequently deployed to deliver national priorities that cut across federal, state and local government responsibilities.",""]],"4":[[1,"3","2","Government Transformation Programme Alignment","The national development programmes are attuned to the six National Key Results Areas, outlined in the Government Transformation Programme, the National Key Economic Areas of the Economic Transformation Programme and the strategic economic reforms in the New Economic Model.",""],[1,"3","2","Government Regulatory and Service Delivery Reform","The Plan details strategies towards a more focused role for the Government as a regulator and catalyst while upholding the principles of 1Malaysia: People First, Performance Now to ensure effective delivery of services.",""],[1,"337","6","Creative and Innovative Public Service Reform","Developing a public service that thinks outside the box by using creative and innovative methods within the Government's processes, systems and policies to deliver solutions.",""],[1,"339","1","Transformational Public Service Initiatives","During the Plan period, the Government will embark on a series of transformational initiatives to respond to the needs of the people and business, including:",""],[1,"339","7","Customer-Oriented Government Service Delivery Reform","Government service delivery will be designed to provide people and business with efficient and convenient services based on understanding and anticipating customer needs.",""],[1,"363","1","Bureaucracy Reduction and Government Interface Improvement","Efforts will be directed towards reducing bureaucracy and improving the interface between government and people, and government and businesses, where a higher level of inter-agency collaboration and cooperation will be adopted.",""],[1,"363","2","Rationalisation of Government Organisations and Structures","Rationalising existing government organisations and structures;",""],[1,"363","3","Capacity Building for Priority-Focused Organizations","Building capacity in organisations focused on national priorities;",""],[1,"363","7","Comprehensive Audit and Rationalisation of Government Agencies","During the Plan period, a comprehensive audit of all government organisations and structures will be carried out looking across government roles, functions, gaps and overlaps.",""],[1,"363","7","Government Agency Rationalisation Plan","The objective of this will be to develop a plan for rationalising agencies with overlapping or redundant functions to align the structure of government with contribution to GDP and national priorities.",""],[1,"363","7","Reallocation of Manpower to Priority Areas","The extra manpower resulting from this rationalisation will be redirected from lower priority to priority areas.",""],[1,"364","2","Streamlining of Diplomatic Missions and Overseas Offices","Efforts will be made to streamline diplomatic missions and all other Malaysian offices abroad to optimise deployment of human resources in the public service.",""],[1,"364","3","Strengthening Priority Delivery Agencies","The ministries and agencies responsible for facilitating and delivering top national priorities will be strengthened.",""],[1,"364","3","Redirecting Talent, Funding, and Leadership to Priority Agencies","Top talent, funding and leadership attention will be redirected to these agencies.",""],[1,"364","3","Refining and Expanding Agency Mandates","several agencies will have their mandates refined or expanded to reflect new priorities.",""],[1,"370","1","Public Sector Transformation for Whole-of-Government Delivery","The public sector must transform to effectively respond to a rapidly evolving global environment.",""],[1,"370","2","Customer-Oriented Public Sector Reform","Public sector reforms will be customer-oriented, with delivery systems and interfaces improved and centred around people and businesses.",""],[1,"370","2","Agency Empowerment and Accountability Reform","To enable greater speed of decision-making and execution, greater empowerment will be provided to selected agencies tied to increased accountability and capability.",""],[1,"370","2","Autonomy for Operating Agencies","Further, greater autonomy will be provided to operating agencies, such as universities and hospitals to increase responsiveness to the customer.",""],[1,"370","2","Performance Competition and Demand-Side Financing Reform","To enhance delivery, competition and market mechanisms will increasingly be introduced, such as league tables for police stations and schools and demand-side financing for universities and training institutions.",""],[1,"370","4","Public Sector Efficiency and Shared Services Reform","The Government will also focus on improving its fiscal position during the Plan period, broadening the tax base through more effective collection, achieving productivity gains in the public sector by consolidating infrastructure requirements and introducing shared services as well as driving efficiencies in procurement and ICT management.",""],[1,"371","1","Public Service Rationalisation and Talent Development","particularly those with overlapping or redundant functions, to be rationalised.",""],[1,"371","1","Strengthening Priority-Focused Organisations","Organisations focused on national priorities will be strengthened",""]],"5":[[1,"4","1","Integrated First-World Talent Development and Retention Approach","To achieve this, an integrated approach to nurturing, attracting and retaining first-world talent base will be implemented.",""],[1,"36","2","Talent Corporation for Diaspora Talent Sourcing","The Government will establish a Talent Corporation, which will have as one of its key functions, the task of actively sourcing top talent including among the Malaysian diaspora.",""],[1,"363","5","Public Service Talent Attraction, Development and Retention","Attracting, developing and retaining top talent in the public service.",""],[1,"364","4","Talent Corporation Establishment","A new independent Talent Corporation will be established in 2011.",""],[1,"366","19","Public Service Talent Development and Retention Strategy","During the Plan period, the following strategies will be implemented to develop and retain top talent in the public service:",""],[1,"366","20","Public Service Performance Culture Strengthening","Strengthening the performance culture within the public service;",""],[1,"367","2","Public Sector Lateral Hiring and Exchange Programme","Injecting best practices into the public sector through lateral hires and exchange programmes;",""],[1,"367","3","Flexible Public Service Scheme Design","Designing flexible schemes of service to effectively match talent and experience with the requirements of the public service;",""],[1,"367","4","Capacity-Building Programme Realignment","Realigning capacity-building programmes to meet job requirements.",""],[1,"367","5","Public Service Delivery-Oriented Culture and Collaboration Reform","the public service will continue to enhance its culture, mindset and practices to be delivery-oriented, highly collaborative and seamless across jurisdictional and functional boundaries and across every level of government.",""],[1,"367","7","Public Service Performance Incentives and Evaluation Reform","Rewards, such as accelerated career tracks, higher performance bonuses and high- profile recognition will be accorded for outstanding performance.",""],[1,"367","7","Annual Performance Evaluation Report Improvement","The Annual Performance Evaluation Report will be improved in order to incorporate more objective measures that are linked to ministry or agency specific KPIs.",""],[1,"367","7","Public Service Exit Policy Review","the Government will review exit policies and mechanisms, such as voluntary separation schemes to remove underperforming personnel from the service.",""],[1,"367","8","Public Sector Talent Attraction and Scholarship Programme","During the Plan period, the Government will continue to strengthen this scholarship programme with a target to provide 60,000 local and overseas scholarships, an increase of 27% of scholarships offered compared to the previous Ninth Plan.",""],[1,"367","8","Talent Scouting and Recruitment Programme","In addition, talent scouting programmes will continue to be strengthened to identify, attract and recruit non-",""],[1,"368","2","Flexible Scholarship Scheme Reform","Moving forward, the Government will continue to strengthen its scholarship programme by increasingly offering flexible scholarship schemes that provide graduates with excellent result the flexibility to serve part of their bonds in GLCs or in the private sector.",""],[1,"368","2","Fast Track Career Progression Path","To identify and groom outstanding young talent, a fast track career progression path will be introduced.",""],[1,"368","3","Nationwide Teaching Profession Marketing Campaign","One such effort is the high-profile nationwide marketing campaign to position the teaching profession as one that is financially attractive, nation-building, career-building and prestigious.",""],[1,"368","3","Public Service Rebranding and Promotional Exercise","During the Plan period, the public service will similarly undergo a rebranding and promotional exercise to redefine the image of the civil service as one composed of the best and brightest talents in Malaysia.",""],[1,"368","4","Lateral Hiring and Multiple Entry Point Recruitment Scheme","Lateral hiring from the private sector will be expanded to attract high calibre individuals into key strategic posts within the Government.",""],[1,"368","5","Cross-Fertilisation Mobility Programme","During the Plan period, this cross-fertilisation programme will be expanded and enhanced to allow for one to two years of mobility between the public sector, GLCs and the private sector.",""],[1,"368","6","Public Service Career Scheme Reform","the public service will introduce schemes of service that will ensure that both content specialists and generalists are provided with competitive career",""],[1,"369","1","Public Service Talent Optimization and Senior Position Opening","The Government will implement measures to optimise the usage of these talents, matching placements within the service to their qualifications and preferences.",""],[1,"369","2","Public Service Scheme Rationalisation and New Service Scheme Creation","Schemes of service will be rationalised and new service schemes created to reflect changing job descriptions and the new skills required.",""],[1,"369","2","Multi-skilling Workforce Training Initiative","To create a more adaptable workforce, individuals should be trained to carry out a variety of roles and functions.",""],[1,"369","2","Multi-skilling Requirements Study","a study on multi-skilling requirements will be undertaken.",""],[1,"369","3","Public Service Skills Training Enhancement","skills training programmes for existing personnel will be enhanced.",""],[1,"369","4","In-Service Training Programme Reform","Training programmes will be reviewed and aligned with personalised on-the-job needs.",""],[1,"369","4","World-Class Civil Service College Establishment","The Government will establish a world-class civil service college, leveraging on existing physical facilities.",""],[1,"371","1","Public Service Talent Development","talent in the public service will continue to be developed.",""]],"7":[[1,"53","6","Procurement Efficiency and Transparency Reform","To achieve this, the Government will focus on efforts to reduce subsidies, drive efficiencies and transparency in procurement, driving productivity in Information Communications Technology (ICT) and broadening the tax collection base.",""],[1,"106","2","Innovation Incentives through Public Procurement and Regulation Design","The Government will deliberately act to create incentives and opportunities for Malaysian companies to invest in innovation, through the public procurement process and the design of regulations.",""],[1,"106","3","Public Procurement Reform for Innovation and Competition","Additionally, procurement will be used to create demand for innovation and push SMEs to develop products in areas that are of benefit to the nation and have larger commercial potential, as shown in Box 3-2.",""],[1,"200","5","Administrative Tendering Process Improvement","Improving existing administrative processes to reduce time required for the tendering process;",""],[1,"200","7","Programme Management and Project Governance Strengthening","Establishing effective programme management and governance of projects.",""],[1,"349","3","MyProcurement Portal Public Tender Information System","Information on government tenders including tender advertisements and successful bidders can be accessed by the public through MyProcurement Portal effective April 1st, 2010;",""],[1,"349","6","Whistleblower Protection Framework","a comprehensive whistleblower protection framework will be established to cover members of the private and public sectors who disclose wrongdoings as well as those who are required to assist in investigations",""],[1,"349","7","Convicted Offender Publication and Corruption Case Expediting Measures","Malaysian Anti-Corruption Commission (MACC) has begun publishing a webpage with the names of all convicted offenders, and a court circular has been issued to all judges requesting for all corruption cases to be completed within one year.",""],[1,"349","8","Anti-Corruption and Integrity Strengthening Efforts","Efforts to combat corruption will focus on:",""],[1,"349","9","Compliance and Monitoring Strengthening","compliance and monitoring will be strengthened to take action on reported instances of abuse of discretionary power.",""],[1,"349","9","Inspection of Enforcement Processes in Customer-Facing Agencies","Compliance efforts within customer- facing agencies will be strengthened through regular inspection of enforcement processes,",""],[1,"350","3","Anti-Malpractice and Abuse of Power Reporting Initiative","Initiatives will also be taken to strengthen and empower agencies to report and take action in cases of malpractice, misconduct or abuse of power;",""],[1,"350","4","Government Procurement Transparency Initiative","Ensuring transparency in the award of government contracts.",""],[1,"350","5","High-Level Corruption Prevention and Whistleblower Protection","Tackling high-level corruption to prevent the abuse of power and misuse of public resources.",""],[1,"350","8","Government Transparency and Accountability Enhancement","Efforts to create greater transparency and accountability will be enhanced, including through the continued public release of the Auditor-General Reports and the establishment of the MyProcurement",""],[1,"350","9","Competitive Government Procurement Reform","Government contracts will be procured through competitive bidding adhering to standard guidelines and policies;",""],[1,"350","10","Anti-Corruption Enforcement and Faster Trial Processing","Enforcing swift and stiffer punishments to deter corrupt practices.",""],[1,"351","1","Publication of Convicted Offenders' Names","This effort has already begun with the MACC's initiative to publish the names of convicted offenders on their website;",""],[1,"351","2","Zero-Tolerance Anti-Corruption Policy","The Government will adopt a zero tolerance policy towards corruption with a clear stance that no individual is above the law and all reported cases of corruption will be fully investigated.",""],[1,"351","2","Public Anti-Corruption Awareness Campaigns","campaigns will be launched to increase awareness of the public on the important role that they can play in combating corruption;",""],[1,"351","3","Anti-Corruption Institutions Review and Strengthening","The Government will undertake a comprehensive review of the institutions at the frontline of combating corruption with the objective of developing ways to promote the independence and empowerment of these institutions;",""],[1,"351","4","Tekad Integriti Action Plan","Towards this end, the Tekad Integriti action plan will be introduced as an enhancement to Tekad 2008.",""],[1,"360","3","Transparency and Efficiency Improvement Measures","To achieve greater value-for-money, the Government has taken measures to increase transparency and efficiency with a commitment to maintain integrity among all parties.",""],[1,"361","5","Transparent Competitive Public Procurement Reporting","Ensuring contracts are conducted in a transparent manner using competitive bidding, and publicly reporting the names of awarded parties and the value of each award on the MyProcurement Portal.",""]],"10":[[1,"36","1","Bilateral Infrastructure Project Collaboration","At a government-to- government level, efforts to deepen collaboration will be intensified, specifically in undertaking infrastructure projects.",""],[1,"36","1","Railway Infrastructure Collaboration with China","leveraging on China's expertise for Malaysia's railway infrastructure",""],[1,"36","1","Joint Investment Exploration Mechanism","The Government will also pursue bilateral collaboration in jointly undertaking investments.",""]],"11":[[1,"53","6","Subsidy Reduction and Fiscal Consolidation Measures","To achieve this, the Government will focus on efforts to reduce subsidies, drive efficiencies and transparency in procurement, driving productivity in Information Communications Technology (ICT) and broadening the tax collection base.",""],[1,"53","6","Tax Base Expansion Measures","To achieve this, the Government will focus on efforts to reduce subsidies, drive efficiencies and transparency in procurement, driving productivity in Information Communications Technology (ICT) and broadening the tax collection base.",""],[1,"66","2","Fiscal Deficit Reduction and Debt Financing Strategy","The Government is committed to reduce its fiscal deficit to a sustainable level and ensure the Government's current account remains in surplus.",""],[1,"84","1","Fiscal Reform and Broad-Based Tax System Expansion","The Government will continue with fiscal reforms to bring greater value for money to government spending and widen its revenue base, particularly through a more broad-based tax system.",""],[1,"95","4","Subsidy Rationalisation Reform","Removing market distortions by rationalising subsidies;",""],[1,"99","4","Subsidy and Price Control Rationalisation","During the Plan period, subsidies and price controls will be gradually rationalised to remove market distortions, which has already begun with sugar.",""]],"12":[[1,"8","3","Facilitation Fund","Establishing a Facilitation Fund",""],[1,"357","3","Private Sector Participation in National Investment and Public Service Delivery","Increase the role of the private sector in new national investments and delivery of public services;",""],[1,"358","2","Private Sector Participation in Public Goods and Service Delivery","To harness these entrepreneurial characteristics of the private sector in the delivery of public goods and services, the Government will create opportunities for private sector participation in investments and service provision.",""],[1,"358","2","Private Sector Collaboration for Frontline Public Services","These models will not be limited to investments in physical infrastructure, but extended to increase collaboration with the private sector in the delivery of frontline public services.",""],[1,"358","3","Private Sector Policy Consultation Mechanism","Engagement with the private sector, either directly or via industry associations, will be intensified, as it provides broader viewpoints and transparency in developing the way forward.",""],[1,"358","3","Private Sector Input in Policy Formulation","In particular, input will be actively sought in the formulation of policy to ensure that the needs of the private sector are understood and incorporated such that market- friendly environments are created.",""],[1,"358","4","Private Sector Delivery of Frontline Public Services","The Government will carve out a greater role for the private sector in the delivery of frontline public services, both as owners and operators.",""],[1,"358","5","Outsourcing of Non-Core Government Functions","The Government will also increase outsourcing of non-core government functions.",""]],"13":[[1,"96","1","Doing Business Improvement Initiative","By the end of the Plan period, the Government aims to make Malaysia one of the top 10 nations in the world for doing business.",""],[1,"96","2","Comprehensive Review of Business Regulations","the Government will begin with a comprehensive review of business regulations, starting with regulations that impact the NKEAs.",""],[1,"96","3","Regulatory Review and Rationalization","outcomes will be retained, while redundant and outdated regulations will be eliminated.",""],[1,"96","3","Malaysia Productivity Corporation Rebranding and Restructuring","This review will be led by the Malaysia Productivity Corporation (MPC), which will be rebranded and restructured to ensure it has strong capabilities and resources.",""],[1,"96","3","PEMUDAH Complementary Productivity Reform Support","Its work will complement the efforts of PEMUDAH.",""],[1,"96","4","Regulatory Review and Simplification","Review existing regulations with a view to removing unnecessary rules and compliance costs.",""],[1,"97","1","Cost-Benefit Analysis of New Policies and Regulations","Undertake a cost-benefit analysis of new policies and regulations to assess the impact on the economy;",""],[1,"97","3","Productivity Research on SME Regulation Impacts","Undertake relevant productivity research (e.g. the impact of regulations on growth of SMEs);",""],[1,"97","4","Policy and Regulatory Productivity Enhancement Reform","Make recommendations to the Cabinet on policy and regulatory changes that will enhance productivity;",""],[1,"97","9","New Zealand Productivity Commission Establishment","In March 2010, New Zealand announced the establishment of a Productivity Commission that will be modelled closely on that of Australia's.",""],[1,"100","4","Business-Government Interface Improvement Measures","the Government will also undertake a series of actions to improve the interface between business and government to make investing and operating in Malaysia more attractive.",""],[1,"128","6","Annual Investor Location Decision Survey and Benchmarking System","The Government will conduct an annual survey to develop a richer understanding of the drivers of the location decision of investors, companies, and people.",""]],"15":[[1,"92","7","SME Growth and Innovation Support Programme","Developing small and medium enterprises (SMEs) as an engine of growth and innovation by reducing regulatory costs borne by SMEs, building capacity in SMEs, supporting the creation of an entrepreneurial culture, strengthening enabling infrastructure, and enhancing access to financing;",""],[1,"117","3","SME Growth and Innovation Support Initiatives","Towards this end, the following initiatives will be undertaken:",""],[1,"117","4","SME Regulatory Cost Reduction","Reducing the regulatory costs borne by SMEs;",""],[1,"118","4","SME Capacity and Capability Building","Building capacity and capabilities of SMEs;",""],[1,"118","6","SME Support Systems Strengthening","Strengthening support systems for SMEs;",""],[1,"120","5","SME Support System Improvement","The support system for SMEs will be improved on several fronts during the Plan period to allow SMEs to fulfil their potential:",""],[1,"120","6","National Mark Quality Certification Promotion","To increase acceptance of SME products and services, the National Mark quality certification will be further promoted.",""],[1,"120","6","Specialised Retail Outlets for SME Products","Additionally, specialised retail outlets will be established nationwide with private sector participation to promote and market SME products and services;",""],[1,"121","2","Expansion of SME Corp Field Offices and Business Centres","SME Corp. Malaysia will expand field offices with business centres to all states.",""],[1,"121","2","SME Information, Counselling, and Coaching Service","These offices will disseminate information on funding and incentives, provide counselling and coaching, and act as a clearing house for all issues related to SMEs.",""],[1,"122","3","SME Competitive Rating for Enhancement Adoption","Financial institutions will be encouraged to adopt SME Competitive Rating for Enhancement (SCORE), a diagnostic tool for rating SME performance at the firm level, as a complementary tool to assess credit worthiness of SMEs.",""],[1,"122","4","SME Upgrade Support under the SCORE System","With the financial assistance as well as the advisory services and training, it is targeted that 16,000 SMEs will be able to upgrade their business and improve their star rating under the SCORE system in the Plan period.",""],[1,"255","5","SME Development Support Programme","The SME Corp. will assist in the development of capable and resilient SMEs to be competitive in the global market.",""],[1,"255","5","SME Support Services and Infrastructure Package","In addition to providing infrastructure facilities, financial assistance, advisory services, market access and other support programmes, SME Corp. will also implement a Skills Upgrading Programme.",""],[1,"255","5","SME Skills Upgrading Programme","SME Corp. will also implement a Skills Upgrading Programme.",""]],"16":[[1,"4","1","Private Sector Growth Enablement and Regulatory Reform","We will remove structural barriers and outdated regulations in order to create an efficient and flexible business environment for the private sector.",""],[1,"18","22","Far-Reaching Reform Programme","Far reaching programme of reforms will provide the enabling environment for NKEAs to deliver the targeted economic growth",""],[1,"19","22","Segmented Policy Instruments for Business Stages","Policy instruments will be segmented to better meet requirements at the different business stages",""],[1,"32","6","Competition Law Implementation","Specific policy initiatives to be undertaken towards driving the competitiveness of the domestic economy include the implementation of Competition Law, removal of distortionary price controls and advancing liberalisation, especially in the services sector.",""],[1,"32","6","Removal of Distortionary Price Controls","Specific policy initiatives to be undertaken towards driving the competitiveness of the domestic economy include the implementation of Competition Law, removal of distortionary price controls and advancing liberalisation, especially in the services sector.",""],[1,"32","6","Services Sector Liberalisation","Specific policy initiatives to be undertaken towards driving the competitiveness of the domestic economy include the implementation of Competition Law, removal of distortionary price controls and advancing liberalisation, especially in the services sector.",""],[1,"32","6","Regulatory Modernisation for Market Efficiency","The Government will continue to review and modernise regulations, such as labour laws, towards facilitating a well functioning market economy where appropriate price signals will lead to efficient allocation of resources.",""],[1,"33","1","Business Environment Regulatory Reform","Priority will be given to regulations that can materially improve the ease of doing business in Malaysia, towards facilitating greater private investments and enabling the private sector to be the engine of growth.",""],[1,"37","4","Support for New and Competitive Growth Sectors","The Government has a key role to play beyond creating a facilitative environment in terms of also supporting new and competitive growth sectors by providing the policy framework, human capital development, enabling infrastructure and supporting the development of industrial clusters.",""],[1,"37","5","National Key Economic Areas Prioritisation Strategy","Therefore, under the Tenth Plan, the Government will focus its resources towards prioritising specific National Key Economic Areas (NKEAs) as part of the strategy towards greater",""],[1,"38","5","Productivity and Innovation Reform","the Government will, in parallel, drive reform in the major enablers for economic transformation along the value chain.",""],[1,"47","1","Public-Private Smart Partnerships Mechanism","Effective and smart partnerships, particularly between the public and private sector, will be instituted as a mechanism to drive the economic transformation agenda.",""],[1,"47","2","Strategic Private Investment Catalyzation Initiative","Catalysing and accelerating strategic private investments;",""],[1,"47","5","Facilitation Fund for Strategic Private Investment","A key public-private partnership (PPP) initiative under the Tenth Plan will be the creation of a RM20 billion Facilitation Fund to catalyse private investments in nationally strategic areas.",""],[1,"47","8","Public-Private Collaboration for Industry Development","The Government, instead of picking winners, will support the private sector in driving industry development.",""],[1,"48","1","Special Financing Schemes for Knowledge SMEs","the Government will provide special financing schemes and skills training and encourage foreign SMEs to set up operations in Malaysia to develop specialised capabilities.",""],[1,"48","2","Government-Private Sector and GLC Partnership Promotion","The Government will encourage greater collaboration, particularly between Government- linked Companies (GLCs) and the private sector to pursue overseas opportunities.",""],[1,"48","2","Private Sector-GLC Collaboration for New Growth Areas","Private sector- GLC collaboration will also be encouraged in pioneering new growth areas and new markets, where risks are higher and the gestation period is longer.",""],[1,"53","3","Private Sector Growth Facilitation Support Package","driving private sector led growth through increasing the allocation for facilitation support, financing businesses, R&D, entrepreneur development and incentives",""],[1,"80","2","Public-Private Partnership Initiative Programme","The implementation of public-private partnership (PPP) initiatives worth RM62.7 billion will be a key component of the Government's efforts in promoting economic growth through private sector participation.",""],[1,"83","1","Development of New Growth Sources in Healthcare, Education, and ICT","Economic growth will leverage on the nation's strengths and competitiveness to develop new sources of growth such as healthcare, education and ICT.",""],[1,"83","1","Upgrading Higher Value-Added Manufacturing and Services Production","There are also opportunities to create higher value add products in established manufacturing and services subsectors as well as in downstream resource-based industries.",""],[1,"83","1","Innovation and Technology-Driven Growth Strategy","These new sources of growth will rely on innovation and the use of technology as well as skilled human capital.",""],[1,"92","6","Public-Private Partnership Facilitation Fund","public-private partnerships (PPPs), establishing a facilitation fund and achieving an appropriate balance between government, government- linked companies (GLCs) and the private sector;",""],[1,"113","3","Strategic Project Facilitation Fund","Establishing a facilitation fund to provide support to private sector for projects of high strategic importance;",""],[1,"114","2","Strategic Private Investment Facilitation Fund","A fund will be established to facilitate private sector investment in projects with high strategic value to the nation and multiplier effects.",""],[1,"114","3","Project Viability Assistance and Co-Financing Scheme","Projects with a minimum capital cost or investment of RM100 million will be eligible for assistance.",""],[1,"114","4","Project Viability Infrastructure Fund","The fund will be provided to finance land cost and basic infrastructure such as construction of access roads, bridges and provision of water supply required to make a project viable.","Prime Minister's Department"],[1,"114","5","Private Sector Investment Acceleration and Firm Internationalisation Platform","This is necessary to accelerate private sector investment and create an effective platform to regionalise and globalise Malaysian firms.",""],[1,"127","5","MIDA Investment Attraction Mandate","Empowering Malaysian Investment Development Authority (MIDA) to attract investment;",""],[1,"128","7","Regulatory Burden Easing and Targeted Tax Incentive Package","Among the initiatives that will be considered are further easing regulatory burden, providing industry-tailored incentives and providing reduced corporate and personal income tax rates to selected industries in specific locations, such as the 15% income tax rate currently in effect for qualified knowledge workers residing and working in Iskandar Malaysia, Johor.",""],[1,"128","7","Industrial Infrastructure and Utilities Upgrading Programme","In addition, physical infrastructure and utilities, including industrial parks, will be upgraded to support industries.",""],[1,"129","1","MIDA Institutional Strengthening and Real-Time Incentive Approval","Several important changes will be made to MIDA during the Plan period to make it a more effective investment promotion agency.",""],[1,"129","3","Direct Negotiation Authority for Targeted Investment Projects","Given the authority to negotiate directly with investors for targeted projects;",""],[1,"129","4","Central Investment Promotion Coordination Agency","Designated as the central investment promotion agency for the manufacturing and services sectors (excluding utilities and financial services), to enhance the coordination and cohesion among the relevant investment promotion bodies in the country.",""],[1,"138","1","Private Sector Business Facilitation Measures","In order to support the private sector the Government has set out a plethora of measures to ease business, reduce cost and stimulate growth:",""],[1,"138","7","Privatisation Investment Facilitation Support","Expanded opportunities for businesses to invest from the new wave of privatisation and support from the Facilitation Fund;",""],[1,"138","12","SME Regulatory Relief and Support Programme","Greater support for SMEs, who will gain in terms of lower regulatory requirements, additional programmes to enhance capacity, a better support system and improved access to financing;",""],[1,"142","1","Private Investment Facilitation and Industry Ecosystem Support","Focus on facilitating private investment, coordinating between agencies, supporting industry ecosystems and creating employment opportunities;",""],[1,"145","3","Business Regulation Modernisation","The economic reform measures in the Tenth Malaysia Plan such as modernising of business regulations, human capital development, increasing domestic competition, removing market distortions and improving infrastructure will provide the enabling ecosystem for NKEAs.",""],[1,"145","3","Domestic Competition Enhancement","The economic reform measures in the Tenth Malaysia Plan such as modernising of business regulations, human capital development, increasing domestic competition, removing market distortions and improving infrastructure will provide the enabling ecosystem for NKEAs.",""],[1,"145","3","Market Distortion Removal","The economic reform measures in the Tenth Malaysia Plan such as modernising of business regulations, human capital development, increasing domestic competition, removing market distortions and improving infrastructure will provide the enabling ecosystem for NKEAs.",""],[1,"157","4","Regulatory Review and Streamlining for Priority Industries","Reviewing and streamlining current regulation and procedures, particularly in the swiftlet, aquaculture and herbal industries to attract greater investments and participation from private sector;",""],[1,"159","2","Business Environment Liberalisation Programme","The Government will make Malaysia one of the most business-friendly environment in Asia through a significant programme of liberalisation, and by empowering the MPC to identify key areas for productivity improvement.",""],[1,"159","3","Innovation-Friendly Business Environment Reform","the Government will create an environment that supports innovation across the economy by ensuring that the business environment creates an incentive to innovate and sends the right price signals.",""],[1,"159","3","SME Regulatory Burden Reduction","Special focus will be placed on reducing the barriers to growth and innovation faced by SMEs by relaxing a number of regulatory requirements.",""],[1,"356","2","Private Sector Enabling Environment Reform","The Government's role will become that of a catalytic facilitator, to create an enabling environment for the private sector through effective policies and regulations, as shown in Chart 7-3.",""],[1,"357","5","Regulatory Environment Strengthening and Policy Clarification","The Government's role and effectiveness as a policy-maker and independent regulator will be strengthened in line with increasing participation from the private sector.",""],[1,"357","9","Regulatory Formulation Improvement and Public Consultation Process","Robust and comprehensive processes that address stakeholder concerns and institutionalises public consultation will be adopted in the formulation of regulations;",""]],"17":[[1,"105","1","Incentives for Multinational Company Research Centres","Incentives will also be provided to multi-national companies (MNCs) for establishing research centres in Malaysia.",""],[1,"105","1","FTA-Based Knowledge Transfer Programmes","FTAs will be leveraged for knowledge transfer through programmes such as student and knowledge worker exchange and technology development collaborations.",""],[1,"105","5","Incubator Financing Shift to Private Sector with PPP Transition","Funding for incubators will be gradually shifted towards private sector financing with PPPs as an intermediate step;",""],[1,"105","6","Third-Generation Incubator Upgrade and Manager Training","Incubators will be encouraged to shift towards the third generation model that moves beyond provision of workspace to include business and development services.",""],[1,"105","6","Specialised Training for Incubator Managers and Operators","Incubator managers and operators will receive specialised training to upgrade professionalism;",""],[1,"105","7","New Incubator Establishment and Evaluation Framework","The establishment of new incubators will be subjected to strict evaluation criteria to ensure financial sustainability, and the impact and effectiveness of incubators will be measured based on clear KPIs such as rate of company maturation into new enterprises.",""],[1,"105","8","Knowledge SME Development Support Programme","The Government will support development of K-SMEs by providing access to special financing schemes, improving research and innovation capabilities as well as providing specialised skills training.",""],[1,"106","1","Attract Foreign Activities to Establish Operations in Malaysia","activities will be encouraged to set up operations in Malaysia to bring in specialised skills and knowledge as well as create a competitive environment.",""],[1,"108","13","Enterprise Innovation Promotion","Promote enterprises innovation",""],[1,"108","19","Technology-Based Enterprise Development","Nurture technology based enterprises",""],[1,"108","23","Commercialization Support Services","Provide support services for commercialization",""],[1,"108","24","Enterprise Innovation Advisory and Training","Advisory & training to enable enterprise innovation",""],[1,"109","3","R&D and Commercialisation Support Initiatives","the Government will support R&D and commercialisation across the value chain under a number of initiatives during the Plan period",""],[1,"111","14","1-InnoCERT Enterprise Innovation Assessment Programme","a dedicated programme known as 1-InnoCERT, which assesses the innovation level of enterprises, will further stimulate R&D activities through funding incentives such as access to preferential rate loans, credit guarantees and grants.",""],[1,"120","7","1-InnoCERT SME Innovation Certification","To support innovation, 1-InnoCERT will be introduced to certify SMEs on the basis of innovation and commercialisation achievement.",""],[1,"121","1","R&D Tax Deduction and Procurement Priority Incentive","will receive benefits such as tax deduction for R&D activities and priority in government procurement.",""],[1,"121","1","SME InnoCERT Certification Programme","By 2015, it is targeted that 500 SMEs will be 1-InnoCERT certified;",""],[1,"365","1","Intellectual Property Commercialisation Support","A key outcome of this will be an increase in the commercialisation rate of R&D outputs through proper management of IPs.",""]],"18":[[1,"154","2","E&E Industry Upgrading through Public-Private Partnerships","During the Plan period, efforts will be intensified to move the E&E industry up the value chain through effective PPPs.",""],[1,"154","2","E&E Automation, Digitisation, and Specialisation Promotion","Opportunities in automation, miniaturisation, digitisation and multimedia applications will be pursued, and specialisation in semiconductors, embedded systems, optoelectronics, radio frequency and wireless will be promoted.",""],[1,"154","2","E&E Sector Enablers Development Initiative","The Government will focus on developing key enablers such as upskilling existing talent and increasing supply of relevant talent, strengthening the R&D ecosystem, growing the domestic vendor base and establishing infrastructure.",""],[1,"154","3","Engineering Centres of Excellence Development","Developing centres of engineering excellence by collaborating with industry and academia, particularly for R&D and training;",""],[1,"154","4","State Skills Training Centres Promotion","Promoting state skills training centres and co-funding masters and PhD programmes in critical fields;",""]],"19":[[1,"42","2","Bumiputera Economic Participation Strategy","the Bumiputera development agenda needs to be undertaken with a fresh approach.",""],[1,"42","3","Market-Friendly Bumiputera Opportunity Mechanisms","Market friendly mechanisms will be implemented to provide opportunities for Bumiputera to capitalise on pro-growth policies.",""],[1,"42","4","Bumiputera Commercial and Industrial Community Development Programmes","The programmes for the development of Bumiputera Commercial and Industrial Community (BCIC) will be segmented, in terms of varying the nature of support based on size of enterprise.",""],[1,"42","4","Bumiputera Enterprise Capacity Building and Direct Assistance","Direct assistance and capacity building will be focused on micro-enterprises based on needs whereas for larger Bumiputera companies, support will be merit based.",""],[1,"42","4","Bumiputera Senior Management Participation Initiative","The priority and focus will be towards building competitive Bumiputera enterprises and also raise the participation of Bumiputera in senior management levels.",""],[1,"48","2","Bumiputera and Non-Bumiputera Business Partnership Promotion","In the spirit of 1Malaysia, the Government will also promote genuine partnerships between Bumiputera and non-Bumiputera businesses.",""]],"20":[[1,"38","5","Cluster Development for Agglomeration Economies","These include driving productivity and innovation, nurturing and attracting top talent and developing clusters with agglomeration economies.",""],[1,"39","4","Concentrated Industrial Cluster Development","Promoting the development of concentrated industrial clusters and supporting ecosystem towards enabling specialisation and economies of scale;",""],[1,"40","6","Liveable Cities and Specialized Industrial Clusters Strategy","At the same time, strategies to promote liveable cities and the development of specialised industrial clusters will provide the environment conducive for top talent.",""],[1,"44","2","Cluster-Focused Corridor Development","A refinement under the Tenth Plan would be to focus development on specific clusters within these corridors",""],[1,"44","4","Cluster Strengthening and Location-Based Development Policy","Government will increasingly focus its resources to strengthen existing clusters and only promote other locations based on the respective strengths and endowments of a particular location.",""],[1,"93","3","Urban Agglomeration and Economic Corridor Development","Focusing on key growth engines by building urban agglomerations, focussing corridors around clusters and developing National Key Economic Areas (NKEAs).",""],[1,"139","1","Urban Agglomeration and Economic Corridor Development","Towards this end, priority will be given to building urban agglomerations, focusing corridors around clusters and developing high economic impact sectors.",""],[1,"139","1","National Key Economic Areas Initiative","As such, 11 sectors and one geographic area have been identified as NKEAs to drive economic growth.",""],[1,"141","1","High-Density Cluster Development in Growth Corridors","Under the Tenth Plan, the economic development of regions will be accelerated by focusing around a limited number of high-density clusters in the corridors that have sector and geographic advantages.",""],[1,"142","2","Anchor Investor Identification for Corridor Development","Identify anchor investors to spearhead development of the corridors;",""],[1,"142","3","Refocus Corridor Authorities on Localized Key Industry Clusters","Refocus corridor authorities on smaller key industry clusters within localised geographies.",""],[1,"143","6","ECER Node-Based Economic Concentration Strategy","Under the Tenth Plan, to provide more focus and strategically develop the ECER, all economic activities will be concentrated within the six identified nodes namely ECER Special Economic Zone (ECER SEZ) as the manufacturing and commercial services hub and distribution and procurement centre, Cross Border Development (Tumpat-Kota Bharu-Bachok-Tok Bali-Besut), Kuala Terengganu City Centre-Kenyir-Dungun Triangle, Mersing-Rompin, Gua Musang-Kuala Lipis and Bentong-Raub.",""],[1,"143","8","Growth Node Development within SCORE","Five growth nodes have been identified with the aim of focusing development and investment efforts within SCORE.",""],[1,"144","4","Sandakan-Beluran-Kinabatangan Bio-Triangle Development Initiative","Sandakan-Beluran-Kinabatangan Bio-Triangle: Beluran and Tongod Agropolitan, Agrobio Innovation Zone-Sandakan Education Hub, POIC Sandakan;",""],[1,"144","9","Brunei Bay Integrated Development Area","Brunei Bay Integrated Development Area.",""],[1,"159","5","Disproportionate Policy Focus on National Key Economic Areas","The Government will devote disproportionate policy focus to NKEAs.",""],[1,"159","5","Focused Support for Selected Economic Clusters","There will also be a stronger focus on a limited number of other economic clusters in order to obtain the productivity benefits that are generated in these concentrations of economic activity.",""]],"21":[[1,"39","7","Innovation Enablers Public Investment Expansion","Increasing public investment into the enablers of innovation, particularly R&D and venture capital funding.",""],[1,"39","8","Entrepreneurship and Creativity Investment Initiative","Under the Tenth Plan, the Government is committed to investing in creativity, including efforts such as stimulating entrepreneurship, revamping school curriculum, focusing on R&D and promoting availability of risk capital.",""],[1,"39","8","Venture Capital Co-Investment Fund Expansion","The Government will provide a larger pool of funds for venture capital, especially on a Mudharabah basis (risk sharing) through co-investment with private sector funds.",""],[1,"39","8","Public and Private R&D Expenditure Increase","The Government will target to increase R&D expenditure during the Tenth Plan period through a combination of greater public R&D funding combined with facilitation support for private sector R&D.",""],[1,"92","4","Innovation Ecosystem and Financing Support","Supporting innovation-led growth by shaping a supportive ecosystem for innovation, creating innovation opportunities, putting in place innovation enablers and funding innovation;",""],[1,"109","4","Risk Capital Industry Strengthening","During the Plan period, the risk capital industry, will be strengthened to increase access to funding for innovative start-ups.",""],[1,"109","4","New Funding Modes for Public Venture Companies","New funding modes for public venture companies will be introduced to better match investment risk profiles and promote greater private sector participation and risk-taking.",""],[1,"109","4","Equity Financing Shift for Public Venture Companies","Government funding to public venture companies namely Malaysian Technology Development Corporation (MTDC) and Malaysian Venture Capital Management Berhad will shift from the current lending model to an equity structure.",""],[1,"109","4","Mudharabah Innovation Fund","A Mudharabah Innovation Fund (MIF), with an allocation of RM500 million, will also be introduced to provide risk capital to government- backed venture companies.",""],[1,"111","11","Business Growth Fund for High-Technology Commercialisation","the Government will establish a Business Growth Fund with an allocation of RM150 million.",""],[1,"111","12","Public Venture Capital Rationalisation","Existing public venture capital initiatives will be rationalised.",""],[1,"111","12","MTDC Restructuring for Developmental Mandate","MTDC, will be restructured so that it focuses on its developmental mandate of nurturing",""],[1,"111","13","Technology Investment Company Establishment","a new technology investment company will be set up to manage funds and investments transferred from the MTDC and Khazanah Nasional.",""],[1,"111","14","R&D Tax Deduction and Matching Grant Incentive Scheme","The Government will continue to fund innovation by allowing tax deductions for R&D and providing matching grants to promote private sector funding of R&D and commercialisation.",""]],"22":[[1,"3","2","Tenth Malaysia Plan","The Plan contains new policy directions, strategies and programmes that enable the country to emerge as a high income nation.",""],[1,"21","15","Strengthening MIDA Negotiation Authority","MIDA will be empowered with additional decision-making authority in negotiations with investors",""],[1,"32","6","Tradeables and Export-Oriented Sector Support","Continued emphasis will be given to tradeables and export orientated sectors, in addition to services that support trade.",""],[1,"33","2","Micro-Enterprise, Venture Capital, and Export Financing Support","funding, particularly in terms of supporting micro- enterprises, venture capital for innovation, and export related financing.",""],[1,"33","2","Prioritised Public Sector Investment in Strategic Sectors","the focus on growth will include prioritising public sector investments with high spinoff potential, particularly in the strategic sectors.",""],[1,"35","1","Trade Promotion and Market Diversification Initiative","Under the Tenth Plan, Malaysia will increasingly focus on new fast growing markets, particularly in Asia and ASEAN.",""],[1,"35","1","Regional Trade Agreement Integration","Key initiatives include trade promotion, enhancing regional connectivity (such as through extending the regional network of flight routes and enhancing broadband connectivity) and regional integration through trade agreements.",""],[1,"35","2","Support for Regional Champions and Market Expansion","The Government will continue to support Malaysian companies to emerge as regional champions and assist in opening new markets.",""],[1,"35","2","Investment Promotion Empowerment for MIDA and MATRADE","Both the Malaysian Investment Development Authority (MIDA) and Malaysian External Trade Development Corporation (MATRADE) have been empowered to secure new investment",""],[1,"36","1","Support for Malaysian Road Projects in India","Facilitating Malaysian companies to undertake road projects in India",""],[1,"37","4","Co-Investment in Skills Training, R&D, and Enabling Infrastructure","the Government's role is not to pick winners but rather to accelerate and facilitate emerging specialisations, especially through co-investments with industry in terms of skills training, Research & Development (R&D) and enabling infrastructure.",""],[1,"138","9","Export Market Entry Support Mechanism","A better mechanism to support firms break into export market;",""],[1,"153","9","Market Marketing and Promotion Intensification","Intensifying marketing and promotion efforts in high potential markets.",""],[1,"159","4","Trade and Investment Relationship Strengthening","Malaysia will continue to strengthen trade and investment relationships within the region - ASEAN, China, India - as well as with the US, Europe, and the GCC countries.",""],[1,"159","4","Support for Malaysian Firms in Global Markets","The Government will support Malaysian firms to compete in global markets.",""],[1,"190","3","Government-to-Government Market Access Negotiations","For mature companies, assistance will include Government- to-Government negotiations to open up new markets, while government procurement, licenses and privatisation will be used to promote participation in strategic areas.",""],[1,"414","2","Agriculture and Agro-based Export Promotion","Increase exports of agriculture and agro-based products",""],[1,"414","4","Professional Services Export Promotion","Increase export of professional services",""],[1,"414","6","Expansion of Malaysian Islamic Finance Global Presence","Expand global presence of Malaysian Islamic finance",""]],"23":[[1,"186","2","Bumiputera Business Establishment Support","Assistance will be provided to Bumiputera in Sabah and Sarawak, particularly ethnic minorities and Orang Asli communities to establish businesses such as home stay and eco-tourism services.",""],[1,"186","3","Entrepreneurship Training, Funding, and Business Linkage Support","Assistance will include providing entrepreneurship training and funding as well as strengthening linkages with established businesses in the identified sectors.",""],[1,"187","1","Community Cooperative Marketing Support Initiative","Initiatives will be undertaken to assist these communities to establish cooperatives to market their products more effectively.",""],[1,"187","3","Loan Schemes for Premium and Leasehold Renewal","Efforts will be initiated to introduce loan schemes by financial institutions to finance payment of premium and leasehold tenure renewal.",""],[1,"187","3","House Upgrading and Business Financing Loan Scheme","The loan scheme will also be made available to assist the residents to upgrade their houses as well as fund their business activities.",""],[1,"187","3","Expansion of Existing Funding Programmes","Existing funding programmes through AIM and TEKUN will be",""],[1,"189","1","Bumiputera Entrepreneurship Strengthening Initiative","Strengthening Bumiputera entrepreneurship to help create competitive businesses in high- impact sectors;",""]],"24":[[1,"4","2","Bottom 40 Percent Livelihood Uplift Programme","The Government is also committed to uplift the livelihoods of the bottom 40% of households, irrespective of ethnicity, background or location, through income and capacity building programmes, strengthening the social safety net and addressing the needs of the disadvantaged groups.",""],[1,"4","2","Bumiputera Commercial and Industrial Community Development Initiative","The agenda to create a robust and vibrant Bumiputera Commercial and Industrial Community (BCIC), as well as ownership of equity and other sources of wealth, will continue with a fresh approach, in line with the current global environment and national priorities.",""],[1,"41","2","Distributional Assistance for Disadvantaged Groups","The distributional policies of the Government will therefore be focused towards ensuring equality of opportunities for all.",""],[1,"41","3","Sustainable Poverty Reduction Programmes","Special programmes will be undertaken to address poverty on a sustainable basis, especially in terms of providing income generating opportunities, such as through agropolitan projects.",""],[1,"41","3","Urban Poor Microcredit Schemes","specific interventions will also be targeted towards the urban poor, such as through micro credit schemes.",""],[1,"42","1","Skills Training and Entrepreneur Development Programmes","Skills training and entrepreneur development programmes will be targeted towards those within the workforce with low-income and low skills.",""],[1,"42","1","Community Self-Reliance and Ownership Programmes","Programmes will also be implemented for those in disadvantaged communities towards inculcating a sense of self-reliance and ownership to achieve personal aspirations.",""],[1,"46","5","Spatially Targeted Localised Intervention Policies","Included in the Tenth Plan are specific initiatives for targeted communities, such as assistance with land matters in new villages, improving living conditions in estates, agropolitan projects in rural areas and micro credit for the urban poor.",""],[1,"87","2","1Malaysia National Unity and Inclusion Concept","The 1Malaysia concept seeks to reinforce national unity, which is crucial to maintain social and political stability - a prerequisite for Malaysia to remain an attractive place for business and investment.",""],[1,"99","6","Protection of Social Service Delivery","The Government, however will not compromise on delivering social services like education, healthcare and welfare.",""],[1,"100","1","Targeted Assistance for Vulnerable Groups from Subsidy Rationalisation Savings","Vulnerable groups and those in low- income brackets who require support will continue to be provided with assistance, as a portion of the savings from subsidy rationalisation will be directed towards them.",""]],"25":[[1,"210","2","Family Support Services and Marriage Strengthening Programme","family support services and programmes will focus on strengthening marriage and promoting equitable sharing of resources, responsibilities and tasks.",""],[1,"210","3","Smart Start Marriage Awareness Programme Expansion","The Smart Start programme will be expanded to create awareness about the roles and responsibilities involved in a marriage institution and promote greater understanding among couples who are about to get married.",""],[1,"210","3","Parenting@Work Parenting Skills Programme","Parenting knowledge and skills, especially among working couples, will be strengthened through the Parenting@Work programme which promotes greater work-life balance and supports the parenting needs of young families.",""],[1,"210","3","Expansion of One-Stop Family Service Centres","The Government will also increase the number of one- stop family service centres during the Plan period to provide accessible family support services such as counselling, therapy and mediation.",""]],"26":[[1,"207","2","Child Welfare and Protection Support Programme","Consequently, concerted efforts to strengthen the family institution and facilitate child welfare, protection and development will be continued.",""],[1,"207","2","Childcare Services Quality Improvement","This will include enhancing the quality of childcare services, strengthening related support programmes including capacity building of caregivers, and upgrading existing welfare institutions such as rehabilitation centres and child welfare homes.",""],[1,"207","2","Community Child Protection Awareness Programme","In addition, the role of the community in protecting the best interest of the child will be enhanced through awareness programmes.",""],[1,"207","3","Community Participation Capacity Building for Child Protection","The role of the community will be enhanced through capacity building efforts that facilitate their effective functioning in helping to protect the best interest of the child and undertake preventive and rehabilitative programmes to curb many social problems affecting children.",""],[1,"207","4","Child Carer Screening for Child Protection","the Royal Malaysian Police will conduct screening for child carers to ensure the safety and protection of children under the care of external parties such as child care centres, nurseries and kindergartens",""],[1,"207","4","Lost and Missing Children Alert System","An alert system for lost and missing children (similar to the U.S. AMBER Alert bulletin) will be established to provide additional security for children, through the cooperation of the mass media and law enforcement agencies",""],[1,"207","5","Children Activity Centre Strengthening","Children activity centres will be strengthened to prevent children, particularly from high-risk",""],[1,"208","1","Community Child Welfare Centres","These centres are set up based on specific community needs in a particular area and provide comprehensive child welfare services, including sports and social activities, learning programmes and counselling facilities.",""]],"27":[[1,"209","1","Disability Inclusion and Mainstreaming Programme","The Plan will focus on integrating PWDs into society to enable them to be independent, productive and valued contributors.",""],[1,"209","2","Universal Design Standards for Accessible Infrastructure","This will be done through the adoption of universal design standards in buildings, public spaces and parks.",""],[1,"209","2","Upgrade of Community-Based Rehabilitation Centres to One-Stop Service Centres","Existing community-based rehabilitation centres will be upgraded to one-stop service centres which will provide more comprehensive services such as registration of PWDs, disability screening and detection, referral services, vocational trainings, job placements and dissemination of information on disabilities.",""],[1,"209","2","PDKNet Programme Enhancement","Furthermore, the PDKNet programme will be improved to strengthen community-based rehabilitation through multimedia technologies and ICT.",""],[1,"209","3","Disabled Employment Promotion in the Civil Service","The Government will also seek to provide greater employment opportunities for PWDs.",""],[1,"209","3","Expansion of the Job Coach Programme","Other existing programmes such as Job Coach will be broadened to ensure sufficient coverage",""],[1,"209","4","ICT-Based Labour Exchange for Persons with Disabilities","to effectively assist PWDs in seeking, obtaining and retaining positions in open employment, through ICT programmes such as an electronic labour exchange system for PWDs operated by the Labour Department.","Labour Department"],[1,"209","4","Specialised Learning Institutions and Vocational Schools for Persons with Disabilities","The Government will also look into establishing specialised learning institutions and vocational schools dedicated to PWDs.",""]],"28":[[1,"203","6","Expansion of Community-Based Nurseries and Day Care Centres","Improvement in work-life balance provisions to encourage greater women participation in the workforce, particularly from the low income households, will be made by increasing the number of community-based nurseries and day care centres under JKM.","JKM"],[1,"203","6","Day Care Centre Registration Enforcement","To this end, the Government will increase its efforts to ensure registration of the day care centres.",""],[1,"203","6","CSR Support for Licensed Day Care Centres","CSR programmes to sponsor the establishment of licensed day care centres in partnership with NGOs will be actively promoted.",""]],"29":[[1,"208","2","Older Persons Health and Well-Being Support","Therefore, during the Plan period, continued emphasis will be placed on ensuring the health and well-being of older persons so that they are able to age with dignity and respect as well as lead independent and fulfilling lives as integral members of their families, communities and country.",""],[1,"208","3","Conducive Environment for Older Persons","Measures will be undertaken to provide a conducive environment for older persons to",""],[1,"208","4","Elderly-Friendly Infrastructure Improvement Programme","programmes will focus on enhancing elderly- friendly infrastructure",""],[1,"208","4","Affordable Healthcare Access Improvement Programme for Older Persons","improving access to affordable healthcare",""],[1,"208","4","Shelter Provision for Older Persons","ensuring adequate provision of shelters",""],[1,"208","4","Financial Security and Employment Opportunities for Older Persons","improving financial security and opportunities for employment",""],[1,"208","4","Community Awareness Programme on Caring for Older Persons","Programmes to create greater awareness among family members and the community in caring for older persons will also be undertaken.",""],[1,"208","5","Tax Rebate for Retraining Older Persons","the 100% tax rebate on costs to retrain older persons will be continued",""],[1,"208","5","Jobs Malaysia Older Persons Employment Database Promotion","the database on employment opportunities for older persons under Jobs Malaysia will be promoted more actively to create greater awareness for those who are actively looking for a job",""],[1,"208","6","Home Help Programme for Older Persons","Independent living will also be emphasised through the Home Help programme where volunteers will provide assistance in managing the daily chores especially for those who live alone.",""],[1,"208","6","Expansion of Day Care Centres for Older Persons","Day care centres for older persons, which are established in partnership with NGOs, will be expanded to ensure older persons are taken care of when family members are working.",""],[1,"208","6","Free Transport to Hospitals and Clinics","Access to healthcare will also continue to be improved through provision of free transport to hospitals and clinics by JKM.","JKM"]],"30":[[1,"272","6","Balanced Rural and Urban Development Policy","Concentrating growth in urban areas will not come at the expense of rural development.",""],[1,"282","5","Strengthening Rural-Urban Economic Integration","Rural areas will benefit from urban agglomeration through strong economic integration of rural and urban activities.",""],[1,"282","5","Development of Regional Growth Poles and Logistics Services","Well-functioning regional growth poles will provide logistics services to adjacent rural areas enabling the integration of these areas into local or international supply chains.",""],[1,"282","5","Promotion of Non-Agricultural Rural Employment","Non- agricultural employment opportunities in rural areas, which support upstream economic activities in urban areas will be promoted in intermediate towns and major local centres, within commuting distances of rural villages, to provide opportunities for increasing rural income levels.",""]],"31":[[1,"4","2","Rural-Urban Connectivity Infrastructure Investment","Investment in infrastructure to connect rural areas to urban clusters will be increased to ensure inclusiveness in the sharing of economic benefits.",""]],"32":[[1,"283","1","Rural Basic Infrastructure Upgrading","Focus in rural areas will be on upgrading basic infrastructure",""],[1,"283","7","Rural Growth Centres Implementation","It is therefore important to enhance and expedite the implementation of Rural Growth Centres (RGCs), where rural citizens can choose to live in order to benefit from high- quality public services such as health, education, communications, public transport, utilities and other community-based services.",""],[1,"283","9","Rural Road Network Expansion and Upgrading","Expanding and upgrading rural road networks.",""],[1,"284","1","Rural Electricity Supply Expansion","Coverage of electricity supply in rural areas will be extended through the grid and alternative systems such as mini hydro and solar hybrid.",""],[1,"284","2","Treated Water Supply Expansion Programme","Expanding coverage of treated water supply.",""],[1,"284","3","Rural Internet and Broadband Connectivity Expansion","Rural communities will be virtually connected to the world through the provision of Internet and broadband services.",""],[1,"284","3","1Malaysia Internet Centres in Rural Communities","1Malaysia Internet Centres in rural communities will provide affordable internet access as well as function as community centres.",""]],"33":[[1,"307","5","Non-Revenue Water Reduction Programme","The non-revenue water (NRW) programme, involving replacement of pipes and old meters, will be expanded with an allocation RM1.1 billion to improve the quality of water and reduce losses in water supply.",""]],"34":[[1,"308","2","Pollution Control Measures Targeting Major Pollution Sources","During the Plan period, measures to improve pollution control targeting these sources will be implemented through:",""],[1,"308","3","Industrial Effluent and Sewage Discharge Enforcement Strengthening","Strengthening the enforcement on industrial effluents and sewage discharge in line with the revisions to the regulations under the Environmental Quality Act 1974;",""],[1,"309","1","River Total Maximum Daily Load Assessment","Assessing the Total Maximum Daily Load and carrying capacity of rivers to determine allowable discharge loads, for both point and non-point sources of pollution;",""],[1,"309","2","Water Quality Index Revision","Revising the current Water Quality Index to incorporate additional parameters, such as biological parameters, for more accurate river water classification;",""],[1,"309","3","National Marine Water Quality Index Development","Developing the National Marine Water Quality Index to replace the current Marine Water Quality Criteria and Standard, which was developed in 2008;",""]],"35":[[1,"306","9","Tariff-Setting Mechanism for Full Cost Recovery","Tariff-setting mechanism to allow full cost recovery to be completely phased in by 2013",""],[1,"306","14","Integrated Water and Sewerage Tariff Reform","Initial efforts towards the introduction of integrated water and sewerage tariffs",""],[1,"307","1","Phased Water Tariff-Setting Mechanism for Full Cost Recovery","the Government will phase in a tariff-setting mechanism that allows full recovery of costs to encourage sustained investments in upgrading and rehabilitating water treatment plants and distribution systems.",""],[1,"307","2","Water Operator Business Planning and Performance Regulation Framework","Water operators will be required to provide detailed 30-year business plans and 3-year operational plans.",""],[1,"307","2","Water Sector Cost Recovery Roadmap","These plans will be the basis for a roadmap towards full cost recovery",""],[1,"307","2","Water Utility Capital Expenditure Funding Planning","These plans will be the basis for a roadmap towards full cost recovery and will allow Pengurusan Aset Air Berhad (PAAB) to plan long term capital expenditure funding.",""],[1,"307","2","Water Operator Performance Regulation and Tariff Incentive System","SPAN will regulate and monitor the performance of water operators based on the plans, linking tariff increases to efficiency gains in operations and capital expenditure;",""],[1,"307","6","Integrated Water and Sewerage Services Reform","Restructuring of sewerage services will be implemented by parcelling out the operations of centralised sewerage services to the respective state water operating companies.",""],[1,"307","6","Integrated Water and Sewerage Tariff System","When completed, the industry will move towards implementing an integrated tariff for both water and sewerage services.",""]],"36":[[1,"21","7","Water Services Industry Restructuring","Restructuring of the water services industry towards improving efficiency in operations and management",""],[1,"304","10","Water Services Industry Restructuring","Continuing efforts to restructure the water services industry;",""],[1,"306","1","Water Services Industry Restructuring","During the Plan period, restructuring efforts will enter into its final phase, as shown in Chart 6-14, with a focus on the following areas:",""],[1,"306","2","Migration of State Water Operators to New Licensing Regime","Completing the migration of state water operators.",""],[1,"306","3","Water Services Industry Restructuring","Restructuring of the water services industry towards improving efficiency in operations and management",""],[1,"306","7","Privatisation and Corporatisation of State Water Authorities","Privatisation and corporatisation of state water authorities",""],[1,"306","10","Water Services Industry Act Enforcement","Enforcement of Water Services Industry Act (WSIA), 2006",""],[1,"306","11","Water Services Industry Restructuring Planning","Planning for restructuring of water services industry",""],[1,"306","12","Water Asset Transfer and Infrastructure Development by PAAB","Pengurusan Aset Air Berhad (PAAB) takes over existing water assets from state at negotiated values and is responsible for implementing water infrastructure development",""],[1,"332","5","Water Services Industry Efficiency and Financial Sustainability Initiative","Continuing efforts to move the water services industry towards efficiency in operations and creating a financially sustainable platform for continued investments in the sector;",""]],"37":[[1,"82","1","Export Market Diversification Initiative","efforts will be taken to reduce dependence on the traditional markets and to make stronger inroads into emerging markets in Asia and the Gulf states.",""],[1,"101","14","MyExport Export Information Portal","Malaysian exporters registered with MATRADE are able to access a variety of services such as up-to-date trade information on trade events and activities, trade statistics and market alerts through the MyExport portal.","MATRADE"],[1,"121","2","Centralised Online Trade Information Platform","An online centralised trade information platform will also be in place to increase access to trade opportunities overseas.",""],[1,"124","1","FTA-Based Export Market Expansion Initiatives","Malaysia will leverage on FTAs and introduce several initiatives to expand its global export market share as follows:",""],[1,"124","3","Export Market Entry Support for Malaysian Firms","Assisting Malaysian firms to break into export markets;",""],[1,"124","6","Export Promotion and Market Diversification Initiative","export promotion will be intensified in fast growing markets in East Asia, India and Gulf Cooperation Council (GCC) countries, and increased market presence will be established in new and emerging markets such as Africa, Latin America and Central Asia.",""],[1,"124","6","Traditional Market Expansion and Export Visibility Enhancement","Opportunities in traditional markets such as the ASEAN, the United States and European Union will be optimised by expanding into new market segments as well as enhancing market visibility and strengthening the credibility of Malaysian goods and services.",""],[1,"124","8","Export Promotion and Branding Support Programme","Malaysian firms will be assisted to promote their products and services through specialised marketing missions, incoming buying missions, trade investment missions and trade fairs.",""],[1,"124","8","Global Brand Development Initiative","Branding initiatives will be undertaken more aggressively to create more Malaysian global brands.",""],[1,"124","8","Export Capability Support Programme","The capability of Malaysian firms to export will be enhanced through various support programmes.",""],[1,"124","8","International Standards Compliance Support","Firms will also be encouraged to adopt and comply with international standards and requirements on quality, safety and environment to improve market access for their products and services.",""],[1,"124","9","Export Market Expansion Support","To facilitate the expansion of Malaysian firms into the export market, the Government will provide assistance in the form of export promotion, improve international branding of leading exporters and build capacity.",""],[1,"125","1","Services Export Support","Services Export Support.",""],[1,"125","2","Brand Promotion Programme","Brand Promotion Programme.",""],[1,"125","3","Malaysia Institute of Exports","Establishing a Malaysia Institute of Exports to provide training for Malaysian exporters and provide information on target export markets;",""],[1,"125","4","EXIM Bank Capacity Enhancement for Export Financing","Enhancing the capacity of EXIM Bank to provide financing to a broad range of Malaysian companies exporting products and services.",""],[1,"125","5","SME Export Market Entry Support","The Government will introduce a more active set of policies and activities to assist Malaysian SMEs to break into export markets.",""],[1,"125","6","SME International Trade Participation and Export Support Programme","programmes to encourage SMEs participation in international trade events, export training, providing shared infrastructure and services overseas, and financial assistance such as the Market Development Grant, which will target to generate 4,000 new exporters during the Plan period.",""],[1,"125","8","FTA Opportunity Awareness and Firm Support Programme","To extract full potential of the FTAs, the Government will help firms understand the opportunities provided by the FTAs in these markets and will provide appropriate support to access the opportunities that have been generated in these markets.",""]],"38":[[1,"101","7","National Single Window for Trade Data Submission","NSW is an online-based single point of entry for submission of trade data and information.",""],[1,"101","8","Expansion of National Single Window Services","During the Plan period, the services under NSW will be expanded to include services of Free Zone declarations, Dangerous Goods declarations, non-customs permits, phytosanitary certificates and Convention of International Trade on Endangered Species certificates.",""],[1,"101","10","Trade Documentation Simplification and Paperless Transaction Reform","To facilitate trade, documentation requirements will be reduced and streamlined with the aim of achieving a paperless transaction environment in line with international standards.",""],[1,"101","11","Single Customs Portal Development","A single Customs Portal will be developed to reduce bureaucracy and facilitate the supply of information and services; it will be supported by an amendment to the Customs Act 1967.",""],[1,"101","13","FPX Nationwide Rollout for Customs Duty Payments","During the Plan period, Bank Negara will define a timeframe for all banks to participate in the FPX to enable a more effective nationwide rollout of the NSW Electronic Customs Duty Payment.",""],[1,"126","2","Trade Transaction Cost Reduction Programme","An active programme for reducing transaction costs such as customs procedures and logistics will be undertaken to facilitate trade and unlock the potential of FTAs.",""],[1,"126","2","National Single Window Service Expansion","This will include expansion of services under the National Single Window to include services for Free Zone declarations, dangerous goods declarations and non-customs permit.",""],[1,"126","9","Shipping Information Digitalization System Upgrade","IT system upgrade - digi- tise shipping information",""],[1,"127","1","Cross-Border Customs and Logistics ICT Modernization","greater use of ICT in the provision of cross border customs and logistics services and will review all regulations and procedures pertaining to trade with the view to reduce cost and time as well as increase efficiency.",""],[1,"344","3","National Single Window for Trade Data Submission","NSW is an online-based single point of entry for submission of trade data and information.",""],[1,"344","4","Expansion of NSW Services","During the Plan period, the services under NSW will be expanded to include services of Free Zone Declarations, Dangerous Goods Declarations, Non-Customs Permits, Phytosanitary Certificates and Convention of International Trade on Endangered Species Certificates.",""],[1,"344","6","Trade Documentation Simplification and Paperless Transaction Reform","To facilitate trade, documentation requirements will be reduced and streamlined with the aim of achieving a paperless transaction environment in line with international standards.",""],[1,"344","7","Single Customs Portal Development","A single Customs Portal will be developed to reduce bureaucracy and facilitate the supply of information and services; it will be supported by an amendment to the Customs Act 1967.",""],[1,"344","10","Nationwide FPX Participation Framework for Electronic Customs Duty Payment","During the Plan period, Bank Negara will define a timeframe for all banks to participate in the FPX to enable a more effective nationwide rollout of the NSW Electronic Customs Duty Payment.","Bank Negara"],[1,"344","11","MyExport Portal Trade Information Services","Malaysian exporters registered with MATRADE are able to access a variety of services such as up-to-date trade information on trade events and activities, trade statistics and market alerts through the MyExport Portal.","MATRADE"]],"39":[[1,"315","2","Reducing Crime NKRA","Given limited police resources, a new approach that engages every arm of the criminal justice system will be emphasised, from Government bodies, at federal and state levels, to the private sector and citizens through programmes that encourage volunteerism.",""],[1,"316","3","Public Safety Perception Improvement Initiative","Improving public perception of safety, especially through public participation and volunteerism;",""],[1,"316","15","Overall Index Crime Reduction Target","The Government is committed to reducing overall index crimes by an annual average of at least 5% from January 2010 to December 2015.",""],[1,"317","1","Police Visibility and Volunteer Support Initiative","The visibility of the police will be increased, with a focus on hot spots through a new volunteerism initiative.",""],[1,"317","1","Police Facilities and Career Improvement Programme","The well-being of the police will also be improved through upgrading police stations and living quarters as well as by improving their career prospects to motivate them to perform better and the Government will set aside RM2.4 billion towards this end.",""],[1,"317","2","Improve Drug Treatment Programme Effectiveness","New measures to address drug abuse will include improving the effectiveness of drug treatment programmes.",""],[1,"317","3","Volunteer Neighbourhood Patrol Initiative","Volunteerism is being encouraged through a range of initiatives such as the Skim Rondaan Sukarela, a voluntary community activity under the Rukun Tetangga in which local residents patrol their own neighbourhoods.",""],[1,"317","3","Rakan Cop Community Crime Reporting Expansion","Rakan Cop, a scheme where people register for membership by short text message (SMS) and then help by reporting crimes or suspicious behaviour to the police via SMS, will also be expanded to encourage greater enrolment and educate people on the type of information that is useful for the police.",""],[1,"317","4","High-Profile Community Policing Patrols","High profile policing that demonstrates the commitment of the PDRM to serve the community and reduce crime will be intensified.",""],[1,"318","2","Expansion of Private Security Guard Responsibilities","This includes measures such as extending the purview of private security guards to guard the safety beyond the building they are protecting to the surrounding area.",""],[1,"332","7","Crime Prevention and Enforcement Strengthening","Intensifying efforts to fight and prevent crime by addressing the entire criminal justice system with increased police presence and improved enforcement efforts.",""]],"40":[[1,"270","4","Healthcare Delivery System Restructuring","Restructuring the healthcare delivery system to increase the quality and capacity of care and moving from strategies that emphasise treatment, to one that emphasises wellness and disease prevention;",""],[1,"294","3","Healthcare Delivery System Reform","the Government will reform the healthcare delivery system, with a focus on four key areas:",""],[1,"295","2","National Health System Restructuring","Transformation of the healthcare delivery system calls for the restructuring of the national health system, both public and private, to enhance coverage for all.",""],[1,"295","2","Public-Private Healthcare Collaboration Framework","The approach will require greater collaboration between the public and private healthcare systems to allow effective delivery, greater efficiency and affordable costs.",""],[1,"295","3","Health Sector Regulatory and Service Delivery Role Streamlining","A clearer demarcation of regulatory and service delivery functions where the Ministry of Health will focus mainly on governance, stewardship of the healthcare sector and enforcement of legislation.","Ministry of Health"],[1,"295","4","Legislation and Regulation Review for Accreditation Enforcement","A review of existing legislation and the introduction of new regulations to emphasise enforcement of accreditation, credentialing and privileging;",""],[1,"295","5","Healthcare Financing Options Review","A review of financing options that allow management of rising costs, while ensuring that healthcare remains accessible and affordable to the people.",""],[1,"332","4","Healthcare Sector Transformation for Service Delivery Equity","Transforming the healthcare sector to reduce the gap between private and public healthcare systems with a focus on the delivery of healthcare services;",""]],"41":[[1,"296","7","Healthy Lifestyles Promotion Initiative","An important initiative in reducing demand for healthcare is by promoting healthy lifestyles.",""],[1,"297","1","Healthy Living Awareness Campaign","Aggressive efforts to increase awareness for the practice of healthy living by individuals and communities will be undertaken, including:",""],[1,"297","2","Healthy Lifestyle Campaign Expansion","Expanding the Healthy Lifestyle Campaign.",""],[1,"297","3","Healthy Lifestyle and Health Promotion Campaign","The campaign, which emphasises healthy eating, physical activity, anti-smoking and mental health, will specifically target school children, adolescents, women and the elderly to ensure better health outcomes;",""],[1,"297","4","Healthy and Active Lifestyle Promotion","Sports and recreational activities will be promoted to enable people to adopt a healthy and active lifestyle.",""],[1,"297","4","Upgrade of Sports and Recreational Amenities","Existing sports and recreational amenities will be upgraded and the private sector will be encouraged to build new facilities in accessible locations.",""],[1,"297","4","Mandatory School Sports Participation","participation in at least one sports activity will be made compulsory for students in schools beginning in 2011.",""]],"42":[[1,"294","5","Healthcare Infrastructure Expansion and Upgrading","Increasing quality, capacity and coverage of the healthcare infrastructure;",""],[1,"295","6","Health Facilities Upgrading and Expansion Programme","The Government will continue to upgrade and expand its health facilities across both urban and rural areas.",""],[1,"295","6","Secondary and Tertiary Care Strengthening Programme","Provision of secondary and tertiary care services will be strengthened and consolidated, while primary care services will be further extended to underserved areas.",""],[1,"295","6","Primary Care Extension to Underserved Areas","Provision of secondary and tertiary care services will be strengthened and consolidated, while primary care services will be further extended to underserved areas.",""],[1,"295","7","Primary Care Clinic Expansion","Expanding primary care services.",""],[1,"296","1","Expansion of Rural, Community, and 1Malaysia Clinics","This will comprise of 156 clinics in the rural areas and 41 community health clinics.",""],[1,"296","1","Additional 1Malaysia Clinics in Underserved Urban Areas","A total of 50 additional 1Malaysia clinics will be set up with expanded scope of services in urban poor and other underserved areas;",""],[1,"296","2","Secondary and Tertiary Care Hospital Expansion","Strengthening secondary and tertiary care services.",""],[1,"296","4","Expansion of Mobile Clinics, Flying Doctor Services, and Village Health Promoters","Provision of mobile clinics, flying doctor services and village health promoters will be expanded to cater to less accessible groups",""],[1,"296","5","Pre-hospital and Emergency Care Enhancement","Delivery of pre-hospital and emergency care will be enhanced to ensure effective early response.",""],[1,"296","5","Ambulatory Care Expansion","Ambulatory care services will also be expanded and enhanced to reduce the cost and duration of hospitalisation.",""]],"43":[[1,"184","5","Special Clinic Days for Chronic Disease Care","Special clinic days for chronic diseases will be set to enable patients with multiple illnesses to receive consultations in a single visit instead of multiple visits as previously required.",""],[1,"184","5","Expanded Mobile Clinic and Flying Doctor Services","Mobile clinics, including flying doctor services will be expanded for groups with lower accessibility such as Orang Asli and ethnic minorities in remote parts of Sabah and Sarawak.",""],[1,"185","1","1Malaysia Clinic Expansion Programme","1Malaysia clinics will be expanded to provide services to urban poor and other underserved areas, with additional clinics to be built during the Plan period.",""]],"44":[[1,"156","4","Healthcare Tourism Strategic Alliance Development","Fostering strategic alliances among local and foreign healthcare service providers, travel organisations and medical insurance groups to provide a more integrated and comprehensive package of services to healthcare travellers;",""],[1,"156","5","Private Hospital International Accreditation Promotion","Encouraging more private hospitals to seek accreditation with international healthcare accreditation bodies;",""],[1,"156","6","High-End Medical Technology Investment and Utilization","Promoting investment in and utilisation of high-end medical technology to increase efficiency, effectiveness and competitiveness;",""],[1,"156","7","Malaysia Healthcare Global Promotion Campaign","Intensifying coordinated and integrated promotional activities to strengthen the presence of Malaysia Healthcare brand globally.",""]],"45":[[1,"296","3","Healthcare Provider Mapping and Service Delivery Streamlining","Mapping of existing healthcare providers against underserved areas will be undertaken in order to identify gaps or opportunities to streamline service delivery.",""],[1,"296","3","Healthcare Personnel Database and Training Needs Assessment","This will be complemented with the development of a personnel database and their training needs to facilitate planning for a network of facilities that will be the basis of a comprehensive healthcare system;",""],[1,"298","1","Human Resources for Health Investment","In order to cope with the increased demand for training, the Government will increasingly utilise specialists",""],[1,"298","2","Outsourcing and Collaboration with Private Training Institutions for Allied Health Personnel Training","the Government will continue to outsource and collaborate with private training institutions for the training of allied health personnel.",""],[1,"298","4","Specialist Training Allocation Increase for Healthcare Professionals","Increasing the specialist training allocation for doctors and other healthcare professionals;",""],[1,"299","1","Post-Basic Training Expansion for Nurses and Allied Healthcare Personnel","Improving and expanding post-basic training for nurses and allied healthcare personnel;",""],[1,"299","2","Personnel Retention and Job Satisfaction Measures","Addressing personnel retention through provision of better remuneration, promotional opportunities and steps to provide greater job satisfaction;",""],[1,"299","3","Private Healthcare Professional Quality Improvement","Improving the quality of private healthcare professionals through credentialing, privileging and structured training.",""]],"46":[[1,"10","4","Housing Assistance Programmes for Poor Households","Providing Housing Assistance Programmes to Deserving Poor Households in Rural and Urban Areas",""],[1,"10","8","Financial Assistance for Home Upgrading and Business Activities in Chinese New Villages","Providing Financial Assistance to Chinese New Villages' Residents to Upgrade Their Homes and Fund Their Business Activities",""],[1,"270","5","Affordable Housing Supply and Housing Industry Development","Ensuring access to quality and affordable housing.",""],[1,"301","5","Affordable Housing Delivery System Streamlining","Streamlining the affordable housing delivery system;",""],[1,"301","8","Affordable Public Housing Construction Programme","During the Plan period, a total of 78,000 units of new affordable public housing will be constructed by the Federal Government across the nation.",""]],"47":[[1,"239","1","Technical Education and Vocational Training Expansion and Quality Improvement","Malaysia aspires to move up the value chain to become a high-income economy, and must therefore significantly increase enrolment in technical education and vocational training (TEVT) and raise overall training quality to upskill the workforce.",""],[1,"239","8","TEVT Curriculum Upgrading and Harmonisation","Upgrading and harmonising TEVT curriculum quality in line with industry requirements;",""],[1,"240","1","Technical and Vocational Education and Training Attractiveness Improvement","The focus will be to improve the value proposition and attractiveness of TEVT to prospective students, providers and industry.",""],[1,"240","2","National TVET Awareness Media Campaign","Throughout the Plan period, a national media campaign will be developed and rolled-out to improve public awareness and perception of TEVT.",""],[1,"241","2","School Counselling and Career Guidance Teams","School counsellors at district levels will form counselling teams and be responsible for establishing close relationships with TEVT institutes and employers as well as improving coordination among these stakeholders through the exchange of information.",""],[1,"241","2","Multi-Year Student Counselling Support","Counsellors in schools will be tasked to take on a multi-year responsibility for students, starting from Form 4 and continuing until these students have successfully transitioned into tertiary education.",""],[1,"241","2","Comprehensive Career Guidance for Students and Parents","The teams will also be responsible for providing comprehensive career guidance to students and their parents, particularly on the various options in TEVT.",""],[1,"241","3","Technical School Rebranding and Conversion to Vocational Schools","vocational and skills streams in technical schools will be rebranded.",""],[1,"241","4","Establishment of New Vocational Schools","new vocational schools will be established by 2015, to allow greater focus and more targeted courses to be delivered to vocationally-inclined students.",""],[1,"241","5","Production and Project-Based Learning in TEVT Programmes","A production and project based learning approach will be introduced to improve the quality and enhance the attractiveness of TEVT programmes to both employers and students.",""],[1,"241","5","Government-Linked Company Internship and Employment Scheme","In addition, the Government will encourage government-linked- companies to provide internships and employment for students from TEVT institutions.",""],[1,"242","3","Public-Private Technical and Vocational Education and Training Delivery","Both the private sector (providing about 80% of financing) and the public sector are involved in financing and delivering TEVT.",""],[1,"242","3","Training Curriculum and Regulation Reform for TEVT","The private sector, in addition to providing and financing for the training, is involved in proposing changes to the training curriculum, drafting changes in training regulations, providing advice and supervision on training and administering examinations.",""],[1,"242","3","Government Coordination and Staffing Support for Vocational Schools","In parallel, the government is actively involved in enacting training regulations, issuing curriculum and paying teaching staff in vocational schools.",""],[1,"242","3","Coordination of TEVT Seat Supply","The government also plays a very active role in co-ordinating the supply and number of TEVT seats available.",""],[1,"243","6","TEVT Curriculum Standardization and Harmonization","The Department of Skills Development will be designated as the agency to develop and standardise TEVT curriculum starting in 2011.",""],[1,"243","7","Technical and Vocational Education and Training Curriculum Quality Assurance","The Department of Skills Development will ensure the TEVT curriculum developed meets the","Department of Skills Development"],[1,"244","1","Curriculum Bank Establishment and Maintenance","the Department will establish and maintain a curriculum bank to deposit all curricula developed.",""],[1,"244","3","National TEVT Certification Standardisation","the Malaysian Skills Certificate will be adopted as the national certification for TEVT.",""],[1,"244","4","Skills Certificate Equivalence Recognition","Recognising and equating various levels of Malaysian Skills Certificate with certifications issued by TEVT providers by 2012;",""],[1,"244","5","Mandatory Malaysian Skills Certificate Requirement for Selected Occupations","Mandating workers to have Malaysian Skills Certificate or equivalent in selected occupations; this will be implemented in stages beginning 2012;",""],[1,"244","6","Expansion of Malaysian Skills Certificate Entry Qualification","Broadening Malaysian Skills Certificate as the entry qualification for more programmes in public service and courses in advanced technical, vocational and higher education institutions by 2011.",""],[1,"244","7","Board of Technologists Malaysia Establishment","To accelerate the recognition of these certifications, a Board of Technologists Malaysia will be established.",""],[1,"244","8","Malaysia-Japan International Institute of Technology Establishment","the Malaysia- Japan International Institute of Technology will be established as an independent institute under the Universiti Teknologi Malaysia.",""],[1,"245","2","TEVT Course Rationalisation and Coordination Review","TEVT institutions will begin to review, rationalise and improve co-ordination of courses offered by the end of 2011.",""],[1,"265","2","National Skills Training Emphasis","Skills training will be given a special emphasis during the Plan period, to ensure Malaysia develops the necessary human capital to meet industry requirements, drive productivity improvements and enable moving up the value chain.",""],[1,"265","2","Technical and Vocational Education Mainstreaming","Technical education and vocational training will be mainstreamed, and tertiary education will be significantly upgraded via greater institutional",""]],"48":[[1,"40","2","Comprehensive Human Capital Development Reform","the Government will undertake a comprehensive reform across the entire life-cycle of human capital development, from upgrading early childhood education right through to upskilling the existing adult workforce.",""],[1,"40","2","Teacher Development and Motivation Initiative","Developing and motivating teachers will be the focus towards driving improvements in student outcomes.",""],[1,"40","2","School and Principal Accountability for Student Performance","Schools and principals will be made increasingly accountable for student performance.",""],[1,"40","5","High Performing Schools Establishment","Initiatives include the establishment of high performing schools and prestigious meritorious scholarships for top performers.",""],[1,"40","5","Meritorious Scholarship Programme for Top Performers","Initiatives include the establishment of high performing schools and prestigious meritorious scholarships for top performers.",""],[1,"53","3","Teacher Improvement for Student Outcomes","moving away from merely building schools, to improving teachers to lift student outcomes",""],[1,"104","2","Development of World-Class Educational Institutions","An important step is to develop world-class educational institutions with world-class leadership, particularly universities.",""]],"49":[[1,"220","8","Teacher Quality and School Leadership Improvement Strategies","the Government will move beyond an emphasis on investing in bricks and mortar for providing access to education, to investing in the most critical levers that impact student outcomes, such as the quality of teachers and the leadership in schools.",""],[1,"220","11","School Leadership Development and Performance Management","Invest heavily in head teachers and principals as the primary drivers of change via rigorous selection, extensive training and robust performance management based on student outcomes;",""],[1,"221","1","Teaching Profession Talent Attraction and Development Programme","Attract and develop top talent in the teaching profession.",""],[1,"227","1","New Deal Performance Incentive for School Leaders","(New Deal) for head teachers and principals commencing in 2010 will reward them financially and non-financially for exceptional performance.",""],[1,"228","1","School Performance Reward and Remedial Training Programme","This would give head teachers and principals a chance to receive a reward regardless of the starting points of their schools, as long as they are able to achieve significant improvements in the performance of their schools.",""],[1,"228","2","Education Leadership Training and Support Programme","The Government recognises that leaders and drivers are critical to any change process, and will continue to strengthen the leadership training and support provided to them.",""],[1,"228","4","Blended Educational and Management Course Delivery","The educational and management courses will be delivered on campus as well as online using the Institute's e-learning platform, and complemented by a digital repository of knowledge.",""],[1,"228","4","Consultation, Coaching and Mentoring Service-Line Approach","Consultation, coaching and mentoring will also be given more emphasis as IAB moves towards a service-line approach to help school leaders improve performance.",""],[1,"228","4","School Improvement Leadership Coaching Support","In line with the School Improvement Programme, specialist principal coaches will provide additional leadership coaching and support to school leaders at low performing schools.",""],[1,"228","5","Teacher Quality Improvement Measures","During the Plan period, the Government will undertake measures to systematically improve both the quality of the new teacher intake as well as to upgrade the quality and professionalism of all existing teachers in the system.",""],[1,"230","2","Nationwide Teaching Profession Marketing Campaign","Programmes will be launched during the Plan period, including a high-profile nationwide marketing campaign, to raise the awareness of teaching as a highly regarded profession.",""],[1,"230","3","Teaching Profession Elevation Initiative","The Government will seek to elevate the status of teaching as the profession of choice by highlighting and reinforcing the following four value propositions:",""],[1,"230","5","New Deal for Teachers Career Development Reform","Under the New Deal for Teachers, the teaching profession will have excellent career prospects, with extensive opportunities for professional development, as well as an accelerated career path for performers;",""],[1,"230","9","Teacher Trainee Practicum Quality Improvement","steps will be taken to improve the consistency and quality of the practicum experience of teacher trainees in terms of increasing time spent on practicum training, and engaging experienced teachers with strong mentoring skills to supervise trainees.",""],[1,"231","2","Teach for Malaysia Programme","Malaysia intends to launch a high profile 'Teach for Malaysia' programme to attract the best and brightest Malaysian graduates to teach for two years at underperforming or rural schools.",""],[1,"231","3","Fast-Track Graduate Teacher Training Programme","Participating graduates will enter a fast-track training programme where they will receive intensive training in latest teaching methods.",""],[1,"231","4","Postgraduate Teaching Course Extension","The Postgraduate Teaching Course will be extended from one year to one and a half years to increase the practicum experience of teacher trainees;",""],[1,"231","5","Practicum Programme Coordination","State Education Departments will coordinate the practicum programme by facilitating the",""],[1,"231","7","Teacher Mentoring Courses for Qualifying Schools","Experienced teachers in qualifying schools will be provided with mentoring courses to upgrade their capabilities;",""],[1,"232","1","Practicum Training Performance Linkage","The quality of the practicum training provided will be linked to the performance evaluation of the school and the mentor teachers.",""],[1,"232","2","Removal of Guaranteed Teacher Trainee Placement","Guaranteed placement for teacher trainees in ITEs and public universities will be removed.",""],[1,"232","3","Teacher Training System Liberalisation and Talent Pool Expansion","The talent pool of teacher trainees will also be expanded from the existing ITEs and public universities to include private universities and colleges to 'open up' sourcing of trained teachers from outside public institutions.",""],[1,"232","4","New Deal for Teachers","During the Plan period, the Government will launch and implement a comprehensive New Deal for all teachers in Malaysia, both to fundamentally transform the attractiveness, as well as to radically raise the professionalism and profile of the teaching profession.",""],[1,"232","4","Increase Graduate Teacher Share in Schools","the Government will increase the percentage of graduate teachers in schools, from 89.4% in 2009 to 90.0% by 2015 in secondary schools, and from 28.0% in 2009 to 60.0% by 2015 for primary schools.",""],[1,"232","5","New Deal for the Teaching Profession","The New Deal for the teaching profession will incorporate three elements:",""],[1,"232","7","Continuous Professional Development for Teachers","Enhanced and systematic Continuous Professional Development (CPD) for all teachers;",""],[1,"233","1","Teacher Career Progression Reform","The slow career progression of the teaching career will be addressed.",""],[1,"233","2","Teacher Career Progression and Fast-Tracking Reform","A faster career progression and fast-tracking for high performing teachers is key to making the teaching profession attractive, and help to ensure high quality potential teacher candidates are not turned away.",""],[1,"233","2","Senior Teacher Advancement and Mentoring System","In addition, allowing more teachers to reach more senior grade levels will result in creating a larger pool of experienced teachers who can then mentor and coach new teachers earlier in their career.",""],[1,"233","3","Teacher Career Track Reform","Under the New Deal, the career track for teachers will be changed with faster timelines for them to progress through the first few grade levels based on competency and performance levels.",""],[1,"233","4","Comprehensive Continuing Professional Development for Teachers","A more comprehensive approach towards CPD will be rolled out in 2011, consisting of the following elements:",""],[1,"233","5","Tailored Continuous Professional Development Modules for Teachers","Tailored CPD modules mapped to each grade level to better equip teachers for new role requirements at each grade level;",""],[1,"233","7","Teacher Continuing Professional Development Expansion","A broader range of CPD modules and modes of delivery, such as formal training courses, post-graduate studies, distance learning, and coaching activities, to allow teachers to have greater choice and to be less disruptive to school operations.",""],[1,"234","1","Teacher Performance Evaluation Reform","Evaluation scores for teachers will need to meaningfully differentiate between different levels of performance, and be less subjective and more evidence-driven.",""],[1,"234","2","New Teacher Evaluation Approach","A new evaluation approach will be implemented in 2011 that is consistent with practices in top performing school systems, to ensure greater consistency, objectivity across evaluations and to instil a stronger performance culture in schools.",""],[1,"265","2","Teacher Quality Improvement Initiative","Developing and enhancing the quality of teachers will be the focus towards driving improvements in student outcomes.",""]],"50":[[1,"246","12","Faculty Recruitment and Retention Initiative","Hiring and retaining the best faculty members.",""],[1,"248","5","Faculty Recruitment and Retention Incentive Scheme","Freedom to attract and retain the best faculty members through attractive incentives and competitive remuneration;",""],[1,"251","2","Faculty PhD Qualification Expansion Programme","Efforts will be intensified to raise the number of faculty members with PhD qualifications.",""],[1,"251","3","Faculty Recruitment and Remuneration Reform","the recruitment process for faculty members will be refined and made transparent to attract top talent.",""],[1,"251","5","Faculty Career Development Support Programme","Career development support will be given greater priority.",""],[1,"251","6","Contract-Based Recruitment of Retired and Foreign Faculty","retired faculty members and capable foreign lecturers will be encouraged to serve in public universities on a contract basis.",""],[1,"251","6","Incentive Scheme for Visiting and Part-Time Lecturers","More visiting and part-time lecturers, especially from industry, will be drawn to teach in public universities by introducing attractive incentives.",""],[1,"251","6","Faculty Service Scheme Review","the scheme of service for faculty members will be reviewed to enable them to advance to the highest grade possible within their own scheme of service without holding administrative positions such as dean or head of department.",""]],"51":[[1,"11","10","Bai'ah (New Deal) for Head Teachers and Principals","Introducing the Bai'ah or New Deal for Head Teachers and Principals Enhancing Support and Coaching for Head Teachers and Principals",""],[1,"20","7","LINUS Literacy and Numeracy Programme","The nationwide LINUS programme is aimed at improving literacy and numeracy for primary school students",""]],"52":[[1,"138","16","Skills Level Improvement Initiative","Commit to improving skill levels.",""],[1,"145","3","Human Capital Development","The economic reform measures in the Tenth Malaysia Plan such as modernising of business regulations, human capital development, increasing domestic competition, removing market distortions and improving infrastructure will provide the enabling ecosystem for NKEAs.",""],[1,"146","7","Industry-Partnership Skills Training Programme","Enhancing skills (both technical and management) training in partnership with industry;",""],[1,"152","5","Industry-Academia-Government Collaboration for Curriculum Development and Industrial Training","This will be done through focussed collaboration between the industry-academia-government, especially for curriculum development and industrial training.",""],[1,"159","3","Science, Technology, Innovation, and Human Capital Investment","Malaysia will also commit to ongoing investment in science and technology, innovation, and human capital.",""],[1,"255","3","Workforce Upskilling and Reskilling Initiative","There is an urgent need to upgrade and re-skill the existing workforce, to move the economy up the value chain.",""],[1,"255","4","Skills Development Fund Expansion for Upskilling and Retraining","The coverage of the Skills Development Fund will be expanded to promote upskilling and retraining of the workforce.",""],[1,"256","1","Expansion of the Human Resource Development Fund Coverage","Cost sharing will also be intensified through extending the coverage of the Human Resource Development Fund (HRDF) from 44 to 70 subsectors.",""],[1,"256","1","SME Training and Skills-Upgrading Matching Grants","During the Plan period, an allocation of RM50 million will be provided to continue the matching grants for training and skills-upgrading for employees in SMEs.",""],[1,"256","1","Apprenticeship Funding for Vocational Training","In addition, RM50 million will be allocated to fund apprenticeships involving more than 8,000 students.",""],[1,"256","2","Industrial PhD Co-Sponsorship Programme","During the Plan period, a programme will be introduced to promote participation from the industry to co-sponsor employees to obtain industrial PhDs.",""],[1,"256","3","Partial Financial Assistance for PhD Candidates at Local Universities","the Government will continue the successful programme introduced under the economic stimulus package in 2009 to provide partial financial assistance for candidates pursuing PhD programmes at local universities",""],[1,"256","4","Private Sector-Led Accredited In-House Vocational Training Programmes","The Government will encourage and intensify the involvement of the private sector to establish accredited in-house training programmes and to extend these programmes beyond their employees to produce qualified skilled workers who are employable across the industry.",""],[1,"256","5","Industrial Skills Enhancement Programme","The Industrial Skills Enhancement Programme (INSEP) is a training and development programme in the engineering, ICT and management fields",""],[1,"258","4","Worker Skills Certification Expansion Programme","programme will be expanded with the goal of formally recognising the experience and expertise of workers, as well as to encourage and reward lifelong learning among the workforce.",""],[1,"258","4","Training Financial Assistance for Skills Certification","Financial assistance for workers to undertake training to qualify for the Malaysian Skills Certificate will commence in 2011.",""],[1,"258","4","Skills Credit Bank for Training Records and Certification","a skills credit bank will be established by the Department of Skills Development to maintain a database for training records and facilitating the certification of skilled workers.","Department of Skills Development"],[1,"265","4","Skills Training for Bottom 40 Percent Households","skills training initiatives will be focused on the bottom 40% of households",""]],"53":[[1,"167","7","Special Education Access Support for Bottom 40% Households","Providing special consideration to the bottom 40% households for placements in boarding schools, matriculation, universities and scholarships,",""],[1,"167","8","Rural Student Hostel Support for Urban School Access","Providing hostels to assist rural children in attending better schools in urban areas",""],[1,"182","2","Equitable Education Access Support for Bottom 40% Households","During the Plan period, more equitable access to education opportunities will be provided to children from the bottom 40% households.",""],[1,"182","3","Rural Student Boarding Support Programme","During the Ninth Plan period, the concept of enabling rural children with high academic potential to attend better schools in urban areas was piloted whereby standard five and standard six children from rural areas were enrolled in special boarding facilities.",""],[1,"182","5","Expansion of Asrama Hostel Programmes","Asrama programmes will also be expanded, whereby urban students from different ethnicities in primary and secondary schools are grouped in hostels to provide a more conducive learning environment and extended learning support.",""],[1,"182","5","KWAPM Student Assistance Scheme","Eligible students from specific target groups will continue to receive assistance from Kumpulan Wang Amanah Pelajar Miskin (KWAPM) such as allowances, scholarships, supplementary food, school uniforms and tuition and transportation fees.",""],[1,"182","5","Priority Placement Support for Bottom 40 Percent Households","A special consideration for placements in boarding schools, matriculation centers and public universities will be given to students from the bottom 40% households.",""],[1,"182","5","Merit-Based Financial Assistance for Private Education Students","students who have secured places in private education institutions will be given financial assistance based on merit, to enable them to pursue their education.",""],[1,"186","4","Sekolah Model Khas Expansion","Sekolah Model Khas will be expanded to address high drop-out rates at secondary school level due to location factors.",""],[1,"186","4","Integrated Primary and Secondary School Management Model","This concept integrates primary and secondary education up to Form Three under the same school management.",""],[1,"186","4","Secondary School Boarding Facilities Expansion","In addition, boarding facilities for secondary schools will be expanded.",""]],"54":[[1,"220","10","School Accountability and Guided Autonomy Reform","Hold schools accountable for changes in student outcomes.",""],[1,"225","1","Annual School Performance Ranking System","All schools in Malaysia will be assessed and ranked annually according to performance bands.","MOE"],[1,"225","2","School Improvement Toolkit and School Improvement Plans","School Improvement Toolkit and Plans.",""],[1,"227","2","Annual Public School Performance Assessment and Ranking","The performance of all public schools will be assessed and ranked annually according to a composite score.",""],[1,"234","5","School Delivery Mechanism Reform","Improving the delivery mechanism for schools will require changes in the most critical processes directly affecting schools, such as teacher deployment, school performance management, as well as the role of the Ministry, State, and District Education Departments.","Ministry | State, and District Education Departments"],[1,"234","5","MOE School Service Lines","To ensure optimal delivery of service, the MOE will deploy specific 'Service Lines' to provide tailored assistance to schools that need it the most, including coaching, capability- building and supporting tools.","MOE"],[1,"265","2","School Accountability and Autonomy Support Reform","Schools and principals will be made increasingly accountable for student performance, and will be provided with the corresponding support and autonomies.",""],[1,"346","4","High Performing Schools Flexibility Initiative","High performing schools will be given flexibility in adapting curriculum and instruction methods",""],[1,"347","1","School Mentoring and Exchange Networks","These schools are responsible for maintaining excellent student outcomes as well as sharing knowledge and expertise with other schools through mentoring networks, teacher attachments and student exchange programmes;",""],[1,"347","7","School Performance Band Ranking and Transparent Reporting System","As part of the School Improvement Programme, the performance of all schools on student outcomes will be ranked into various performance bands.",""]],"55":[[1,"223","4","Literacy and Numeracy Screening Programme","The Literacy and Numeracy Screening (LINUS) programme aims to ensure all students3 have basic literacy and numeracy skills after the first three years of primary education.",""],[1,"223","5","Special Programme for Children with Learning Disabilities","Children with learning disabilities will be placed in a special programme with separate targets.",""],[1,"224","1","School Remedial Teaching Programme","will deploy trained facilitators and remedial teachers to schools to implement the programme.",""],[1,"224","2","Upholding Bahasa Melayu and Strengthening English Programme","The Government will implement the Upholding Bahasa Melayu and Strengthening English programme during the Plan period.",""],[1,"224","3","English Teaching and Learning Curriculum Reform","The programme will also seek to strengthen the teaching and learning of English with the introduction of a new curriculum, stressing the five key skill areas of reading, speaking and listening, writing, grammar and language arts.",""],[1,"224","5","English Proficiency Improvement Initiatives","The Government will continue to access the effectiveness of the programme on an ongoing basis and will develop further initiatives to improve English proficiency in students.",""]],"56":[[1,"239","7","TEVT Instructor Development Programme","Developing highly effective TEVT instructors;",""],[1,"241","6","TEVT Instructor Career Progression Acceleration","The career progression path for TEVT instructors will be accelerated to make TEVT teaching",""],[1,"243","2","Flexible Entry Pathways for Vocational Instructors","To facilitate this, flexible pathways of entry into the vocational instructor and trainer profession will be created, and any requirements that discourage mid-career entry into the profession will be removed.",""],[1,"243","3","Expansion of Part-Time Instructor Working Arrangements","part-time working arrangements will be expanded and encouraged to tap those who wish to develop a career as an instructor and at the same time retain a job in industry.",""],[1,"243","4","TVET-Industry Partnership and Instructor Industry Placement","Moving forward, the interchange and partnership between TEVT institutions and industry will be strongly encouraged, so that vocational instructors spend substantial time in industry to update their knowledge, and vocational instructors in firms",""],[1,"243","5","Expansion of Instructor Training Capacity","the capacity of the Centre for Instructor and Advanced Skills Training will be expanded with new training approaches and methodologies.",""],[1,"243","5","New Centre for Instructor Skills Training","A new centre for instructor skills training will be developed to add a further training capacity of 800 instructors each year.",""],[1,"243","5","Coordination of Instructor Training Programmes","the Department of Skills Development will coordinate the provision of instructor training programmes in other public skills training institutions.",""],[1,"246","5","Workplace Coach and Instructor Training Programme","A total of RM7.5 million will be allocated to train these coaches, instructors, and facilitators.",""]],"57":[[1,"246","10","University Autonomy and Performance Culture Reform","Providing greater autonomy to universities and strengthening their performance cultures;",""],[1,"248","8","Accelerated Programme for Excellence University Autonomy","Under the Accelerated Programme for Excellence (APEX), an APEX university is granted autonomy in governance, human resource (selection of staff, faculty members and top management), finance and student admissions.",""],[1,"249","1","Higher Education Institutional Rating System (SETARA)","A Rating System for Malaysian Higher Education Institutions (SETARA) is being introduced for public universities and will be extended to all private degree-conferring tertiary institutions.",""],[1,"249","2","University Vice-Chancellor Performance Accountability System","The vice chancellor of a university will be held accountable for the performance of the university, as determined by the performance assessment, with the consequence of non-renewal of contract in the event of poor performance.",""],[1,"249","2","University Staff Performance Accountability Cascade","the vice chancellor will hold all university staff accountable for their performance, which will push the culture of accountability further through the institution.",""],[1,"249","3","Performance-Based Funding for Public Tertiary Institutions","During the Plan period, performance-based funding for public tertiary institutions will be implemented, with the intention of providing a transparent funding mechanism to catalyse improved performance.",""],[1,"249","4","Performance-Based University Funding Mechanism","Government performance-based funding linked to SETARA rating.",""],[1,"249","5","Demand-Side Funding Reform for Tertiary Education","Shift from supply-side to demand-side funding.",""],[1,"250","1","Demand-Side Tertiary Education Financing Reform","The existing approach of direct public funding or grants disbursed to public institutions will increasingly shift towards demand-side funding via student loans and scholarships in line with a more market-based approach;",""],[1,"250","2","University Alternative Funding Diversification","Public universities must increasingly seek alternative sources of funds, including from corporations, the private sector or alumni.",""]],"58":[[1,"53","5","Outsourced Skills Training Service Delivery","building and operating public services towards buying services from the private sector.",""],[1,"355","6","Private Sector Skills Training Procurement","the Government will increasingly move away from building physical infrastructure and operating public services towards buying services from the private sector.",""]],"59":[[1,"265","1","Comprehensive Human Capital Development Reform","The Government will undertake a complete reform across the entire life-cycle of human capital development, from upgrading early childhood education right through to upskilling the existing adult workforce.",""]],"60":[[1,"93","1","World-Class Infrastructure for Growth Initiative","Putting in place world-class infrastructure for growth by significantly increasing broadband penetration, continuing to upgrade physical infrastructure to enhance access and connectivity, and ensuring effective sourcing and delivery of energy;",""],[1,"104","4","National Broadband Expansion","Information technology (IT) infrastructure will be substantially extended under the Plan period to facilitate connectivity to the global knowledge network.",""],[1,"104","4","Household Broadband Coverage Target","The Government will target 75% of households to have broadband by 2015",""],[1,"104","4","Malaysia Research and Education Network Promotion","the Malaysia Research and Education Network (MyREN) will be further promoted to allow Malaysian researchers to connect to the global research community.",""],[1,"131","1","National Infrastructure Upgrading Investments","During the Plan period, continued investments will be made to upgrade the quality of the nation's infrastructure including broadband networks, ports, double-track railway lines and airports that enhance access and connectivity and, therefore, improve productivity.",""],[1,"132","1","Household Broadband Expansion Initiatives","This will be achieved via two main initiatives: High- Speed Broadband (HSBB) and Broadband to General Population (BBGP), which leverage both wired and wireless technologies.",""],[1,"132","2","High-Speed Broadband Initiative Expansion","The HSBB initiative will cover about 1.3 million premises by 2012 in the high population, high economic impact 'Zone 1' areas (state capitals, large urban and industrial zones) as shown in Chart 3-16.",""],[1,"132","3","National Broadband Rollout","The national rollout of broadband is expected to incur a cost of approximately RM2.6 billion.",""],[1,"132","3","Broadband for General Population (BBGP) Expansion","complemented by the BBGP which will cover 'Zones 2 and 3' (semi-urban and rural areas).",""],[1,"132","3","High-Speed Broadband Rollout Financing Arrangement","The cost of HSBB rollout will be complemented by the private sector whereas that of BBGP will be partly funded through Universal Services Provision Fund.",""],[1,"133","9","Broadband Access Incentives and Affordability Measures","a series of measures will be introduced, including tax rebates for broadband subscription, providing affordable packages for students and the rural population, encouraging computer ownership as well as promoting development of local content both in the public and private sectors.",""],[1,"133","9","Mandatory Broadband Facilities in Building By-law","The existing Uniform Building By-law 1984 will also be amended to make it mandatory for developers to provide broadband facilities in residential and commercial areas.",""]],"61":[[1,"342","3","Online Multi-Agency Public Service Portal","This online portal offers services that cut across multiple agencies through a single interface.",""],[1,"342","4","Digital Payment and Notification Service Enhancement","To improve ease of use, the service offers payments via credit or debit card transactions as well as tailored notifications and alerts through email and SMS.",""],[1,"343","1","eKL Online Government Service Portal Expansion","During the Plan period, the system will be expanded to other regions outside of the Klang Valley, with a focus on areas of strategic economic growth under the Government Regional Electronic Advancement Transformation Programme (GREAT).",""],[1,"343","3","Public Service Access Hubs for Underserved Communities","These hubs will also function as an additional channel for people in underserved communities to access public services such as renewal of road tax, driving licenses and business licenses.",""]],"62":[[1,"361","6","Whole-of-Government ICT Infrastructure Consolidation","The Government will continue to improve its productivity through a whole-of-government ICT infrastructure consolidation exercise which will result in increased productivity, minimised redundancies and improved efficiencies brought about through centralised management and maintenance of shared resources.",""]],"63":[[1,"198","5","Rural ICT Access and Digital Skills Exposure","The rural population will also be exposed to the utilisation of ICT facilities and appropriate software packages to improve their knowledge.",""],[1,"198","5","Telecentre Strengthening and Reorientation Programme","In this context, the role of telecentres will be strengthened and reoriented to link them to income generating opportunities, particularly in enhancing marketing of rural products as well as improving access to business opportunities.",""],[1,"198","5","Sub-district Telecentre Establishment","it is targeted that at least one telecentre will be established in each sub-district (mukim).",""],[1,"199","1","1Malaysia Telecentres","the Government together with the communications and multimedia industry will create 1Malaysia telecentres especially in the rural areas.",""]],"64":[[1,"333","3","Environmental Resource Valuation Policies and Mechanisms","This means establishing policies and mechanisms for the proper valuation of environmental resources in terms of assessing opportunity costs and environmental impacts of both public and private investments.",""]],"65":[[1,"309","4","Environmental Outreach and Awareness Programmes","Expanding outreach and awareness programmes targeting various segments of society, such as the Langkawi Award, Rakan Alam Sekitar, Malaysia Environment Week, Promotion of Cleaner Production to Industries and Environmental Debate amongst higher institutions.",""],[1,"322","2","Environmental Sustainability Awareness Campaign","To achieve this, the Government will pursue co-operative efforts with the private sector and civil society to bring this message to all Malaysians;",""],[1,"329","2","Public Awareness and Participation Promotion Programme","Promoting education and awareness programmes in collaboration with universities, researchinstitutes, NGOs, aswellas the private sector as part of their corporate social responsibility programmes.",""]],"66":[[1,"21","9","Federalisation of Solid Waste Management and Public Cleansing Functions","Federalisation of solid waste management and public cleansing functions to drive improved outcomes for the public and environment",""],[1,"304","5","Solid Waste Management Restructuring","Restructuring solid waste management.",""],[1,"312","1","Federalisation of Solid Waste Management and Public Cleansing","During the Plan period, the Government will complete restructuring efforts in this sector with the federalisation of solid waste management and public cleansing and full enforcement of the Solid Waste and Public Cleansing Management Act 2007.",""],[1,"312","6","Local Authority Core Functions Focus","Local authorities will be able to focus on core functions",""],[1,"312","8","Federal Transfer of Solid Waste Management and Public Cleansing Responsibilities","With federalisation, Solid Waste Management (SWM) and Public Cleansing (PC) responsibilities will be transferred to the federal government",""],[1,"313","1","Federalisation of Solid Waste Management and Public Cleansing","With the completion of the federalisation effort, local authorities will be relieved of this workload, allowing them to focus their efforts on core functions such as licensing, enforcement, planning and development.",""],[1,"313","2","Household Solid Waste Collection Privatization","The Government will fully privatise the collection of household solid waste to three concessionaires.",""],[1,"313","2","Licensed Private Solid Waste Management and Public Cleansing Services","Other private operators will be licensed to operate solid waste management and public cleansing services.",""],[1,"313","2","Performance-Based Solid Waste Service Contracting","These operators will be subjected to a stringent performance management regime linked to KPIs such as the coverage of service, compliance to schedule and frequency of collection, number of complaints and soiling of roads from leachate.",""],[1,"313","2","Performance-Linked Payments to Concessionaires","Payments to concessionaires will be linked to achievement of these KPIs.",""],[1,"313","2","Solid Waste Operations Efficiency Measures","Measures to drive efficiencies in operations will include optimising transportation costs by utilising the best available",""],[1,"332","6","Federalisation of Solid Waste Management and Public Cleansing Services","Completing the federalisation of solid waste management and public cleansing services to facilitate the modernisation of waste collection, handling and disposal as well as the upkeep of shared public spaces;",""],[1,"363","9","Federalisation of Solid Waste Management and Public Cleansing","Under the federalisation initiative, the functions of solid waste management and public cleansing responsibilities will be shifted from the jurisdiction of local authorities to the federal government.",""]],"67":[[1,"49","9","Eco-Tourism Promotion Initiative","Promoting eco-tourism to create commercial value in sustainability;",""],[1,"49","10","Community-Based Eco-Tourism and Biodiversity Conservation Support","Facilitating greater participation of local communities in eco-tourism activities (e.g. fishermen as guides at Kilim Geopark, Langkawi) and bio-diversity protection (e.g. compilation of knowledge on bio-tropical herbs) as a self sustaining means to support environmental conservation.",""],[1,"49","11","Public-Private CSR Flagship Species Conservation Initiatives","Initiating public-private CSR initiatives around protection of flagship species (e.g. the Malayan tiger, orangutan, leatherback turtle) as part of broader habitat conservation efforts.",""],[1,"51","11","Community-Based Environmental Conservation Cooperation Mechanisms","The Government will therefore explore means to facilitate such cooperative mechanisms, including promoting greater participation of local communities and developing income generating activities in eco-tourism.",""],[1,"331","2","Local Community Conservation and Eco-Tourism Participation","Co-opting local communities in conservation efforts.",""]],"68":[[1,"312","16","Household Waste Separation at Source for Recycling","Separation at source by households to facilitate recycling",""],[1,"314","3","Household Waste Separation and Recycling Policy Review","Options to make it compulsory for homeowners to separate waste at source to facilitate recycling will be reviewed.",""],[1,"314","3","Private Sector Solid Waste Management and 3R Programme","The Government will require private sector commitment, in particular manufacturers, to improve solid waste management, especially through the Reduce, Reuse and Recycle (3R) programmes.",""],[1,"314","3","Deposit Refund and Take-Back Scheme","As part of this effort, a deposit refund scheme and a take back system will be implemented.",""],[1,"328","1","Public Awareness Campaign on Waste Reduction, Reuse, and Recycling","The Government will further enhance public awareness on the importance of reducing, reusing and recycling of waste.",""]],"69":[[1,"328","2","Forest Gazettement and Protected Area Expansion","During the Tenth Plan period, further initiatives will be undertaken to encourage States to gazette forests, especially the water catchment areas, as protected areas.",""],[1,"328","2","National Tree Planting Initiative","the Government with the participation of the private sector, non-government organisations (NGOs) and the public at large will continue its efforts in planting more trees to green the country.",""],[1,"329","6","Common Vision on Biodiversity Implementation","To protect these assets, the Government adopted the Common Vision on Biodiversity, which promotes a three-pronged implementation approach and outreach strategy that consists of: strengthening the Protected Areas System; managing landscapes and seascapes for biodiversity; and mainstreaming of biodiversity.",""],[1,"329","7","Central Forest Spine and Heart of Borneo Biodiversity Protection Initiative","During the Plan period, efforts to protect biodiversity and habitats will be strengthened with the implementation of the Central Forest Spine of 4.32 million hectares in Peninsular Malaysia and the Heart of Borneo of 6.0 million hectares in Sabah and Sarawak.",""],[1,"330","1","Wildlife Management and Endangered Species Protection","Malaysia will intensify its efforts in wildlife management and in the protection of endangered species.",""],[1,"330","1","Enforcement of Endangered Species Trade Regulations","The Government will enforce regulations governing the trade of endangered fauna and flora in line with Malaysia's obligation to the Convention on International Trade in Endangered Species of Wild Fauna and Flora (CITES).",""],[1,"330","1","Flagship Species Conservation Partnership","The orang utan, Malayan Tiger, tapir and gaur, among others, serve as flagship species for Malaysia and will become focal points for conservation efforts in partnership with the private sector.",""],[1,"330","1","National Tiger Conservation Action Plan","The National Tiger Conservation Action Plan will be implemented to increase the tiger population and provide effective protection for tigers and their prey including through efforts to conserve contiguous forest ecosystems.",""]],"70":[[1,"330","2","Integration of the Coastal Zone Physical Plan into the NPP","the integration of the Coastal Zone Physical Plan into the NPP will allow improved management and protection of the shoreline, including efforts to intensify mangrove planting",""],[1,"330","2","Review of Marine Park Management Plan and Legislation","The Marine Park Management Plan for Peninsular Malaysia and existing legislation will be reviewed to further enhance the management of marine biodiversity",""],[1,"330","2","National Action Plan on the Coral Triangle Initiative","the National Action Plan on the Coral Triangle Initiative will be implemented to ensure the conservation and sustainable use of marine resources",""],[1,"330","2","Marine Resource Management Capacity Enhancement","the capacity of marine resource management will be enhanced to track changes in marine habitats and resources",""]],"71":[[1,"330","3","Integrated Biodiversity Database Development","During the Plan period, efforts will be implemented to link or integrate existing biodiversity inventory and databases, with a view to develop a comprehensive one-stop database in the future.",""],[1,"331","3","Access and Benefit Sharing Legal Framework","The Government will establish a legal framework on access and benefit sharing to ensure that the benefits derived are distributed fairly and equitably.",""],[1,"331","4","Biosafety Act Enforcement for Living Modified Organisms","Effective enforcement of the Biosafety Act 2007 will ensure that potentially adverse impacts on biodiversity and human health from biotechnology that uses LMOs is minimised and properly managed.",""]],"72":[[1,"281","2","Creative Industry Grants and Loans for Art Clusters","Support for artists will be provided in the form of creative industry grants or loans for the creation of art clusters, namely the Art Enclave or Perkampungan Seni.",""],[1,"281","7","Biennial Exhibition Space and Arts Education Facilities Development","The US$27 billion also involves building a bienniale exhibition space, arts school and an arts college",""],[1,"281","8","Performing Arts and Cultural Infrastructure Expansion","Seoul will invest US$7.9 billion to build more performing arts theatres, increase the number of art galleries from 25 to 50, and museums from 67 to 150 by 2015",""],[1,"281","9","Historical Sites Renovation Investment in Beijing","In Beijing, the government is investing US$289 million to renovate historical places of interest, such as the China National Museum",""],[1,"282","2","International Arts and Cultural Events Promotion","the Government will encourage the hosting of international arts and cultural events in cities.",""],[1,"282","2","Transformation of Iconic Cultural Institutions","iconic cultural institutions such as the Muzium Negara, Balai Seni Lukis Negara and Istana Budaya will be transformed to attract international talent to create, premiere, perform and exhibit in Kuala Lumpur.",""],[1,"282","3","Malaysia Truly Asia Centre Development","The Malaysia Truly Asia Centre will be developed as an iconic tourism destination to showcase Malaysian culture, art",""]],"73":[[1,"151","2","Tourism Product Development and Promotion Initiative","the need to develop vibrant and iconic tourism products, improve maintenance of existing tourism sites and adopting focused tourism promotions.",""],[1,"151","5","Focused Tourism Cluster Development","Improving tourism products through the creation of focused tourism clusters that will leverage on existing and new iconic tourism products.",""],[1,"151","6","Development of Iconic Tourism Products through Public-Private Partnerships","Developing new iconic tourism products through the private sector and public-private partnership.",""],[1,"151","6","Promotion of Tourism Products and Activities","Tourism products and activities such as parks and gardens, arts tourism, shopping, signature events and festivals will also be promoted;",""],[1,"151","8","Tourism Malaysia Overseas Market Realignment","Realigning promotional and advertising activities and physical presence of Tourism Malaysia offices overseas by focusing on core markets, particularly Russia, India, China and Middle East;",""]],"74":[[1,"151","7","Tourist Site Maintenance Improvement Measures","Improving maintenance of tourist sites through multiple approaches, including through GLCs and corporate sponsorship, stronger enforcement and imposition of gate fees, particularly in environmentally sensitive and heritage sites;",""],[1,"151","9","Progressive Certification of Tourism Products and Activities","Introducing progressively certification of tourism products and activities to ensure quality, sustainability and safety.",""]],"75":[[1,"49","6","Feed-in Tariff for Renewable Energy Investment","Introducing Feed-in-tariff to help finance renewable energy investments;",""],[1,"49","7","Green Technology Fiscal Incentives and Funding","Providing fiscal incentives and funding for green technology investments;",""],[1,"106","5","National Green Technology Policy","There will be a push towards green technology through the National Green Technology Policy, in preparation for green products and services becoming the preferred choice for public procurement.",""],[1,"106","5","Green Technology Financing Scheme","the green technology financing scheme will continue to issue credit guarantees of 60% for companies developing or using green technology.",""],[1,"106","5","Standards Compliance Promotion for Firms","Firms will also be encouraged to meet Malaysian Standards and recognised international standards for goods and services such as Hazard Analysis and Critical Control Points and Good Manufacturing Practice.",""],[1,"155","7","Green Technology Council Streamlining","Streamlining the Green Technology Council to drive the green technology agenda across multiple ministries and agencies which include regulatory aspects, developmental, awareness and promotion;",""],[1,"155","9","Building Energy Efficiency Regulation Enforcement","Developing and enforcing regulations especially on energy efficiency in buildings for new developments;",""],[1,"155","10","Renewable Energy Investment Promotion and Long-Term Contracting","Promoting investment in renewable energy to provide long-term contracts for renewable energy providers and create the spillover effects on the related domestic service providers;",""],[1,"324","3","Greenhouse Gas Emissions Reduction Programmes","The Government has embarked on several programmes aimed at reducing emission of GHGs.",""],[1,"325","1","Renewable Energy Investment Incentive Framework","Creating stronger incentives for investments in renewable energy (RE);",""],[1,"325","7","Renewable Energy Policy and Action Plan Implementation","the Tenth Plan, several new initiatives anchored upon the Renewable Energy Policy and Action Plan will be undertaken",""],[1,"325","8","Feed-in Tariff for Renewable Energy","Introduction of a Feed-in Tariff (FIT) of 1% that will be incorporated into the electricity tariffs of consumers to support the development of RE.",""],[1,"325","9","Renewable Energy Fund Establishment","Establishment of a Renewable Energy Fund from the FIT to be administered by a special agency, the Sustainable Energy Development Authority, under the Ministry of Energy, Green Technology and Water (KeTTHA) to support development of RE.","Ministry of Energy, Green Technology and Water (KeTTHA)"],[1,"326","2","Renewable Energy Transition","Moving towards renewable energy replaces the need for fossil-fuel power plants",""],[1,"326","3","Feed-in Tariff Support for Renewable Energy Investments","RE investments will receive a huge push through FiT",""],[1,"326","5","Feed-in Tariff Introduction","Introduction of Feed-in Tariff (FIT) of 1% to be incorporated into the electricity tariffs of consumers",""],[1,"326","6","Renewable Energy Fund under the Feed-in Tariff","Establishment of a Renewable Energy Fund from the FiT to be administered by a special agency under KeTTHA.","KeTTHA"]],"76":[[1,"49","3","Energy and Water Pricing Reform","during the Plan period, the energy policy will move towards market pricing of gas by 2015 while water tariffs will be restructured towards full cost recovery.",""],[1,"135","3","Market-Based Energy Pricing Reform","The Policy will focus on five strategic pillars: adoption of market- based energy pricing;",""],[1,"136","13","Electricity Tariff Structure Review","the electricity tariff structure will be reviewed as a means of attracting high-quality investment.",""],[1,"136","14","Energy Subsidy Rationalisation","In line with overall strategy to rationalise subsidies, energy subsidies will be reduced, with the goal of",""],[1,"137","1","Market-Based Energy Pricing Reform","Gas prices for the power and non-power sectors will be revised every six months to gradually reflect market prices.",""],[1,"137","1","Energy Subsidy Decoupling and Bill Itemization","A decoupling approach for energy pricing will be undertaken to explicitly itemise subsidy value in consumer energy bills and eventually delink subsidy from energy use.",""],[1,"137","1","Targeted Energy Assistance for Low-Income Households","For low-income households and other groups for which the social safety net is required, different forms of assistance will be provided.",""],[1,"310","8","Gas Price Subsidy Rationalisation","gas prices for the power and non-power sectors will be revised every",""],[1,"311","1","Energy Subsidy Rationalization and Targeted Household Assistance","Consumer energy bills will explicitly itemise subsidy values and eventually de-link subsidy from energy use.",""],[1,"311","1","Power Sector Accounting and Regulatory Reform","Greater market discipline will be instilled through measures such as creating separate accounting for generation, transmission and distribution activities, introducing performance-based regulation and renegotiation of power purchase agreements.",""]],"77":[[1,"135","3","New Energy Policy (2011-2015)","The New Energy Policy (2011-2015) emphasises energy security and economic efficiency as well as environmental and social considerations.",""],[1,"135","3","Reliable Energy Supply Management Initiatives","The Policy will focus on five strategic pillars: initiatives to secure and manage reliable energy supply;",""],[1,"135","3","Energy Efficiency Promotion Measures","The Policy will focus on five strategic pillars: measures to encourage energy efficiency (EE);",""],[1,"135","3","Energy Governance Strengthening and Change Management","The Policy will focus on five strategic pillars: stronger governance and managing change, as shown in Chart 3-17.",""],[1,"135","4","Alternative Energy Resource Development and Fuel Import Diversification","Energy security will be enhanced through the development of alternative resources, particularly hydro as well as importation of coal and liquefied natural gas (LNG) by 2015.",""],[1,"135","4","Mandatory Biofuel Blending Policy","In the transport sector, blending of bio-fuel will be made mandatory beginning in 2011, further enhancing fuel security.",""],[1,"135","4","New Coal-Based Power Plant Development","Development of new coal-based plants will be undertaken to ensure security of supply in Peninsular Malaysia.",""],[1,"135","4","Supercritical Coal Technology Exploration","The application of super critical coal technology will be explored to reduce carbon emissions.",""],[1,"136","11","Nuclear Energy Feasibility and Preparedness Programme","of nuclear energy as an option for electricity generation will be considered to ensure reliable and cost-effective supply in Peninsular Malaysia.",""],[1,"136","12","Energy Efficiency Master Plan","During the Plan period, EE initiatives will gain momentum with the formulation of the Energy Efficiency Master Plan, setting of minimum energy performance standards for appliances and development of green technologies.",""],[1,"325","2","Energy Efficiency Promotion Initiative","Promoting energy efficiency to encourage productive use of energy;",""],[1,"326","9","National Energy Efficiency Master Plan","The National Energy Efficiency Master Plan, 2010 will be a holistic implementation roadmap to drive efficiency measures across sectors with a target to achieve cumulative energy savings of 4,000 kilo tonnes",""],[1,"327","2","Incandescent Light Bulb Phase-Out","Phasing out of incandescent light bulbs by 2014 to reduce carbon dioxide emissions by an estimated 732,000 tonnes and reducing energy usage by 1,074 gigawatts a year",""],[1,"327","3","Expanded Energy Performance Labelling Scheme","Increasing energy performance labelling from four (air conditioner, refrigerator, television and fan) to ten electrical appliances (six additional appliances - rice cooker, electric kettle, washing machine, microwave, clothes dryer and dishwasher).",""],[1,"327","5","Energy-Efficient Machinery and Equipment Adoption","Increasing the use of energy efficient machineries and equipment such as high efficiency motors, pumps and variable speed drive controls",""],[1,"327","6","Minimum Energy Performance Standards for Appliances","Introduction of Minimum Energy Performance Standards for selected appliances to restrict the manufacture, import and sale of inefficient appliances to consumers",""],[1,"327","7","Revision of Uniform Building By-Laws for Energy-Efficient Buildings","Revision of the Uniform Building By-Laws to incorporate the Malaysian Standard: Code of Practice on Energy Efficiency and Renewable Energy for Non-Residential Buildings (MS1525).",""],[1,"327","7","Wider Adoption of the Green Building Index","Wider adoption of the Green Building Index (GBI) to benchmark energy consumption in new and existing buildings",""],[1,"327","7","Thermal Insulation for Air-Conditioned Buildings","Increasing the use of thermal insulation for roofs in air conditioned buildings to save energy",""]],"78":[[1,"198","4","Rural Electricity Supply Expansion","During the Plan period, the coverage of electricity supply in rural areas will be extended through the national grid and alternative systems such as mini-hydro and solar hybrid.",""],[1,"199","9","Electricity Supply Expansion for Rakyat","Supplying electricity to rakyat with particular focus on Sabah and Sarawak.",""],[1,"200","2","Electricity Coverage Expansion Programme","In increasing electricity coverage, a total of 670 projects have commenced, covering 25,310 houses.",""],[1,"429","6","Rural Electricity Expansion","Expand rural electricity coverage",""]],"79":[[1,"205","3","Youth Skills and Values Preparation Programme","The Government recognises the vital importance of youth in the economy, therefore the Plan aims to better prepare them to undertake their roles in contributing towards national development, through instilling the right skills set, values and",""],[1,"205","6","Youth Development Programmes","The objective of youth development programmes will be to produce a youth population that is capable in the areas of skills, entrepreneurship and leadership.",""],[1,"205","7","Youth Development Programmes","Youth development programmes will be set up to create a generation of youth that is forward- looking and driven towards academic and career achievement.",""],[1,"206","1","Youth Monetary Incentives and Overseas Study and Internship Programme","including providing monetary incentives as well as overseas study and internship programmes.",""],[1,"206","2","National Youth Skills Institute Expansion","The National Youth Skills Institute (IKBN), which offers skills courses that have high market demand, will be expanded to provide greater options for youth in various fields of study.",""],[1,"206","2","Youth Soft Skills Training Programme","IKBN will also provide soft skills training such as leadership courses to its students.",""],[1,"206","2","Youth Sports Exposure and Training Initiative","Greater exposure to capital-intensive sports such as golf and motorsports, will be provided through courses by IKBN with the objective of enhancing youth participation in potentially lucrative sports sectors.",""],[1,"206","2","Youth Entrepreneurship Training and Awareness Expansion","Entrepreneurship training and awareness programmes will be expanded through various institutions including the Malaysia Youth",""],[1,"206","3","Youth Leadership Internship Programme","Leadership skills, particularly among youth leaders, will be strengthened through internship programmes at government departments, companies and NGOs for up to one year.",""]],"80":[[1,"205","5","Cabinet Committee on Youth Development","a Cabinet Committee on Youth Development chaired by the Deputy Prime Minister has been established.",""],[1,"205","6","Youth Patriotism and Volunteerism Promotion","The Government will nurture positive attitudes towards patriotism and volunteerism to produce youth that love the nation and appreciate the spirit of solidarity amongst all Malaysians - in line with the 1Malaysia concept.",""],[1,"205","6","Merit-Based Youth Competitiveness Programme","Programmes for youth will be focused to establish a competitive culture based on merit and ability.",""],[1,"206","1","National Youth Award Recognition Scheme","The National Youth Award will continue to be used to recognise outstanding youth achievements in various categories including leadership and volunteerism.",""],[1,"206","1","Youth International Conference and Forum Participation Programme","youths that have outstanding leadership qualities and active participation in societies will be given the opportunity to attend various international conferences and forums such as the Global Model UN Programme where they will be able to interact with youths from other countries on a wide range of global issues.",""],[1,"206","4","RELA Youth Squad Expansion","The RELA Youth Squad will be expanded to encourage greater sense of volunteerism and discipline.",""],[1,"206","4","Inclusive Youth Participation Activities","To promote greater unity among youths, activities will be tailored to ensure more inclusive participation such as sports competitions.",""],[1,"206","4","Youth Association Capacity Building Programme","The Government will also strengthen and develop youth associations through leadership and management courses to ensure the associations are financially independent.",""],[1,"206","4","Youth Associations Registration Transfer and Monitoring Reform","The migration of youth associations registration from Registrar of Societies to Registrar of Youth Societies under the Ministry of Youth and Sports will ensure a more effective delivery and monitoring of youth related development programmes.","Ministry of Youth and Sports"]],"81":[[1,"202","4","Women’s Empowerment Initiative","the Government will increase its efforts towards addressing issues confronting women to enable them to realise their full potential and participate more effectively in the economic",""],[1,"203","6","Flexible Working Arrangements Promotion","Flexible working hours and work from home policies in the public and private sectors will continue to be promoted to encourage a more family-friendly workplace.",""],[1,"203","7","Women Entrepreneurship Promotion Initiative","Efforts will be made to improve women's participation in entrepreneurial activities through greater collaboration between the Department of Women Development and institutions such as AIM to achieve the target of creating 4,000 women entrepreneurs by 2012.","Department of Women Development"],[1,"204","3","Skills Development Programme for Single Mothers","Skills development programmes for single mothers will be expanded and strengthened such as the Intensive Skill Training for Single Mother (I-KIT) entrepreneurship and skills programme.",""],[1,"204","3","Special Assistance Schemes for Women in Challenging Circumstances","Other special assistance schemes will also encourage women in challenging circumstances to undertake more entrepreneurial activities.",""],[1,"204","3","Cottage Industry Skills Training Programme","In addition, skills training programmes in cottage industries such as beading and tailoring",""],[1,"204","4","Women’s Entrepreneurship Programmes for Bottom 40% Households and Minority Communities","will be expanded through the Jejari Bestari and Inkubator Keusahawanan Wanita (I-KeuNITA) entrepreneurship programmes for women in bottom 40% households, Orang Asli communities and ethnic minorities in Sabah and Sarawak.",""]],"82":[[1,"43","6","Public Transport Expansion and Connectivity Improvement","Major investments in public transport include the expansion of the Kuala Lumpur Light Rail Transit (LRT) coverage and the implementation of a high capacity mass rapid transit system.",""],[1,"43","6","Feeder Bus and Covered Walkway Network Expansion","the network of feeder buses and covered walkways will be extended to provide end to end connectivity for commuters and pedestrians;",""],[1,"72","1","SPAD Regulatory Oversight and Service Standards Enforcement","SPAD will be involved in regulatory oversight as well as enforcement of service standards across all modes of land-based public transport.",""]],"83":[[1,"254","3","Managed Reduction of Unskilled Foreign Labour","The dependence on unskilled foreign labour will be gradually reduced.",""],[1,"254","3","Needs-Based Foreign Labour Admission for Shortage Sectors","sectors where labour shortages persists, such as construction and plantation, will be allowed to employ foreign labour based on needs.",""],[1,"254","3","Foreign Worker Welfare and Housing Standards","Measures will be put in place to ensure employers improve the working conditions and welfare of these workers, including providing better housing and basic amenities.",""],[1,"254","4","Multi-tiered Levy System for Unskilled Worker Employers","A new multi-tiered levy system will be implemented for employers of unskilled workers to encourage the move towards a highly-skilled workforce.",""],[1,"254","5","New Levy System for Unskilled Foreign Labour","Under the new levy system to regulate the entry of unskilled foreign labour, the levies will be borne by employers and not by employees.",""]],"84":[[1,"360","1","Fiscal Deficit Reduction and Public Sector Productivity Improvement","Additionally, the Government is also committed to reducing its fiscal deficit from 7.0% of GDP in 2009 to below 3.0% of GDP by 2015 and reducing total Federal Government debt from 53.3% in 2009 to 49.9% of GDP at the end of the Plan period.",""],[1,"360","1","Public Sector Productivity Improvement","Consequently, the Government will significantly improve productivity to deliver better outcomes without increasing allocations,",""],[1,"360","3","Best Practices Strengthening Initiative","The adoption, adaptation and application of best practices will continue to be strengthened.",""]],"86":[[1,"43","2","Urban Liveability Enhancement Policy","Therefore, a policy priority in the Tenth Plan will be to enhance the liveability of cities.",""],[1,"44","1","Urban Heritage Restoration and Redevelopment Initiative","Urban rejuvenation efforts to restore and protect heritage buildings and to unlock the development value of land such as the Kampung Bharu urban redevelopment effort in Kuala Lumpur.",""],[1,"44","1","En-Bloc Redevelopment Mechanism for Collectively Owned Property","the Government proposes to introduce en-bloc mechanism to facilitate redevelopment of collectively-owned property and land.",""],[1,"44","2","City Liveability and Connectivity Improvement Initiatives","specific strategies will be implemented for other city conurbations, such as Georgetown, Johor Bahru, Kuching and Kota Kinabalu, particularly in terms of liveability, connectivity and further strengthening localised industrial clusters according to their respective strengths",""],[1,"44","2","Public Transportation Enhancement and Waterfront Development","Major liveability initiatives include enhancing public transportation and also developments to strengthen the waterfront identity of these cities",""],[1,"277","3","Urban Renewal and Brownfield Redevelopment Programme","urban renewal and redevelopment of brownfield sites will be pursued.",""],[1,"280","3","River and Waterfront Restoration Priority","the restoration of rivers and waterfronts in Malaysian cities will be a priority.",""]],"87":[[1,"195","3","Kampong Bharu Rejuvenation and Development Corporation","The Government will establish the Perbadanan Pembangunan Kampong Bharu or Kampong Bharu Development Corporation that will work with the residents of Kampong Bharu to develop a business model whereby the gains from land re-development will be equitably shared, identify a mutually acceptable temporary re-settlement area and develop innovative funding schemes that would enable existing residents to purchase units in the re-developed areas.",""]],"88":[[1,"260","4","Urban Livability and Vibrancy Improvement Initiatives","the Government will undertake concerted efforts to make other major cities, such as Georgetown, Johor Bahru, Kuching and Kota Kinabalu more liveable and vibrant.",""],[1,"274","5","Urban Livability and Vibrant Cities Approach","A new approach to building vibrant and liveable cities will be adopted to address these challenges, as shown in Table 6-1.",""],[1,"275","21","Local Authority Collaboration for Frontline Input in Planning","Greater collaboration and cooperation with local authorities to incorporate frontline input into planning and decision making",""],[1,"280","1","Urban Open Space Strategy Integration","Local Plans will incorporate open space strategies that move beyond just allocating land for open space activities, to understanding how cities can enhance and attract people to these public spaces.",""],[1,"280","1","Interconnected Urban Green Space Network","the Government will support local authorities in creating a seamless network of interconnected green spaces within the cities, connecting major activity hubs and housing sites, and be equipped with facilities such as amphitheatres, cycling and pedestrian pathways and other amenities.",""],[1,"280","1","Corporate Social Responsibility Support for Green Spaces","Companies will be encouraged to provide support in the establishment and maintenance of green spaces as part of their corporate social responsibility programmes.",""],[1,"280","2","Lake Gardens Botanical Garden Development","In Greater KL, the 101-hectare Lake Gardens will be developed into a Botanical Garden with a wide variety of unique trees and flowers, nature trails and themed mini-gardens.",""],[1,"280","2","Lake Gardens Access and Public Transport Improvement","In order to enable easy access to the garden, pedestrian walkways connecting the Lake Gardens and the city centre will be built along with improved public transport services.",""],[1,"280","2","Lake Gardens Activity and Performance Facilities","Within the garden, activity centres such as open plazas and cafes will be introduced.",""],[1,"280","2","Lake Gardens Cultural Performance Programme","A range of cultural and contemporary performances will be encouraged to premiere at the amphitheatre facility within the garden.",""],[1,"282","3","Leisure and Sporting Activities Promotion","a wide range of leisure and sporting activities will be encouraged to create a vibrant, exciting environment in which to work in the day and play in the evenings and on weekends.",""],[1,"282","3","Little India Urban Rejuvenation Initiative","The rejuvenation of places with distinctive identities, such as Little India in Greater KL will capitalise on the strengths of Malaysia's ethnic diversity and unique cultural heritage.",""]],"90":[[1,"270","3","Rakyat-Centric Public Transport System Development","Developing a rakyat-centric public transport system.",""],[1,"285","2","Urban Public Transport Improvement NKRA","Improving urban public transport was chosen as one of six National Key Result Areas (NKRAs), which are national priority areas of focus identified under the Government Transformation Programme (GTP), as shown in Box 6-1.",""],[1,"285","2","Urban Public Transport NKRA Funding Allocation","An allocation of approximately RM2.8 billion has been made for the NKRA initiative to be completed in the first two years of the Plan period.",""],[1,"285","4","High-Capacity Rail and Bus Rapid Transit Investment","Increasing the capacity of the system to cater for latent and future growth by investing in high-capacity rail and innovative bus rapid transit systems;",""],[1,"286","4","Integrated Transport Terminal Development","Completion of Integrate Transport Terminal (ITT) in Bandar Tasik Selatan and constructionof ITT Gombak by 2012 to alleviate congestion caused by intercity buses congregating in Kuala Lumpur's city centre.",""],[1,"286","9","Transport Capacity Investment Expansion","Increasing investments in transport capacity to keep pace with urban growth;",""],[1,"286","12","Public Transport Improvement Delivery Authority","With the establishment of SPAD, there is now a single point of accountability to deliver improvements in public transport",""],[1,"288","3","Bus Rapid Transit and Cashless Ticketing System","Introducing innovative initiatives, such as the Bus Rapid Transit (BRT) System and a single cashless ticketing system across various operators;",""],[1,"288","7","Public Transport Capacity Expansion","Investments in public transport will focus on enhancing the efficiency of existing systems that already operate at their limits of capacity as well provide capacity to accommodate future growth.",""],[1,"288","8","Light Rail Transit Capacity Expansion","In Greater KL, a major initiative to improve the capacity of the Light Rail Transit (LRT) lines is the 34-km extension of the existing lines.",""],[1,"288","8","Kelana Jaya LRT Rolling Stock Expansion","the full delivery of the 35 sets of new four-car trains will increase the capacity of the Kelana Jaya LRT line from approximately 24,000 to 98,000 passengers per hour",""],[1,"289","8","Monorail System Extension Study","a potential extension of the monorail system will be considered.",""],[1,"289","8","KTM Komuter Fleet Expansion","The capacity of the KTM Komuter system will be augmented with the purchase of 38 new six-car Electric Multiple Units (EMUs) to be delivered by 2012",""],[1,"289","8","Greater KL Bus Rapid Transit System","a 49-km Greater KL BRT System consisting of three major corridors will be implemented.",""],[1,"289","9","Greater Kuala Lumpur Mass Rapid Transit System","a high-capacity mass rapid transit system will be implemented to meet future demand of thousands of commuters moving in and out of the city daily.",""],[1,"289","10","Bus Rapid Transit System for Iskandar Region Growth Centres","Outside Greater KL, a BRT system will be considered for implementation to connect new urban growth centres in the Iskandar Region",""],[1,"290","1","RapidPenang Bus Service Expansion","RapidPenang, will continue to expand the frequency and coverage of its bus services.",""],[1,"290","2","Small-Scale Public Transport Capacity Expansion for Medium-Sized Cities","the Government will consider the implementation of smaller-scale approaches to increase the capacity of public transport for medium sized cities",""],[1,"290","2","Bus Route Optimization and Dedicated Bus Lanes","efforts will be made to optimise bus routes to minimise travel time and introduce dedicated bus lanes in city centres with high demand",""],[1,"290","2","River Transportation Enhancement and Water Taxi Tourism Promotion","The Government will also further enhance river transportation as a mode of public transport, particularly in Sarawak",""],[1,"433","6","Urban Public Transport Expansion","Increase urban public transport",""],[1,"433","9","Komuter Rail Service Extension to Tanjung Malim","Extension of Komuter rail service to Tanjung Malim, Perak",""],[1,"433","11","LRT Train Procurement","Procurement of 35 sets of 4-car trains for LRT service",""],[1,"433","12","Integrated Transport Terminal Construction","Construction of the Integrated Transport Terminal in Bandar Tasik Selatan",""]],"91":[[1,"118","7","SME Financing Access Enhancement","Enhancing access to financing for SMEs.",""],[1,"121","4","SME Financing Access Programmes","In order to enhance access to financing to such SMEs, the following programmes will be put in place:",""],[1,"121","6","Special Financing Schemes for SMEs in New Growth Areas","Special financing schemes by development financial institutions and other participating institutions will be provided to SMEs in new growth areas;",""],[1,"121","7","Preferential SME Loan and Hybrid Grant Financing Scheme","financial support will be provided to SMEs in the form of preferential rate loans or hybrid grant loans.",""],[1,"122","1","Working Capital Guarantee Scheme Reintroduction","The WCGS will be reintroduced.",""],[1,"122","2","Financial Help Desks at Trade Associations and Chambers of Commerce","Financial advisory services will be enhanced with the setting up of financial help desks at trade associations and chambers of commerce, which will be promoted via road shows to enhance awareness;",""]],"92":[[1,"165","4","Institutional Ownership for Bumiputera Equity and Property","Therefore, under the new approach highlighted in Table 4-1, there will be increased emphasis on instruments such as institutional ownership over corporate equity and property, which enables pooling and mobilising of funds and distribution of profits to a larger group of",""],[1,"166","2","Bumiputera Corporate Equity Acquisition and Capital Mobilization","Pooling and mobilising Bumiputera capital to acquire corporate equity (mainly Malaysian listed companies) and sharing the gains",""],[1,"166","3","Expansion of Bumiputera Property Investment Trust","Expansion of this successful concept to other types of wealth, e.g. property investment via Yayasan Amanah Hartanah Bumiputera",""],[1,"166","5","Bumiputera Equity Allocation Requirement","Requiring companies to allocate 30% equity to Bumiputera",""],[1,"189","2","Wealth Ownership Expansion through Institutional Investment","Increasing wealth ownership beyond corporate equity to include other properties and business assets such as retail space landed properties, commercial buildings, intellectual properties and other services through pooling of funds and institutional investment;",""],[1,"194","3","Bumiputera Real Estate Investment Trusts","Yayasan Amanah Hartanah Bumiputera (YAHB) will set up Real Estate Investment Trusts (REITs) to reduce the entry barrier for Bumiputera to invest in commercial and industrial properties",""],[1,"195","1","Institutional Investment Capacity Strengthening and Asset Development Initiative","Initiatives will also be undertaken to strengthen the investment capability of institutions such as Baitulmal and to increase the value of their assets including land development for commercial purposes.",""],[1,"195","2","Bumiputera Asset Value Unlocking Initiative","More concerted efforts will be undertaken to unlock value from Bumiputera assets such as land.",""]],"93":[[1,"167","4","BCIC Segmentation Approach for Bumiputera Companies","Development of new approach of BCIC by segmenting Bumiputera companies by their business stages",""],[1,"167","9","Strengthening Bumiputera Development Institutions","Bumiputera-specific institutions such as Majlis Amanah Rakyat (MARA) will enhance their roles in supporting the Bumiputera development agenda",""],[1,"188","1","Bumiputera Economic Participation Agenda","the overall Bumiputera development agenda will continue to be a major thrust of Malaysia's economic policy.",""],[1,"188","2","Bumiputera Economic Participation Support Programmes","Since the Second Malaysia Plan period, the Government has continuously provided programmes to enhance Bumiputera participation in the economy.",""],[1,"188","5","Market-Friendly Bumiputera Economic Participation Instruments","This will be achieved through more transparent, market-friendly and merit-based instruments, focused on:",""],[1,"189","4","Bumiputera Commercial and Industrial Community Segmentation Approach","a new approach to the development of a Bumiputera Commercial and Industrial Community (BCIC) will be undertaken through segmenting the Bumiputera companies by their business stage.",""],[1,"190","4","Segmented Policy Instruments for Business Stages","Policy instruments will be segmented to better meet requirements at the different business stages",""]],"94":[[1,"44","5","Rural Development and Basic Infrastructure Upgrade","under the Tenth Plan, the Government will continue to emphasise rural development particularly in the context of improving access to education and utilities, connectivity and upgrading rural economic activities.",""],[1,"46","4","Major New Rural Road Infrastructure Construction","major new rural road infrastructure will be built, particularly in Sabah and Sarawak.",""]],"96":[[1,"21","11","Safe City Crime Prevention Initiatives","Safe City initiatives will promote crime prevention",""]],"97":[[1,"225","3","Basic School Infrastructure and Amenities Delivery","the Government is committed towards delivering these basic infrastructure and amenities to all schools.",""],[1,"225","4","School Infrastructure and Facilities Improvement Programme","the Government will continue to focus investments in infrastructure and facilities in schools across Malaysia that need support the most, especially for schools in rural areas in the states of Sabah and Sarawak.",""],[1,"225","5","High Performing Schools Programme","HPS strive to raise the standards of schools to be comparable with the best schools globally and be models as well as provide support via coaching and mentoring networks to other schools.",""]],"98":[[1,"20","21","Greater Kuala Lumpur Mass Rapid Transit System","The mass rapid transit system will be a landmark project for Greater KL",""]],"99":[[1,"152","2","MSC Malaysia Niche Sector Development and MNC Anchor Strategy","MSC Malaysia will identify and support the development of niche areas in software and e-solutions, creative multimedia, shared services and outsourcing as well as e-business.",""],[1,"152","3","ICT Adoption Promotion Across Industries","The Government will aggressively promote the use of ICT in all industries in parallel with the development of the ICT sector.",""],[1,"152","3","Cloud Computing Services for SMEs","Cloud computing services will be developed to provide SMEs with critical software applications for customer relations management, enterprise resource planning, supply-chain management, human resource management, and financial and accounting management.",""],[1,"152","3","Niche ICT Applications Development in Priority Sectors","Niche areas for applications development include healthcare, education and financial services especially in Islamic banking;",""],[1,"152","4","National Creative Industry Policy","A National Creative Industry Policy will be formulated",""],[1,"152","4","National Digital Terrestrial Television Broadcasting Roll-out","the National Digital Terrestrial Television Broadcasting (DTTB) project will be rolled-out to help spur the expansion of related creative industries",""],[1,"154","5","Knowledge SME Incubators and Shared Services Centres","Strengthening incubators and shared services centres for knowledge SMEs;",""]],"100":[[1,"163","5","Capacity and Capability Building for Inclusive Economic Participation","This involves stepping up capacity and capability building, enhancing access to employment opportunities and adopting a more targeted approach in encouraging innovation-driven entrepreneurship;",""],[1,"163","5","Targeted Innovation-Driven Entrepreneurship Support","This involves stepping up capacity and capability building, enhancing access to employment opportunities and adopting a more targeted approach in encouraging innovation-driven entrepreneurship;",""],[1,"163","6","Social Safety Net for Disadvantaged Groups","Providing a social safety net for disadvantaged groups.",""],[1,"164","1","Focused Support for Bottom 40% Households","This will involve providing focused support towards encouraging greater participation from specific groups that are most in need, especially the bottom 40% household income group (herein referred to as bottom 40% households).",""],[1,"164","8","Bottom 40% Household Inclusiveness Programme","Inclusiveness programmes will focus on the bottom 40% households",""],[1,"172","1","Bottom 40 Percent Household Income Support","Therefore, focus will now be re-oriented to elevate the income levels of the bottom 40% households.",""],[1,"174","8","Bottom 40% Household Livelihood Improvement Strategy","During the Plan period, a three-pronged strategy will be adopted to improve the livelihoods of the bottom 40% households as show in chart 4-5.",""],[1,"176","1","Low-Income Households Poverty Reduction Programme","The Low Income Households NKRA aims to completely eradicate hardcore poverty, reduce the incidence of poverty and enhance the productivity of low-income households through:",""],[1,"185","2","Additional Targeted Poverty Reduction Programmes for Bottom 40% Households","they will also benefit from additional targeted programmes to strengthen their capabilities and reduce incidence of poverty among them.",""],[1,"211","1","Bottom 40% Livelihoods and Vulnerable Household Support Programmes","Programmes to elevate the livelihoods of the bottom 40% households and safeguard the vulnerable will be emphasised.",""],[1,"211","1","Skills Upgrading and Employment Linkage Initiative","This will be done by elevating their income-earning ability through upgrading skills, linking them with potential employers and increasing capacity for entrepreneurship.",""],[1,"211","1","Social Safety Net Strengthening","At the same time, the social safety net will be strengthened to protect the vulnerable.",""],[1,"211","1","Balanced Economic Participation and Bumiputera Equity Allocation Instruments","In addition, balanced economic participation will continue to be pursued.",""],[1,"211","2","Inclusive Economic Participation and Capability-Building Programmes","Moving forward, focus will be given towards achieving balanced participation in higher paying jobs, strengthening entrepreneurship in higher- value added activities and enabling accumulation of wealth across a broader categorisation of assets.",""],[1,"211","2","Market-Friendly Inclusive Programme Design Principles","Principles of market-friendly, needs based, merit-based and transparent will be applied in the design and implementation of programmes to ensure inclusiveness is consistent with growth.",""]],"101":[[1,"217","1","Integrated Human Capital and Talent Development Framework","the Government will adopt an integrated human capital and talent development framework",""],[1,"217","2","Education System Revamp","Revamping the education system to significantly raise student outcomes;",""],[1,"219","2","International Student Assessment Benchmarking","Going forward, Malaysian student performances will continue to be benchmarked against international standards and assessments.",""],[1,"219","3","Comprehensive Education System Review and Assessment","the Ministry of Education (MOE) will also undertake a comprehensive review and assessment of the current status of the education system focusing on implementation and delivery capabilities.","Ministry of Education (MOE)"],[1,"219","4","School Sports and Co-curricular Participation Enhancement","During the Plan period, to further reinforce this philosophy, emphasis will be placed on the participation in sports and co-curricular activities in schools to contribute towards character- building of students.",""],[1,"219","4","Values and Ethics Education Reinforcement","The education system will reinforce the importance of values and ethics as these represent critical building blocks on the journey to Vision 2020.",""],[1,"219","4","ICT Integration in Schools","The use of information and communications technology (ICT) in schools will be given greater emphasis to nurture creativity and innovation among students, in order to equip them with new skills and capabilities to meet the demands of a high-income economy.",""],[1,"220","6","Education NKRA Student Outcomes Improvement Programme","The education NKRAs is targeted at improving student outcomes and is anchored upon four areas: Pre-school enrolment rates, High Performing Schools, Literacy and Numeracy Screening (LINUS) programme, and a New Deal for Head Teachers and Principals.",""],[1,"220","9","Student Support and Remedial Assistance Programme","Set the same high expectations for all students regardless of background and provide systematic help and support to students who fall behind;",""],[1,"224","6","Education System Revamp Based on Student Outcomes","Moving forward, efforts to revamp the educational system will be explicitly anchored on student outcomes and on holding schools accountable for those outcomes.",""],[1,"265","4","School Improvement Programme","the school improvement programme and LINUS initiative will aim to close the achievement gap for disadvantaged students and low performing schools to ensure every student in Malaysia can succeed.",""],[1,"265","4","LINUS Initiative","the school improvement programme and LINUS initiative will aim to close the achievement gap for disadvantaged students and low performing schools to ensure every student in Malaysia can succeed.",""]],"102":[[1,"221","4","Expansion of Early Childhood Education Adoption","the Government will increase the focus on improving and expanding adoption of early childhood education to provide more children in Malaysia with a better head-start.",""],[1,"221","5","PERMATA Early Childhood Development Programme Expansion","The early childhood development programme for children aged four and below (PERMATA), aimed at nurturing and producing the country's future 'gems', will come under the purview of the MOE by 2011 to improve co-ordination and integration with the formal education system.","MOE"],[1,"222","1","Pre-School Education Expansion and Quality Improvement Programme","pre-school education is designated a focus area under the Education NKRA.",""],[1,"222","2","Early Childhood Development and Pre-School Programme Rollout","With the implementation of the early childhood development and pre-school programme, more children will be ready to enter school at a younger age than is currently practised.",""],[1,"234","5","Public Pre-school Harmonisation and Quality Improvement","the Government will continue to harmonise and improve the quality of all public pre-schools provided by the different Government agencies.",""],[1,"234","5","Pre-school Delivery Capability Enhancement","This will require productivity improvements in human and financial capacity, as well as to significantly enhance delivery capabilities.",""],[1,"236","2","Private Pre-School Expansion Incentive Scheme","The Government will leverage upon private sector provision of pre-school education.",""],[1,"236","3","Pre-School Co-Payment and Fee Assistance Scheme","A co-payment scheme to increase demand for pre-school education will be implemented during the Plan period.",""]],"103":[[1,"252","1","Labour Market Reform for Talent Attraction and Retention","Efforts to reform the labour market are necessary to ensure efficient matching of demand with supply, and to improve the retention of top talent and to enhance the attractiveness of Malaysia to local and foreign talent as well as the Malaysian diaspora.",""],[1,"252","3","Labour Market Reform for Job Mobility and Upskilling","During the Plan period, the Government is committed to undertake a reform of the labour market, with special emphasis on improving job mobility and upskilling the current workforce, in particular those from the bottom 40% of households.",""],[1,"252","5","Workforce Skills and Capability Upgrading","Upgrading the skills and capabilities of Malaysia's existing workforce;",""],[1,"252","8","Labour Legislation Review for Knowledge Economy Needs","During the Plan period, efforts will be undertaken to review provisions of labour legislation in line with the needs of a knowledge economy and the",""],[1,"253","2","Labour Legislation Review for Faster Dispute Settlement","Therefore, a review of labour legislation will be conducted, towards ensuring that Malaysia adopts an optimal balance between labour market flexibility and job stability and which provides for efficient and speedy settlement of labour disputes.",""],[1,"253","6","Public Employment Services Modernization Programme","The Government will enhance and modernise public employment services by upgrading existing public job centres to improve the delivery of career advice across different industries, provide industry-driven matching and placement services and conduct continuous community outreach or education programmes on employment trends and career opportunities.",""],[1,"254","1","Public-Private Employment Clearing House","The goal is to create an effective and efficient public clearing house operated jointly by the public and private sectors.",""]],"104":[[1,"254","6","Part-Time Work Regulations under the Employment Act 1955","The Government will introduce Part-Time Work Regulations under the Employment Act 1955.",""],[1,"255","1","Female Labour Force Participation Increase Measures","measures will be undertaken to increase the female labour force participation rate from 46% in 2010 to 55% in 2015.",""],[1,"255","2","Flexible and Part-Time Work Policy for Older Workers","Adoption of flexible and part-time working practices and policies will encourage post- retiring age Malaysians to continue contributing to the economy, particularly in sectors and occupations where their specific expertise is needed.",""]],"105":[[1,"301","9","Public Housing Agency Rationalisation and Streamlining","the Government will rationalise and streamline the role of federal agencies involved in public housing.",""],[1,"302","1","Housing Provision Rationalisation","Moving forward, the Government will rationalise housing provision with only one federal agency responsible for the provision of federally funded housing, with the private sector being expected to play a greater role in these efforts.",""],[1,"302","3","Housing Quality Law Review and Provider Accreditation","existing laws, including the Uniform Building By-Laws 1984, will be reviewed to incorporate minimum specifications of housing quality, particularly on ensuring quality in the provision of affordable housing developments.",""],[1,"302","3","Housing Provider Accreditation Scheme","The Government, through the Construction Industry Development Board, will encourage housing providers to be accredited, particularly for the usage of skilled and qualified labour and improved construction processes.",""],[1,"303","3","En-Bloc Sale Mechanism for Urban Rejuvenation","The Government will implement a mechanism to ease the sale of collectively-owned developments.",""],[1,"303","4","Monitoring and Enforcement Strengthening","Strengthening monitoring and enforcement.",""],[1,"303","6","Build-Then-Sell Housing Development Incentive Scheme","Housing developers will be encouraged to adopt the BTS approach through the provision of additional incentives such as shortening the approval processes for land and building plans and exemption of deposit payments for licensing housing developments;",""],[1,"303","7","Rehabilitation of Abandoned Housing Projects","The Government will continue to provide assistance towards the rehabilitation of abandoned housing projects.",""]],"106":[[1,"363","4","High-Performance Monitoring Units","Establishing high performance monitoring units;",""],[1,"365","2","Monitoring and Delivery Units for Outcome Management","other monitoring and delivery units to manage the delivery of specific outcomes include the Project Management Unit (PMU), Performance Management and Delivery Unit (PEMANDU) and the new Economic Delivery Unit (EDU).",""],[1,"365","7","Project Monitoring System II Shared Data and Reporting System","Leverage Project Monitoring System II (SPP II) as a common data and reporting system.",""],[1,"366","1","Performance-Oriented Delivery Monitoring Units","Performance-oriented units monitor and track the delivery of priority areas",""],[1,"366","15","EDU Monitoring and Delivery Support for National Key Economic Areas","EDU to monitor and assist in the delivery of National Key Economic Areas (NKEAs)",""],[1,"366","16","Stimulus Package and Budget 2010 Fund Disbursement Oversight","It oversees, manages and monitors the disbursement of funds and work carried out under the stimulus package and the Budget 2010",""],[1,"370","3","Outcome-Based Planning and Resource Allocation Framework","An outcome-based approach will be adopted for planning, resource allocation, monitoring and",""],[1,"370","4","Outcome-Based KPI Monitoring System","To ensure accountability, KPIs to measure outcomes will be attributed to individuals and their KPIs will be regularly monitored.",""],[1,"435","4","Outcome-Based Planning, Monitoring and Evaluation System","Implementing outcome-based planning, monitoring and evaluation",""]],"107":[[1,"362","1","ICT Architecture Streamlining Initiative","Further streamlining ICT architecture.",""],[1,"362","2","ICT Operations Simplification and Consolidation","Simplifying and consolidating ICT operations.",""],[1,"362","3","ICT Project Cost-Benefit Assessment","Implementing cost-benefit assessment to obtain more value from ICT projects.",""],[1,"434","3","eKL Online Government Services Portal","eKL initiative as an online-based portal for the Klang Valley that provides interface for services such as electronic payment, online submission, online news and job application",""],[1,"434","3","Complaints Management System Improvement","iSPAAA, a complaints management system, provides faster resolution of complaints to less than two months",""],[1,"434","3","MyGovernment Single-Window Services Portal","MyGovernment Portal set up as a single services and information gateway - provides 1,274 online services and 3,094 downloadable forms",""],[1,"434","3","MySMS Government Services Mobile Platform","MySMS 15888 set up as a mobile platform for government services with 121 participating agencies and 1,620 services being offered",""],[1,"434","3","Government Secure Network Infrastructure","EG-Net and Putrajaya Campus Network (PCN) secured network infrastructure for electronic communication and transaction",""],[1,"434","3","One-Stop Centre Approval Streamlining","More application processes with shorter approval time from 367 days to 120 days through the setting up of One-Stop Centres (OSC)",""],[1,"434","3","Online Property Registration Process Improvement","Reducing the time taken for property registration through improvement of processes and enabling online applications for property registration",""],[1,"434","3","Business Start-Up Simplification Reform","Reducing the procedures and time taken to start a business to 3 procedures and 3 days with the introduction of a standard company identification number or MyCoID",""],[1,"435","3","E-Payment Channel Expansion","Growth in e-payment channels such as the Financial Process Exchange (FPX)",""],[1,"435","3","Tax Collection and E-Filing Refund Improvement","Improvements in tax collection mechanisms with tax refunds made within 14 to 30 days when returns are filed through e-filing",""],[1,"435","3","OSC Online Development Order Processing System","Establishment of OSC online to process development orders more efficiently",""]],"109":[[1,"4","2","Urban Cluster Development Programme","Specific cities and urban clusters will be developed into vibrant, productive and liveable cities comparable to other major cities in the world.",""]],"110":[[1,"38","5","Top Talent Attraction and Development Initiative","These include driving productivity and innovation, nurturing and attracting top talent and developing clusters with agglomeration economies.",""],[1,"39","3","Workforce Upskilling for Value Chain Upgrading","Focusing on skills development, especially in terms of upskilling the existing work force to facilitate industries to move up the value chain;",""],[1,"40","6","Talent Corporation for Top Talent Attraction and Retention","Specifically, a Talent Corporation will be formed with the primary mandate to secure the top talent required to drive key economic sectors for the nation.",""],[1,"40","6","Facilitative Immigration Policy for Knowledge Workers","To support this, a more facilitative approach to immigration will be implemented for knowledge workers.",""],[1,"88","6","Talent Development, Attraction and Retention Strategy","Central to this will be strategies to develop, attract and retain quality talent base;",""],[1,"127","6","Talent Recruitment Investment","Investing in talent recruitment.",""],[1,"129","5","Talent Corporation Establishment","Malaysia will introduce several initiatives including establishment of the Talent Corporation (TC).","Prime Minister's Department"],[1,"129","6","National Talent Management Initiatives","TC will have three key roles: as a catalyst to lead and drive innovative national talent management initiatives; as a facilitator for private sector efforts in attracting, creating and motivating a world class workforce; and to deliver major national initiatives on talent across the human capital development pipeline.",""],[1,"129","6","Diaspora Talent Mobilization and Foreign Talent Attraction Measures","This will include leveraging the diaspora of Malaysians abroad, simplifying the path for foreign talent to work in Malaysia, ensuring better working conditions and providing the appropriate incentive packages.",""],[1,"129","6","National Talent Blueprint Formulation","The National Talent Blueprint will also be formulated by 2011 to identify the talent needs focused on the NKEAs and develop the specific initiatives to accelerate the pipeline for the talent required.",""]],"111":[[1,"39","9","Bankruptcy Law Review","A review of bankruptcy law will be undertaken on the premise that innovation requires an environment that accepts failure, promotes a diversity of views and gives entrepreneurs a second chance.",""],[1,"39","9","Regulatory Flexibility for Micro Enterprises","To promote innovation through knowledge-based small enterprises, regulatory flexibility will be accorded for companies with five or less employees.",""],[1,"79","4","Business Environment Liberalisation Measures","improvements in the business environment for private investment will be given priority, including measures to further liberalise the economy.",""],[1,"80","1","Statutory and Regulatory Review for Entrepreneurship Promotion","Statutory and regulatory reviews will be undertaken to promote entrepreneurship and improve risk-taking profiles of the private sector.",""],[1,"92","3","Business Regulation Modernization and Competition Reform","Creating a private sector-led economy by modernising business regulation, liberalising the services sector, removing market distortions, introducing competition legislation and improving the interface between government and business;",""],[1,"105","2","Insolvency Law Simplification and Bankruptcy Law Review","The insolvency law pertaining to companies and individuals will be simplified to support a culture of taking calculated risk, eliminate the stigma of failure and allow those who failed in the first instance to continue being economically active.",""],[1,"105","2","Malaysian Department of Insolvency Corporatisation","the Malaysian Department of Insolvency will be corporatised by 2015.",""],[1,"119","1","Small Business Regulatory Exemption and Easing Measure","During the Plan period, in order to encourage entrepreneurial activity, the Government will exempt some of the more costly business regulations for companies employing five or fewer people until the company expands beyond five employees.",""]],"112":[[1,"40","3","Skills Training and TVET Mainstreaming","Skills training will be given special emphasis under the Tenth Plan to ensure that Malaysia develops the necessary human capital to meet industry's requirements and drive productivity improvements to move up the value chain.",""],[1,"40","4","Vocational Dual Training and Graduate Internship Expansion","The Government will also expand programmes involving practical on-the-job training through the vocational dual training system and also through graduate internship programmes.",""],[1,"69","3","Lifelong Learning and SME Skills Retraining Programme","provision of lifelong learning programmes in which employees, particularly in the small and medium enterprises (SMEs), were trained and retrained to improve their skills.",""],[1,"70","4","Lifelong Learning Expansion Programme","Lifelong learning programmes were enhanced through the expansion of distance learning, e-learning, retraining and skills-upgrading offered by various institutions.",""],[1,"70","4","Community College Retraining and Skills-Upgrading Programme","At the local level, community colleges assumed a greater role in implementing retraining and skills-upgrading programmes, benefiting a total of 507,940 participants.",""]],"113":[[1,"43","5","International Financial District Development","Major new developments will be undertaken including an International Financial District in Kuala Lumpur",""],[1,"43","5","Sungai Besi Airport Redevelopment","redevelopment of the Sungai Besi airport",""],[1,"43","5","Sungai Buloh Township Development","township development in Sungai Buloh",""],[1,"43","5","World-Class Integrated Convention Facilities Development","establishing a world class integrated convention facilities at Jalan Duta and a Malaysia Truly Asia Centre",""],[1,"45","3","International Financial District Development","the establishment of the International Financial District in Kuala Lumpur will help establish a critical mass of finance professionals and a concentration of financial institutions, including international Islamic financial institutions",""]],"114":[[1,"45","4","Road Infrastructure Connectivity Improvement","The policy challenge is to help firms and workers overcome physical distance to successful areas through improving connectivity, such as through improving road infrastructure.",""],[1,"45","4","East Coast Highway Connectivity Project","the East Coast Highway will help enhance the connectivity of east coast states to the Klang Valley;",""],[1,"46","1","Iskandar Malaysia Connectivity Enhancement Initiative","the development of Iskandar Malaysia will be further facilitated through initiatives to enhance connectivity to Singapore.",""]],"115":[[1,"47","7","New Wave of Privatisations","The Government proposes to undertake a new wave of privatisations during the Plan period.",""],[1,"47","7","Competitive Bidding for Toll Highways and Power Plants","This includes undertaking competitive bidding for future toll highways and power plants.",""],[1,"47","7","PPP Development of Strategic Industry Clusters","In addition, a PPP approach will be undertaken to drive the developments of strategic industry clusters such as the development of industrial parks and incubators.",""],[1,"47","7","Public-Private Co-Investment in High-Growth Strategic Sectors","The Government will also co-invest with the private sector, particularly in high growth and strategic sectors, through Government fund agencies such as Malaysian Venture Capital Management Berhad (MAVCAP), Malaysian Technology Development Corporation (MTDC) and Ekuiti Nasional Berhad (EKUINAS).",""],[1,"92","5","Government Business Rationalisation through Privatisation","Rationalising the role of government in business by increasing privatisation",""],[1,"113","1","Government and GLC Role Rationalisation Initiative","active steps will be taken to rationalise the role of the Government and GLCs in business.",""],[1,"113","5","Privatisation and Public-Private Partnership Programme","Malaysia has been implementing privatisation programmes since 1983 and has already established 510 privatisation and PPP projects in the transportation, road, communications, health and energy sectors.",""],[1,"113","6","Privatisation and Public-Private Partnership Programme","A new wave of privatisation will be implemented under the Tenth Plan in order to increase private investment in the economy, improve efficiency in the delivery of services and relieve the financial burden of the Government.",""],[1,"113","7","Infrastructure and Asset Development Projects Under Consideration","will be substantially intensified under the Plan period with 52 projects with an estimated value of RM62.7 billion already under consideration.",""],[1,"113","9","Public Sector Asset Monetisation Programme","Monetisation of public sector assets through outright sale, joint venture or long-term lease of land with commercial potential, such as the Rubber Research Institute in Sungai Buloh and 1Malaysia Development Berhad land development project in Sungai Besi;",""],[1,"113","10","Prospective Company Screening and Eligibility Checks","Putting in place rigorous checks to ensure that prospective companies meet a minimum set of criteria, including financial standing, track record and management excellence;",""],[1,"114","1","Value-for-Money Public-Private Procurement Framework","Adopting value for money drivers such as optimal distribution of risks between the public and private sector, whole life costing, output specification that allows bidders to innovate in the design of the project, competition that provides fair value and performance-based payment mechanism.",""],[1,"114","5","Public-Private Sector Balance and Regulatory Separation Reform","there is a need to ensure an appropriate balance between government, GLCs and the private sector, as well as to create an appropriate separation between regulator and operator.",""],[1,"114","6","GLC Role Rationalisation","The role of GLCs will be rationalised to focus on areas that support the creation of a vibrant private sector while withdrawing from areas that do not enhance value creation.",""],[1,"115","1","Gradual Divestment of Non-Competitive GLC Assets","non-competitive assets of GLCs will be gradually divested in areas where new strategic shareholders have the potential to enhance value creation.",""],[1,"115","1","GLC Sector Catalysis and Nurturing in New Growth Areas","GLCs will continue to catalyse and nurture development of the sectors to lower entry barriers and help build the critical mass required to stimulate private investments.",""],[1,"115","1","GLC Co-Investment for New Markets and Global Expansion","GLCs will also co-invest with the private sector to venture into new markets and ensure Malaysian firms achieve a larger footprint globally.",""],[1,"115","3","Privatisation of Selected Minister of Finance Incorporated Companies","privatisation of companies under Minister of Finance Incorporated such as Percetakan Nasional Berhad, CTRM Aero Composite, Nine Bio Sdn. Bhd. and Inno Bio Sdn. Bhd. will be completed",""],[1,"115","4","State Asset Divestment and Privatization Oversight","The Government will divest its ownership stakes in such a way as to ensure that these assets are broadly held and that the divestment and privatisation initiatives will not affect public interest or the well-being of the rakyat.",""],[1,"115","5","Regulatory Role Review and Market Delineation Reform","a clear delineation between regulator and market players will be introduced.",""]],"116":[[1,"48","3","Public-Private-Civil Society Collaboration for Social Objective Delivery","The Government will support greater collaboration between the public sector, private sector and civil society to enhance delivery of social objectives.",""],[1,"48","3","Expanded Government-NGO Welfare Partnerships","Successful partnerships will be extended, particularly between the Government and non-governmental organisations (NGOs) in welfare initiatives",""],[1,"48","3","Corporate Social Responsibility Programmes in Education and Environmental Conservation","Successful partnerships will be extended, particularly between the Government and non-governmental organisations (NGOs) in welfare initiatives and between public and private sector in corporate social responsibility (CSR) programmes, such as in education and environmental conservation.",""],[1,"48","3","Matching Grants for Low-Cost Housing and Heritage Conservation","The Government will also work with civil society in areas such as the maintenance of low cost housing and heritage conservation through mechanisms such as matching grants.",""],[1,"120","2","Government-to-Government SME Training Partnerships","Malaysia will also foster links with training centres abroad via government-to-government cooperation to develop specialised courses for SMEs.",""]],"117":[[1,"49","1","Sustainable Management of Environmental Assets and Ecological Resources","The Government will ensure that Malaysia's environmental assets and ecological resources are managed sustainably, so that present developmental needs are met without compromising the future.",""],[1,"49","1","Climate Change Adaptation and Mitigation Strategy","In responding to global climate change, the Government will focus on adaptation strategies to ensure sustainable growth and mitigation strategies to reduce the emission of greenhouse gases.",""],[1,"49","2","Mainstream Environmental Considerations in Economic Planning","Mainstreaming environmental considerations will be undertaken, particularly in economic planning to ensure sustainability of resources.",""],[1,"49","2","Environmental Resource Valuation for Investment Appraisal","key to sustainability is a proper valuation of our environmental resources, through assessing the opportunity cost and environmental impact of public or private investments.",""],[1,"49","8","Carbon Credit Eligible Projects Promotion","Promoting projects eligible for carbon credits;",""]],"118":[[1,"53","2","Outcome-Based Planning, Budgeting, and Monitoring Approach","A key initiative involves operationalising an outcome-based approach to planning, budget and monitoring.",""],[1,"352","1","Outcome-Based Planning and Performance Management Approach","An outcome-based approach will be adopted for planning, resource allocation, monitoring and evaluation.",""],[1,"353","2","Outcome-Based Resource Allocation Framework","Resource allocation will be designed around the outcome-based approach.",""],[1,"353","3","Outcome-Based Budgeting Reform","Adopting outcome-based budgeting.",""]],"119":[[1,"53","3","Soft Infrastructure Investment Shift","the proportion of development funding for soft infrastructure will be increased to about 40% compared to only about 22% in the Ninth Plan",""],[1,"86","1","Development Expenditure for Non-Physical Programs","development expenditure will focus on non-physical programmes for which allocation will rise from 22% in the Ninth Plan to 40% in the Tenth Plan.",""]],"120":[[1,"53","6","ICT Productivity Enhancement Initiative","To achieve this, the Government will focus on efforts to reduce subsidies, drive efficiencies and transparency in procurement, driving productivity in Information Communications Technology (ICT) and broadening the tax collection base.",""],[1,"100","4","Digital Service Delivery Enhancement for Businesses","During the Plan period, the Government will continue to enhance the delivery and efficiency of services to business by leveraging ICT.",""],[1,"101","3","MyGovXchange Single Business Gateway Enhancement","The existing MyGovXchange will be enhanced as the single gateway for businesses, covering registration, licence application, licence expansion as well as applications for loans and grants from various public agencies.",""],[1,"101","5","SSM Enterprise Services Gateway Expansion","The system will be expanded from five agencies to include all public agencies dealing with business entities.",""]],"121":[[1,"77","2","Domestic Demand Promotion and Private Sector Stimulation","an important strategy will be to promote domestic demand to become a major driver of growth mainly by energising the private sector.",""],[1,"77","2","Enabling Environment for Productivity, Competitiveness and Innovation","Hence, the nation must create an enabling environment which encourages productivity, competitiveness and innovation.",""],[1,"78","2","Productivity-Driven Growth Strategy","Growth during the Tenth Plan period will be driven by significant increases in productivity, rather than by higher capital and labour inputs, as well as by efficiency gains from removing distortions within the economy.",""],[1,"78","2","Human Capital, Technology Adoption, and Entrepreneurship Development","Productivity growth will be achieved through higher levels of input from human capital, adoption of new technologies and development of entrepreneurship to drive innovation and creativity.",""],[1,"79","1","Niche Growth Area Investment Promotion","Malaysia will benefit from higher investment in niche growth areas, particularly through the intensive use of knowledge, innovation and technology.",""],[1,"79","1","Human Capital Skills and Competency Development","Human capital development will focus on creating talent through enhancing skills and competency of the nation's human resources.",""],[1,"95","1","Private Sector Support Initiatives","To support the private sector and unleash its growth potential, a series of initiatives will be undertaken during the Plan period:",""]],"122":[[1,"95","5","Competition Legislation Introduction","Introducing competition legislation;",""],[1,"100","2","Competition Law Introduction","The Competition Law will be introduced to govern all firms including GLCs against anti-competitive practices.",""],[1,"100","3","Competition Commission and Appeal Tribunal Establishment","A Competition Commission and a Competition Appeal Tribunal will be established by the end of 2010 to ensure smooth and effective implementation of the legislation.",""],[1,"100","3","Competition Law Enforcement Rollout","Enforcement will be implemented after an 18-month grace period to allow for advocacy and to familiarise businesses with the legislation.",""],[1,"115","2","Competition Law Introduction","Introduction of the Competition Law will also ensure fair competition for all companies including GLCs and will control against abuse from market dominance.",""]],"123":[[1,"98","2","Services Sector Liberalisation","During the Plan period, the services sector will be liberalised under the ASEAN Framework Agreement on Services (AFAS), World Trade Organisation (WTO) and free trade arrangements (FTAs).",""],[1,"98","3","ASEAN Services Liberalisation Commitments","further liberalisation will be undertaken for all 128 subsectors, allowing at least 70% ASEAN equity ownership by 2015.",""],[1,"98","3","Sectoral Liberalisation Commitments in Priority Services","improvements and new commitments will include healthcare, tourism, telecommunications, education, environment, transport and business",""],[1,"99","1","Further Liberalisation of Financial and Air Transport Services","financial and air transport services will also be further liberalised towards meeting the targets for 2015.",""],[1,"99","2","Services Sector Liberalisation and Trade Negotiation Programme","the Government will expand on its commitments made to the WTO in 1995 to liberalise 65 services subsectors.",""],[1,"99","3","Services Sector Liberalisation Policy Review","The Government will review domestic policies and regulations that inhibit effective liberalisation of the services sector, including foreign equity restrictions and limits on employment of foreign talent.",""],[1,"99","3","Domestic Service Provider Capability Support","The Government will continue to support domestic service providers to build capabilities and prepare for the rise in competition after liberalisation.",""],[1,"126","1","Bilateral and Regional Preferential Trade Arrangement Expansion","Malaysia will continue to engage in bilateral and regional preferential trade arrangements with its important trading partners to complement efforts in the WTO and seek better access to individual markets.",""],[1,"126","1","Free Trade Agreement Negotiation Programme","During the Plan period, Malaysia will target free trade arrangements with the EU, Transpacific Strategic Partnership, ASEAN+3 and several emerging economies.",""],[1,"126","1","Cost-Benefit Evaluation of New Free Trade Agreements","In pursuing new FTAs, Malaysia will undertake a thorough evaluation of costs and benefits to Malaysian businesses to ensure that they achieve beneficial outcomes.",""]],"124":[[1,"103","3","National Innovation Policy Reform","The Government's innovation agenda will therefore promote innovative activity across the Malaysian economy.",""],[1,"103","5","Innovation System Strengthening Measures","The Government will take a series of actions to strengthen Malaysia's innovation system along four key dimensions:",""],[1,"103","8","Innovation Enablers","Putting in place innovation enablers;",""],[1,"103","9","Innovation Support Environment","The Government will support innovation by creating an environment in which companies, research organisations, and individuals are",""],[1,"104","5","Innovation and R&D Infrastructure Development in Strategic Sectors","The Government will also focus on developing comprehensive innovation and research and development (R&D) infrastructures in selected areas where Malaysia has inherent strength and competitive advantage (such as downstream palm oil, modern agriculture, and oil and gas) in order to become a world leader in these areas.",""],[1,"104","5","Alignment of Innovation and R&D Initiatives with NKEAs and Geographic Clusters","Innovation and R&D initiatives will also be aligned with NKEAs and the geographic cluster strategy to ensure that the science and technology development is consistent with the overall economic agenda.",""],[1,"104","6","Innovation and FDI Incentive Package Reform","Trade and investment policy will be biased towards building innovation capabilities as well as market access and production and volume of investment.",""],[1,"106","4","Regulatory Reform to Drive Innovation","During the Tenth Plan, several regulatory changes are expected to drive innovation.",""],[1,"108","1","Innovation Institutional and Intellectual Property Regime Strengthening","The innovation institutional structure and intellectual property (IP) regime will be strengthened during the Plan period as they are critical innovation enablers.",""],[1,"108","2","Review of the Institutional Structure for Innovation and R&D","A review of the institutional structure supporting innovation and R&D is imperative to improve innovation outcomes.",""],[1,"108","3","Institutional Structure Reform","Therefore, a reform of institutional structure will be undertaken during the Plan period, as shown in Chart 3-5.",""],[1,"108","10","Policy Instruments and Programmes Evaluation","Undertake evaluation of policy instruments and programmes",""],[1,"108","15","Science and Technology Development Policy Formulation","Formulate policies for S&T development",""],[1,"108","16","Oversight of Resource Allocation for Non-Technological Innovation","Oversee resource allocation for non-technological innovation",""],[1,"108","17","Resource Allocation Oversight for Technological Innovation","Oversee resource allocation for technological innovation",""],[1,"108","21","R&D Investment Prioritization","Set priorities for R&D investment",""]],"125":[[1,"48","1","Industry Co-funding for Post-graduate Courses, R&D and Centres of Excellence","the Government will also initiate co- funding with industry for post-graduate courses, R&D and centres of excellence.",""],[1,"104","1","Human Capital, Innovation Infrastructure, and Incubator Support","These measures will include developing human capital, investing in innovation infrastructure and nurturing new ventures through incubators.",""],[1,"104","3","Global Academic Leadership Recruitment and Capability Transfer Partnerships","the Government will commit to using global search to headhunt the best academic leadership for programmes that support innovation, and will also partner with leading global research institutions to ensure deep and sustained capability transfer.",""],[1,"104","3","University-Industry Mobility and Contract Research Scheme","education and training will be brought closer to industry by allowing greater mobility of academics to conduct contract research and consultancy and for industry practitioners to teach in universities.",""],[1,"104","3","Industrial PhD Co-Sponsorship Programme","A programme will be introduced to promote participation from the industry to co-sponsor employees to obtain industrial PhDs.",""]],"126":[[1,"109","2","Intellectual Property Regime Upgrade","The IP regime, including the expertise and institutional capacity of IP examiners and agents, will be upgraded to improve the investment climate and investor confidence and provide a dynamic environment for the creation of new and innovative products and services.",""],[1,"109","2","Online Intellectual Property Filing and Search Services","web-based facilities will be provided including a voluntary registration system for copyright protection and a patent search database.",""],[1,"109","2","IP Filing Incentive Grants and Preferential Loans","To incentivise the filing and maintenance of IP, the Government will make available grants and preferential rate loans.",""]],"127":[[1,"108","20","Productivity Enhancement Research and Activities","Undertake productivity enhan- cement research & activities",""]],"128":[[1,"119","3","SME Supplier Training for MNC Standards","Employees of SMEs that supply products and services to MNCs and large companies will be given hands-on training to upgrade their knowledge and skills.",""],[1,"119","4","SME Skills Training Programme","Skills training programmes.",""],[1,"120","1","Medium-Term Industry Training Maps and Industry-Related Training","To support SMEs in human capital management, the Government will collaborate with trade and industry associations to develop medium-term training maps and undertake industry-related training;",""],[1,"120","2","SME Overseas Training Support","The Government will assist SMEs to obtain training in areas which are not available locally by engaging foreign trainers and experts.",""],[1,"120","3","SME-University Internship Programme Enhancement","the Government will enhance the SME-University Internship Programme.",""],[1,"120","3","Youth Entrepreneurship Promotion through Business Plan Competitions","The Government will also promote entrepreneurship to young Malaysians by sponsoring business plan competitions at schools and universities, introducing business-related",""],[1,"120","4","Student and Graduate Entrepreneurship Promotion Programme","funding public campaigns that showcase successful Malaysian entrepreneurs.",""],[1,"120","6","SME Branding Capabilities Training Programme","Additionally, in order to support SMEs in developing branding, capabilities training will be provided in collaboration with universities and the mobile branding and packaging gallery initiative, which provides advisory services, will also be expanded to provide coverage to smaller towns.",""]],"129":[[1,"126","7","Port Infrastructure Investment","Investment in port infrastructure",""],[1,"134","1","Multimodal Transportation Network Development","a multimodal transportation network will be further developed.",""],[1,"134","1","East-Coast Highway Completion","The East-Coast Highway from Kuantan to Kuala Terengganu will be completed in 2012",""],[1,"134","1","Kuantan Port Expansion","the expansion of Kuantan Port",""],[1,"134","1","Penang Second Bridge Completion","the completion of the Penang Second Bridge",""],[1,"134","1","South Klang Valley Expressway Completion","the South Klang Valley Expressway, which is expected to be completed in 2012 will provide a second access to Westport of Port Klang",""],[1,"134","2","Electrified Double-Track Railway Extension to Johor Bahru","the electrified double-track railway project will be extended to Johor Bahru to complete the network and increase operational efficiency.",""],[1,"134","3","Johor Bahru to Padang Besar Freight Rail Track Project","track project from Johor Bahru in the south to Padang Besar, Perlis in the north, at an estimated cost of RM16.5 billion",""],[1,"134","3","Rail Freight Capacity Expansion","To accommodate increasing freight volume, existing train sets will be refurbished and new ones will be purchased.",""],[1,"134","3","East Coast and Sabah Rail Modernisation Programme","rail services will be enhanced by modernisation of facilities and technologies to increase access to rural areas.",""],[1,"134","3","Kuala Lumpur Mass Rapid Transit System","a mass rapid transit system covering a 20km radius from the Kuala Lumpur city centre will be implemented",""],[1,"134","4","National Port Policy Formulation","During the Plan period, a national port policy will be formulated to outline the objectives, strategic directions and further development of the port sector.",""],[1,"134","4","Maritime Infrastructure Upgrading Programme","Maritime infrastructure will be upgraded to ensure competitiveness of Malaysian ports, including spending about RM1 billion for the capital dredging of port channels to cater for bigger vessels and upgrading works at Westport of Port Klang, Selangor and Port of Tanjung Pelepas, Johor to provide additional capacity for import and export of goods.",""],[1,"135","1","Port Upgrading Works","upgrading works of Westport, Port of Tanjung Pelepas and Penang Port, totalling RM6 billion.",""],[1,"135","2","Airport Capacity Expansion Programme","this will necessitate expansion of airport capacity at a cost of RM3.3 billion.",""],[1,"135","2","Kuala Lumpur International Airport Low-Cost Carrier Terminal Construction","A new low cost carrier terminal will be built at Kuala Lumpur International Airport (KLIA) to cater for the rising number of flights.",""],[1,"135","2","Penang International Airport Upgrade","the Penang International Airport will be upgraded, in terms of both passenger and cargo facilities, to support the development of the Northern Corridor Economic Region (NCER).",""],[1,"135","2","Airline Attraction and Connectivity Enhancement Effort","the expansion of airport capacity will be complemented with concerted efforts to attract more airlines, thus creating better connectivity to support KLIA as an aviation hub.",""],[1,"135","2","Aviation Sector Stakeholder Council","a council consisting of major stakeholders will be formed to address issues pertaining to the aviation sector including formulating a route allocation policy.",""]],"130":[[1,"137","2","Gas Supply Liberalisation and Electricity Sector Restructuring","the gas supply industry will be further liberalised to facilitate the entry of new suppliers and third-party access arrangements.",""],[1,"137","3","New Energy Policy Structural Reform Initiatives","The New Energy Policy necessitates fundamental structural changes during the Plan period.",""]],"131":[[1,"140","7","Kuala Lumpur Investment Attraction Ecosystem","During the Plan period, the potential of Kuala Lumpur will be harnessed by providing a comprehensive ecosystem to attract high quality investment in a selected number of areas, improving the quality of living and bring greater vibrancy.",""],[1,"140","7","City Specialisation and Liveability Investment Programme","Additionally, other cities such as Georgetown, Johor Bahru and Kota Kinabalu will specialise in order to achieve critical scale, and investments will be made to improve liveability, with clearly measurable targets.",""],[1,"158","2","Crime Reduction Initiative for Greater Kuala Lumpur","Major initiatives have been identified under the national key results areas (NKRAs) to address this, particularly on combating crime and improving urban public transport.",""],[1,"158","2","Urban Public Transport Improvement Initiative for Greater Kuala Lumpur","Major initiatives have been identified under the national key results areas (NKRAs) to address this, particularly on combating crime and improving urban public transport.",""],[1,"158","2","Public Space, Arts and Leisure Enhancement Initiative","initiatives to create attractive public spaces, nurture a uniquely internationally relevant arts and culture scene, and provide a rich mix of leisure activities will create a distinctive urban character for Greater KL, making it an ideal place to live, work and play.",""],[1,"158","4","Kuala Lumpur International Financial District Development","Establishing Kuala Lumpur International Financial District as a global financial centre, especially for Islamic finance and its related professional services, in order to attract local and international financial policy and monitoring organisations and talent;",""],[1,"158","6","Greater KL Tourism Destination Development","Making Greater KL a tourist destination by leveraging on existing iconic institutions such as Muzium Negara and Istana Budaya, and also Malaysia Truly Asia Centre, which is to be established during the Plan period;",""],[1,"158","7","Comprehensive Open Space Strategy","Creating a network of attractive open public spaces by developing a comprehensive open space strategy that moves beyond allocating land and infrastructure for open spaces, to one that incorporates strategies to attract people to these spaces.",""],[1,"158","7","Lake Gardens Botanical Garden and Green Space Network","The 101-hectare Lake Gardens will be developed into a world-class botanical garden, connected to a citywide network of interconnected green spaces that are equipped with facilities such as cycling paths and pedestrian pathways;",""],[1,"158","8","Mass Rapid Transit System for Greater Kuala Lumpur","Transforming urban public transportation across greater KL through the Mass Rapid Transit System to ensure seamless interconnectivity links.",""]],"132":[[1,"142","6","Iskandar Malaysia Growth Node Investment and Economic Cluster Development","During the Tenth Plan period, Iskandar Malaysia will further draw investments into the 5 identified growth nodes to build economic clusters in the areas of education, healthcare, finance, creative industry, logistics and tourism.",""],[1,"142","6","Johor Premium Outlet Development Project","Among the keys projects will be the Johor Premium Outlet and MSC Cyberport City.",""],[1,"142","6","MSC Cyberport City Development Project","Among the keys projects will be the Johor Premium Outlet and MSC Cyberport City.",""],[1,"142","7","Johor Bahru City Centre Infrastructure Improvement Programme","Complementing the above projects, several infrastructure projects such as the road construction surrounding Johor Bharu (JB) city centre, the improvement in the public transport system and the proposed JB City Transformation project will be implemented.",""],[1,"142","7","Johor Bahru City Transformation Project","the proposed JB City Transformation project will be implemented.",""]],"133":[[1,"143","4","Penang Logistics Hub Development","Logistics: To develop the region as a major import and export centre leveraging Penang International Airport, Second Penang Bridge, double tracking and the augmentation of the Penang Port.",""]],"134":[[1,"141","3","Private Sector Collaboration for Priority Industry Development","Refocus on catalysing growth through collaborating with the private sector to develop priority industries;",""],[1,"144","2","Priority Industry Promotion and Development through Private Sector Participation","Priority industries which will be promoted and developed through greater private sector participation include aluminium, glass, steel, oil- based, palm oil, fishing and aquaculture (Halal Hub), livestock, timber-based, marine engineering and tourism.",""]],"135":[[1,"147","3","Palm Oil Hub and Foreign Investment Promotion","Promoting Malaysia as a global hub for palm oil and preferred destination for foreign investments in areas such as oleochemical based products, bulking facilities and R&D;",""],[1,"147","4","Palm Oil Industrial Cluster Development","Developing Palm Oil Industrial Clusters into integrated sites for promoting downstream activities such as biofuel, oleochemicals, biofertilisers, specialty food products, biomass products, nutraceuticals and pharmaceuticals;",""]],"136":[[1,"147","5","Good Agricultural Practices and Mechanisation Support for Smallholders","Encouraging good agriculture practices, agronomic management and mechanisation especially among smallholders;",""],[1,"147","6","Centralised Agricultural Input Procurement","Centralising procurement of agricultural inputs such as fertilisers and pesticides to lower input costs for smallholders.",""],[1,"157","3","Agricultural Consortiums and Cooperatives Development","Setting up agriculture consortiums and cooperatives to reap the benefits of scale, encourage adoption of accredited practices by farmers, fishermen and agropreneurs, and strengthen marketing through contract farming and strategic alliances;",""],[1,"157","5","ICT-Based Agriculture Flagship Project","Promoting innovation-based growth and production processes that utilise modern farm technology and ICT, including ICT-based Agriculture Flagship Project;",""],[1,"157","6","Infrastructure and Logistics Support for Value Addition in Food Production Parks and Aquaculture Zones","Providing adequate and specific infrastructure, facilities and logistics to support value addition activities based on availability and proximity of resources, particularly in the designated Permanent Food Production Parks and Aquaculture Industrial Zones;",""],[1,"157","7","Collaborative Agricultural Research and Innovation Programme","Intensifying collaborative R&D with established agriculture research institutes to leapfrog innovation in the production processes, disease control, safety and quality control, including development of new high-value added products.",""]],"137":[[1,"157","8","National Rice Supply Security Measures","During the Plan period, strategies to ensure sufficient supply of rice include maintaining rice stockpile at 292,000 metric tonnes or sustained consumption for 45 days, entering long-term contract agreements to import rice with matching agreements to export palm oil or oil, and increasing the productivity of existing granary and non-granary areas through upgrading of infrastructure.",""]],"138":[[1,"148","3","Financial Sector Strengthening Initiative","During the Plan period, the financial sector will be further strengthened so that it remains competitive, resilient, diversified, inclusive and continues to meaningfully contribute to economic growth.",""],[1,"148","3","Capital Market Liquidity Enhancement","The role and liquidity of capital market will also continue to be enhanced.",""],[1,"148","4","New Financial Sector Blueprint","Formulating a new financial sector blueprint to articulate strategies to further evolve the Malaysian financial sector to support and drive the next phase of Malaysia's economic development, which includes promoting financial inclusion and continued equitable financing access to all segments of the economy, greater leveraging of technology and innovation in the delivery of financial services, enhancing the financial system infrastructure including institutional and capacity building, and implementing adequate safeguards to preserve financial stability.",""],[1,"148","4","General Insurance Industry Consolidation and Rationalisation","The structural issues within the general insurance industry will be addressed by promoting further consolidation and rationalisation.",""],[1,"148","4","Insurance Penetration Expansion through Alternative Distribution and Product Innovation","Insurance penetration will also be enhanced via alternative distribution channels and greater product innovation;",""],[1,"149","1","Strengthening Malaysia International Islamic Financial Centre Initiatives","Enhancing Malaysia's position in Islamic finance globally via the strengthening of the Malaysia International Islamic Financial Centre (MIFC) initiatives, fostering greater linkages and collaboration with international standard setting bodies and other jurisdictions, and streamlining R&D development to enhance Malaysia's attractiveness as a preferred centre for Islamic financial education, research, training and product innovation.",""],[1,"149","2","Capital Market Masterplan 2","Developing the Capital Market Masterplan 2 with strategic initiatives to expand the role of capital market in supporting the transition to a high income and knowledge-based economy.",""]],"139":[[1,"150","4","Retail and Wholesale Sector Liberalisation and Investment Promotion","Liberalising the retail and wholesale sector and promoting investment;",""],[1,"150","5","Local Retailer Consolidation Initiative","Encouraging consolidation among local retailers to encourage efficiencies and achieve economies of scale;",""],[1,"150","6","Modern Retail Format Promotion","Encouraging modern retail formats such as hypermarkets, supermarkets, convenience stores, specialty stores to stimulate investment and expedite modernisation;",""],[1,"150","7","Franchise, Direct Sales, and E-Commerce Promotion","Promoting franchise, direct sales and e-commerce to achieve their full potential.",""]],"140":[[1,"153","4","Demand-Side Higher Education Financing Expansion","Expanding demand-side financing and undertake new provision of public higher learning institution (IPTA) seats through off-take in private higher learning institution (IPTS) and create private seats in IPTAs by expanding capacity through private subsidiaries.",""],[1,"153","5","Performance-Based Funding for Private Higher Education Institutions","Improving quality of IPTS through performance-based funding by expanding the Rating System for Malaysian Higher Education Institution (SETARA) to cover private universities and college universities, and at the faculty level;",""],[1,"153","6","PTPTN Sliding-Scale Student Loan Expansion","Expanding the sliding scale on the National Higher Education Fund Corporation (PTPTN) loans to promote cost sharing based on means test of parent's income to ensure financial sustainability and increased access of low and middle income families;",""],[1,"153","7","Central Student Enrolment System","Introducing a central enrolment system for all students including international students in stages with flexible credit accumulation framework for all courses across public and private provision;",""],[1,"153","8","Conducive Educational Ecosystem for International Branch Campuses","Providing conducive educational ecosystem to attract students and world leading faculties in niche areas to set up branches in Malaysia;",""]],"141":[[1,"155","1","Development of Construction-Related and Environmental Management Services","To achieve this target, the focus will be on further developing construction related and environmental management services.",""],[1,"155","3","Support for Exporting Professional Construction Services","Providing support such as market intelligence, networks and government-to-government relations to enable firms to export professional construction services within ASEAN region, India and China as well as Organisation of Islamic Countries (OIC) countries;",""],[1,"155","4","Overseas Promotion of Malaysian Professional Construction Services","Establishing a consolidated presence and brand for Malaysian professional construction services overseas.",""],[1,"155","5","Legislative Amendment for Industry Liberalisation Commitments","Amending legislation to facilitate commitments made at bilateral, regional and multilateral levels to liberalise the industry and create new business opportunities.",""]],"142":[[1,"164","9","Basic Infrastructure and Services Expansion","citizens will be able to enjoy equitable access to basic infrastructure and services through expanding the provision of electricity services, treated water supply, road infrastructure, education and healthcare services",""],[1,"198","5","Rural Basic Infrastructure and Social Amenities Provision","Apart from expanding the provision of basic infrastructure, initiative will continue to undertaken to provide social amenities, sanitation facilities, sport facilities and recreational areas to the rural population to improve their quality of life.",""]],"143":[[1,"164","4","New Affirmative Action Instruments","New affirmative action instruments will allow resources to be optimally allocated and not cause, contribute or perpetuate economic distortions;",""],[1,"164","10","Inclusiveness Support Programme for Disadvantaged Groups","Inclusiveness programmes will ensure that disadvantaged groups such as the disabled are supported to be valued participants in society and where necessary, adequately assisted to raise their quality of life.",""],[1,"165","5","Consultative Setting of Inclusiveness Requirements and Targets","a more consultative approach will be undertaken in setting inclusiveness requirements and targets for companies that are beneficiaries of government contracts, licences and incentives.",""],[1,"171","7","Phase Out Quota-Based Instruments","Past instruments, based purely on quotas that are no longer relevant and sustainable, will be phased out to make room for market-friendly policies and instruments that are compatible with national competitiveness.",""],[1,"171","7","Adopt Market-Friendly Competitiveness Policies","Past instruments, based purely on quotas that are no longer relevant and sustainable, will be phased out to make room for market-friendly policies and instruments that are compatible with national competitiveness.",""],[1,"171","7","Promote Social Mobility and Income Gap Reduction","The focus now will be to build on the new Bumiputera middle class and move the nation towards higher income, whilst at the same time improving social mobility within all parts of society and ensuring that the income gap does not widen.",""]],"144":[[1,"165","1","Merit-Based Programme Allocation","Programmes will encourage competition and award opportunities to the most qualified individuals and businesses;",""],[1,"165","2","Transparency in Policies, Procedures, and Criteria","Policies, procedures, and criteria will be made clear and public.",""]],"145":[[1,"167","1","Basic Training and Small-Scale Self-Employment Support","Focusing on basic training and supporting small scale to promote self employment establishments, particularly amongst disadvantaged groups and the unemployed",""],[1,"167","2","Bottom 40% Household Entrepreneurship Programmes","Strengthening and expanding for bottom 40% households entrepreneurship programmes regardless of ethnicity, with targeted programmes for special needs groups",""],[1,"175","6","Integrated Business Start-Up Support","Greater support in establishing own businesses through integrated provision of training, funding and key equipment",""],[1,"175","14","Employment and Self-Employment Support Expansion","increasing access to opportunities for employment whilst at the same time strengthening the support for self-employment.",""],[1,"175","15","Urban Bottom 40% Capability Building Programmes","During the Plan period, the wellbeing of the urban bottom 40% households will be addressed through capability building programmes to improve their income and overall quality of life.",""],[1,"176","7","Holistic Support Programmes for Micro-Enterprises","Providing holistic support programmes for micro-enterprises;",""],[1,"180","1","Urban Bottom 40% Micro-Enterprise Support Programme","Expanding micro-enterprise support programmes for bottom 40% households in urban areas;",""],[1,"180","6","Micro-Enterprise Expansion for Urban Bottom 40% Households","Micro-enterprise programmes will be expanded to assist urban bottom 40% households to establish small businesses.",""],[1,"180","7","Entrepreneurship Training and Start-up Financing Support","institutions such as Institut Keusahawanan Negara (INSKEN) will be leveraged to provide the training and qualified participants who graduate from the training programmes will be provided with financial assistance to support their new business start up.",""],[1,"180","8","Mentor-Mentee Programme for Entrepreneur Development","Entrepreneur development organisations such as Perbadanan Usahawan Nasional Berhad (PUNB) and MARA have implemented mentor-mentee programmes as a means to replicate the proven business models, product portfolios and supply chain networks of successful entrepreneurs.",""],[1,"190","2","Micro Enterprise Promotion Support Programme","Micro enterprises will be promoted through funding, capability building and infrastructure provision in a means-tested approach, targeted primarily at improving the livelihoods of Bumiputera",""]],"146":[[1,"175","4","Employment Hubs Linking Employers and Rural Talent","Employment hubs will be created to link employers in clusters and cities to talent pool in rural areas and provide training",""],[1,"177","8","Employment Hubs for Career Counselling and Job Placement","The Government will establish employment hubs to provide career counselling and job placement programmes in areas where employment opportunities are scarce.",""],[1,"178","1","Employer-Linked Workforce Matching and Pre-Employment Training","identify the categories of workforce requirements through consultation with key employers in nearby clusters and cities and match the requirements with suitable candidates in adjacent rural areas.",""]],"147":[[1,"176","6","Rural Household Income Enhancement Programmes","Programmes to increase the incomes of rural households will focus on upgrading their skills, linking them to employers in nearby clusters and cities as well as providing support for self employment, micro-businesses and small scale industries.",""],[1,"176","6","Agro-based Productivity and Sustainability Programme","Efforts will also be undertaken to increase the productivity and sustainability of agro-based activities through the adoption of modern agricultural technology and expansion of contract farming.",""],[1,"176","9","Contract Farming for Agricultural Income Sustainability","Increasing sustainability of income in the agriculture sector through the concept of contract farming;",""],[1,"176","10","Rural Business Ownership Support","Providing opportunities for business ownership for capable rural entrepreneurs;",""],[1,"176","11","Land Amalgamation for Agricultural Productivity","Increasing land productivity and yield through land amalgamation;",""],[1,"177","5","Expansion of the Agropolitan Concept","Expanding the application of the agropolitan concept to other agriculture and agro-based industries.",""],[1,"177","7","Home Stay and Eco-Tourism Support Programme","in areas where tourism is a key industry, residents will be provided with support to establish home stay programmes and provide eco-tourism services.",""],[1,"178","2","Contract Farming Expansion Programme","To create better market access and more sustainable incomes in the agriculture sector, contract farming will be expanded.",""],[1,"178","3","Modern Agriculture Business Development in Rural Areas","Government agencies such as the Department of Agriculture in collaboration with the government- linked companies (GLCs) such as Khazanah Nasional Berhad's subsidiary, Blue Archipelago, will take the lead in establishing modern agriculture businesses in rural areas such as environmentally","Department of Agriculture"],[1,"178","4","Sustainable Aquaculture and Organic Farming Entrepreneurship Programme","This will include building facilities, establishing markets, obtaining the required certification and establishing processes based on good agricultural practices.",""],[1,"178","5","Land Parcel Amalgamation and Professional Management Programme","Amalgamation of larger parcels of land via government agencies such as the Rubber Industry Smallholders Development Authority (RISDA), the Federal Land Consolidation and Rehabilitation Authority (FELCRA) and cooperatives will be encouraged to increase scale and improve land productivity.",""],[1,"179","1","Rural Agriculture Productivity and Income Improvement Programmes","The Government will continue to implement programmes to improve the productivity and income of workers and small business owners within the rural agriculture and agro-based industries.",""],[1,"179","1","Fishermen Fuel Subsidies and Infrastructure Support","the fishermen community will continue to be provided with petrol and diesel subsidies as well as better infrastructure equipment and facilities such as boats, docking bays and jetties.",""],[1,"179","1","Fishermen Direct Sales Marketing Programme","A marketing programme will be designed to assist fishermen in direct sales of their catches to gain a greater share of profits.",""],[1,"179","1","Entrepreneurship Development Scheme for Agro-Businesses","Under the entrepreneurship development scheme, start-up capital as well as training courses will be provided to develop more entrepreneurs and sustainable small-scale agro-businesses.",""],[1,"179","1","Youth Participation in Agriculture Programmes","Specific programmes will also be introduced to encourage greater youth participation in agricultural activities.",""],[1,"179","2","Agropolitan Rural Development and Land Share Scheme","Agropolitan development strategies will utilise an integrated approach to advance rural development in agriculture, agro-based and otherrural industries.",""],[1,"179","3","Settler Infrastructure and Support Services for Commercial Farming","Each settler will be provided with housing and land for commercial farming, including livestock, crops or aquaculture, and participants are expected to earn a minimum monthly income.",""],[1,"179","3","Agricultural Capability Building and Market Support","A number of support services and enablers will also be provided including capability building programmes, technology transfer for good agriculture practices, transport, marketing support and availability of consumer credit during the early stages of the project.",""],[1,"179","4","Small Business Modernisation and Scale-Up Programmes","efforts to modernise and scale-up small businesses will be implemented through various programmes conducted by agencies such as AIM and TEKUN.",""]],"148":[[1,"177","6","Holistic Funding, Equipment, and Training Support Programmes","Funding programmes, conducted by agencies such as Majlis Amanah Rakyat (MARA), Amanah Ikhtiar Malaysia (AIM) and Tabung Ekonomi Kumpulan Usaha Niaga (TEKUN), will be strengthened to provide a more holistic approach incorporating funding, equipment and training in business and technical areas.",""],[1,"177","6","Continued Skills Development and Community Training Services","Institutions such as Pusat Giat MARA, community colleges, Jabatan Kemajuan Masyarakat (KEMAS) and skills development centres will continue to provide",""],[1,"177","7","Skills Training for Self-Employment Programme","skills training in areas such as carpentry, tailoring, baking, hospitality, handicrafts, motor mechanics and food processing to support self-employment.",""],[1,"177","7","Localised Training Delivery for Target Localities","The delivery of these training programmes will be tailored to the specific opportunities of target localities.",""],[1,"179","1","Fishermen and Farmers Training Support","Training will be given to assist fishermen and farmers to increase their productivity and improve their standard of living.",""],[1,"179","4","Skills Training and Skills Upgrading Programmes","Initiatives to increase income and quality of life of this group will include capacity enhancement programmes through skills training and skills upgrading to enable them to secure higher paying jobs as well as engage in skills-based businesses.",""],[1,"179","5","Industry-Specific Skills Centres","Establishing industry-specific skills centres based on targeted geographic areas;",""],[1,"180","5","Industry-Related Skills Development Programmes","Government agencies will collaborate with industry associations and key players to establish industry-related skills development programmes in targeted areas.",""],[1,"180","5","Tourism Talent Pipeline Programme","The focus will be on creating relevant jobs programmes such as programmes to build a talent pipeline for the tourism industry in Sabah and coastal Terengganu as well as a pipeline of skilled agricultural workers in Kedah.",""],[1,"180","5","Skilled Agricultural Workers Pipeline Programme","The focus will be on creating relevant jobs programmes such as programmes to build a talent pipeline for the tourism industry in Sabah and coastal Terengganu as well as a pipeline of skilled agricultural workers in Kedah.",""],[1,"180","6","Technical and Entrepreneurship Training for Micro-Entrepreneurs","Technical training will be provided in areas such as health and wellness, laundrettes, auto workshops, restaurants, franchised businesses and tailoring, while general entrepreneurship training will cover financial management, marketing, contract management and operations management.",""]],"149":[[1,"180","2","Mentor-Mentee Business Opportunity Programme","Enhancing mentor-mentee programmes to create additional business opportunities;",""],[1,"180","3","Incubator Expansion for Entrepreneurship and Employment","Extending the incubator concept to increase entrepreneurship and employment opportunities;",""],[1,"180","4","Anchor Company Programme Expansion","Expanding anchor company programmes to enable the formation of partnerships and clusters.",""],[1,"180","9","Food Industry Incubator Expansion","MARA has successfully piloted a food industry incubator facility, and this concept will be extended in the Plan period to provide employment opportunities in low income areas.",""],[1,"181","2","Expansion of Anchor Company Programmes","Anchor company programmes led by GLCs and government agencies such as MARA will be expanded.",""],[1,"181","2","Incentives for Anchor Company Cluster Development","Incentives will be provided for the anchor companies to establish clusters in partnership with smaller businesses in rural and urban areas.",""],[1,"181","2","Funding Support for Programme Implementation","In addition, funding support will be provided to facilitate the implementation of the programmes including",""],[1,"193","2","Expansion of Cluster Initiatives","The implementation of existing cluster initiatives will be expanded while new clusters will be explored.",""],[1,"193","2","Anchor Company and Vendor Development Programme","Established companies will be identified as anchor companies for each cluster and undertake vendor development programmes to support participation across the value chain.",""],[1,"193","2","Cluster Anchor Company Target","During the Plan period, the Government targets to establish a minimum of 100 anchor companies to support the operation of 1,000 vendors.",""]],"150":[[1,"182","6","Social Protection Programme Strengthening","Social protection programmes will be strengthened to ensure immediate issues impacting the living standards of disadvantaged groups are addressed.",""],[1,"184","1","Subsidy Restructuring and Targeted Income Support","During the Plan period, subsidies will be restructured whilst a more targeted approach will be adopted to provide income support for eligible groups within the bottom 40% households.",""],[1,"184","2","Income Support for Vulnerable Groups","The Department of Social Welfare or Jabatan Kebajikan Masyarakat (JKM) will continue to provide income support for groups with specific needs such as the older persons with disabilities and single mothers.","Department of Social Welfare | Jabatan Kebajikan Masyarakat (JKM)"],[1,"184","2","eKasih Social Assistance Database Enhancement","A central database, eKasih, will be used to identify and coordinate the delivery of income support.",""],[1,"184","3","Direct Assistance to Bottom 40% Households","assistance will be channelled directly to the bottom 40% households to ensure that they are not adversely impacted.",""],[1,"184","4","Targeted CSR and Non-Governmental Aid Disbursement Support","made available to registered non-governmental organisations (NGOs), charities and corporations to enable better targeting and disbursement of non-governmental aid programmes as well as to encourage more companies to be involved in CSR programmes.",""],[1,"184","4","Corporate CSR Participation for Targeted Support","GLCs such as Petroliam Nasional Berhad (PETRONAS), Sime Darby Berhad and United Engineers (Malaysia) Berhad (UEM) will be encouraged to participate through incorporating and tailoring their own CSR programmes to provide targeted support to individuals that are most in need.",""],[1,"184","4","PETRONAS Essential Food Assistance Programme","PETRONAS has committed RM100 million to provide support to identified households in the form of essential food assistance to alleviate their hardships.",""]],"151":[[1,"183","2","Rural Housing Construction and Upgrading Assistance","For rural areas, assistance will continue to be given to build and upgrade rural homes especially for households with larger household size, older persons, single parents or individuals with",""],[1,"183","3","House Construction on Eligible Household Land","Where eligible households own a parcel of land, the Government will construct a house on the land.",""],[1,"183","3","CSR Housing Provision by GLCs and Private Sector","GLCs and the private sector will be encouraged to provide houses through their corporate social responsibility (CSR) programmes.",""],[1,"183","4","Affordable Housing Expansion Programme","For urban and semi-urban areas, affordable housing programmes and clusters as well as the provision of low-cost housing will be expanded.",""],[1,"183","4","Affordable Medium-Cost Housing Development Incentives","The private sector will also be encouraged to develop more affordable medium-cost housing.",""],[1,"183","4","Inclusive Housing Facilities Upgrade","In addition, efforts will be undertaken to incorporate facilities that will encourage greater community development and better access for older persons and persons with disabilities.",""],[1,"199","8","Housing Construction for Poor and Hardcore Poor Households","Building housing for poor and hardcore poor;",""]],"152":[[1,"185","3","Integrated Poverty Reduction Programmes for Bumiputera and Indigenous Communities","During the Plan period, integrated development programmes and specific enhancement assistance will be implemented to address the high incidence of poverty among the Bumiputera in Sabah and Sarawak, particularly ethnic minorities such as the Bisaya, Orang Sungei, Rungus, Suluk, Tidong, Penan, Kajang, Kedayan and Kelabit, and Orang Asli communities in Peninsular Malaysia.",""],[1,"185","4","Orang Asli Land Development and Ownership Programme","For the Orang Asli communities, a land development and ownership programme will be",""],[1,"186","1","Orang Asli Reserve Land Agricultural Development Programme","The Government will develop Orang Asli reserve land for agriculture use.",""],[1,"186","1","Potential Land Development Programme for Ethnic Minorities in Sabah and Sarawak","Possibility of implementing similar programmes will be considered for the ethnic minorities in Sabah and Sarawak.",""]],"153":[[1,"187","5","Treated Water Supply for Estate Workers","a total allocation of RM109 million will be provided between 2011 and 2012 to supply treated water to estates that are 1,000 acres in size or smaller and are located less than five kilometres distance from the main pipeline",""],[1,"187","5","Estate Community Coordination Committees","Jawatankuasa Kemajuan dan Keselamatan Kampung will be established to foster closer ties between residents of estates and nearby villages with district offices",""],[1,"187","6","Estate Owner Collaboration for Access Roads and Basic Amenities","Efforts will be initiated to encourage collaboration with estate owners in providing access roads and basic amenities such as housing and school facilities.",""],[1,"187","6","Expanded Training and Re-skilling for Displaced Estate Workers","Existing training and re-skilling programmes will also be extended to include displaced estate workers to increase their employability.",""]],"154":[[1,"190","3","Private Equity Support for Growth-Stage Businesses","For businesses in the development and growth stage, support will focus on promoting consolidation and scaling up to achieve competitiveness, for example through provision of private equity funding.",""],[1,"191","4","Growth Stage Company Investment Programme","During the Plan period, Ekuiti Nasional Berhad (EKUINAS) will receive RM4.5 billion of Government allocation and raise additional funding from the private sector to undertake investments in growth stage companies.",""],[1,"192","1","Strategic Equity Investment and Buy-Out Programme","types of investments, i.e. buy-outs of non-core assets of GLCs, Multinational Companies (MNCs) and Public Listed Companies (PLCs); buy-outs of suitable Malaysian companies where existing shareholders are exiting; and investing in existing strong Bumiputera companies to accelerate growth of the company.",""],[1,"192","2","Renewal and Expansion of Private Equity Programmes in GLICs","Private equity programmes in government-linked investment companies (GLICs) such as PNB, Lembaga Tabung Angkatan Tentera (LTAT) and Tabung Haji (TH) will be renewed, strengthened and expanded to consolidate and pool various funds to expand equity ownership and control.",""],[1,"192","2","Diversification of GLIC Investments into High-Return Activities","These institutions will also be encouraged to actively venture and diversify into high-return economic activities that generate greater opportunities for Bumiputera.",""],[1,"192","3","Management Buy-Out and Business Acquisition Loan Facility","Loans to enable management buy-out (MBOs) and/or acquisition of businesses with positive cash flows will be provided through PUNB.",""]],"155":[[1,"192","5","Demand-Driven High-Value Industry Development Approach","A demand-driven approach will be adopted to catalyse businesses in high value added activities.",""],[1,"192","5","Targeted Sector High-Potential Industry Identification","In targeted sectors, industry development organisations will identify areas of high potential such as molecular marker research services for agriculture (biotech); animal fat substitutes (halal industry) and oil recovery technologies (oil and gas).",""],[1,"192","5","Government Funding Allocation for High-Potential Industries","Government will allocate funding",""]],"156":[[1,"193","3","Bumiputera Entrepreneur Development Funding Programme Restructuring","Bumiputera entrepreneur development funding programmes will be restructured and managed by fewer agencies to ensure adequate coverage by sector and business lifecycle.",""],[1,"193","5","Review and Rationalize Entrepreneur Development Organizations and Development Financial Institutions","Existing entrepreneur development organisations (EDOs) including MARA, PUNB and Perbadanan Nasional Berhad (PNS) and development financial institutions (DFIs) will be reviewed to increase their effectiveness.",""],[1,"193","5","Rationalization and Streamlining of EDO and DFI Functions","The functions of EDOs and DFIs will be rationalised and streamlined to reduce duplication, improve efficiency and effectiveness of the delivery system and optimise usage of resources.",""],[1,"193","5","Performance-Linked Compensation for Entrepreneur Support Institutions","Competitive performance-linked compensation will be put in place to encourage achievement of target outcomes as well as increase the organisation's ability to attract and retain high quality talent and ensure sufficient talent specialisation in innovation-intensive sectors.",""]],"157":[[1,"192","4","Innovation-Driven Entrepreneurship Promotion","During this Plan period, more effective approaches will be undertaken to promote innovation-driven entrepreneurship by entrepreneurs with industry or academia track records.",""],[1,"193","1","Private Sector Venture Bidding and Government Equity Divestment","invite the private sector to bid for the rights to the ventures.",""],[1,"193","6","General Entrepreneurship Training Rationalisation","General entrepreneurship training is currently fragmented and will therefore be rationalised.",""],[1,"193","6","Bumiputera Entrepreneurship Talent Development Programme","MARA will continue to be the lead agency for building general Bumiputera entrepreneurship talent.",""],[1,"194","1","Sector-Specific Technical Programmes by Industry Development Organisations","MARA's programmes will be supplemented by sector specific technical programmes conducted by industry development organisations (IDOs) such as Malaysian Biotechnology Corporation and Multimedia Development Corporation.",""]],"158":[[1,"189","3","Bumiputera High-Paying Jobs Representation Initiative","Promoting Bumiputera representation in high paying jobs through enhanced capability building and demand-side incentives.",""],[1,"196","1","Bumiputera Talent Development and Incentive Programme","more focused programmes will be implemented to build talent and put in place appropriate incentives to enable more Bumiputera representation especially in key management, professional and technical positions.",""],[1,"196","2","Postgraduate Scholarship Expansion for Talented Bumiputera","During the Plan period, the number of scholarships will be increased for postgraduate programmes in renowned institutions.",""],[1,"196","4","Industry Centres of Excellence","The Government will establish industry centres of excellence to provide research and postgraduate training, which will be done in collaboration with industry associations and existing research institutes or institutes of higher learning.",""],[1,"196","5","Bumiputera Attachment and Overseas Secondment Expansion","The number of Bumiputera in attachment programmes and on overseas secondment programmes will also be increased to broaden Bumiputera exposure to higher value-added businesses, build international business experience and enable international professional networks to be forged.",""],[1,"196","5","Balanced Employment and Training Conditions for Large Government Contracts and FDI Incentives","Companies that secure large Government contracts, as well as local and foreign investors who are the recipients of pre-package special incentives under the provision of foreign direct investment incentive schemes, will be asked to commit to balanced employment targets, training programmes or attachment/ secondment programmes, especially to increase Bumiputera participation at international level.",""],[1,"196","5","GLIC Partnership Attachment and Secondment Programmes","In addition, GLICs will establish similar programmes with their major business partners and overseas acquisitions.",""]],"159":[[1,"197","1","Rural Treated Water and Sanitation Provision","efforts will be made during the Plan period to ensure that the rakyat, particularly those in rural communities, are provided with adequate supply of treated water and sanitation facilities, access to road networks,",""],[1,"198","2","Rural Treated Water Supply Expansion","More intensive efforts will be undertaken to increase the extent of treated water in rural areas by upgrading and building new pipelines and water treatment plants.",""],[1,"198","2","Rural Water Service Maintenance and Quality Improvement","Measures will also be intensified to improve services and maintenance to ensure water quality and sustainable supply.",""],[1,"198","2","Alternative Rural Water Supply Systems","Alternative systems such as gravity systems, tube wells, underground water and rain harvest will be used in remote and isolated areas.",""],[1,"199","7","Clean and Treated Water Supply Expansion","Supplying clean and treated water through additional connections and other alternative solutions;",""],[1,"200","2","Water Treatment Plant Construction Programme","A total of 11 water treatment plants are under construction, whilst 70,180 houses will be expected to be connected to treated water supply by 2010.",""]],"160":[[1,"198","1","Rural Road Network Expansion and Upgrading","Moving forward, the Government will focus on the expansion and upgrading of rural road networks.",""],[1,"199","6","Rural Road Construction and Upgrading","Building and upgrading of roads to connect rural areas to social and economic centres;",""]],"161":[[1,"199","3","Basic Rural Transport Services Improvement","The provision of basic rural transport services, such as air and water transportation, will be further improved to increase connectivity and accessibility for rural populations especially in Sabah and Sarawak.",""],[1,"199","3","Rural Bus Route Expansion","In Peninsular Malaysia, new stage-bus routes and new express buses between rural centres and towns will meet the needs of the rural population for efficient, affordable and safe transport.",""]],"162":[[1,"199","4","Rural Basic Infrastructure Improvement","To ensure that focused efforts will be made towards improving access to basic infrastructure, the Government has selected rural basic infrastructure",""],[1,"199","5","Rural Basic Infrastructure Improvement Initiative","The Rural Basic Infrastructure NKRA aims to improve the provision of basic infrastructure for the rakyat living in rural areas through:",""],[1,"200","1","Rural Basic Infrastructure Delivery Acceleration","increased efforts will be made to accelerate the delivery of basic infrastructure in rural areas.",""],[1,"200","2","Rural Basic Infrastructure Expansion Programme","Work has commenced on increasing road coverage by 500 kilometres in Peninsular Malaysia, Sabah and Sarawak, whilst 86 kilometres of roads has already been completed.",""],[1,"200","4","Integrated Rural Infrastructure Development Planning Platform","Utilising developmental plans as a platform for integrating the planning and implementation of rural infrastructure development programmes;",""]],"163":[[1,"201","2","Employment Composition Disclosure Requirement","employers will be asked to disclose their employment composition by major inclusiveness elements such as gender and ethnicity to the Securities Commission (for listed companies) or the Companies Commission of Malaysia (for all other companies) to enable the Government to better track Malaysia's overall progress on these measures.",""]],"164":[[1,"203","4","Support Services for Women in Challenging Circumstances","Improving provision of support for women in challenging circumstances such as widows, single mothers and those with lower incomes;",""]],"165":[[1,"203","8","Gender Sensitisation Implementation Committee","A special committee, chaired by the Minister of Women, Family and Community Development, will be established to implement gender sensitisation","Ministry of Women, Family and Community Development"],[1,"204","1","Women’s Representation in Decision-Making Positions Programme","The Government will also increase its efforts to achieve a quota of at least 30% of decision-making positions to be held by women during the Plan period.",""],[1,"204","2","Nur Bestari Leadership and Capability Development Training Programme","Leadership and capability development will continue to be promoted under the Nur Bestari training programme.",""],[1,"204","2","Specialised Training Courses for Women in the Public Sector","In addition, specialised training courses for women in key areas such as politics, management and motivation will be developed to improve confidence and soft skills for women employed in the public sector.",""],[1,"204","2","Women’s Advancement in Managerial and Key Positions","Private sector and NGOs will also be encouraged to increase the participation of women in managerial and key positions.",""],[1,"204","5","Gender Sensitisation and Women's Rights Education Programme","Women's rights and gender sensitisation programmes will continue to be expanded to educate women about their right and recourse for justice.",""]],"166":[[1,"203","7","Special Training and Re-skilling Window under the Human Resource Development Fund","Training and re-skilling opportunities will also be provided through a special window under the Human Resource Development Fund.",""]],"167":[[1,"204","4","Rural HIV Prevention Awareness Campaigns","Health awareness programmes such as on HIV prevention will continue to be promoted in rural areas with the cooperation of Ministry of Health and NGOS.","Ministry of Health"]],"168":[[1,"206","5","Youth Preventive and Rehabilitative Programmes","Preventive and rehabilitative programmes will be improved and broadened to better shape the identity of youth and enhance their outlook on life whilst strengthening their discipline to avoid social ills such as crime and drug addiction and associating with groups involved with such social ills.",""],[1,"207","1","Youth Crime Prevention Expansion","on discouraging youth involvement in criminal activities, will be expanded to support the reduction of street crime.",""]],"169":[[1,"234","6","Primary and Secondary School Curriculum Reform","During the Plan period, a new curriculum for primary and secondary schools will be introduced.",""],[1,"235","1","Secondary School Curriculum Reform","a new curriculum for secondary schools.",""],[1,"235","2","1Malaysia Curriculum Integration","The new curriculum will incorporate the principles of 1Malaysia in the pedagogical approach to deliver education.",""],[1,"235","2","School Sports Curriculum Expansion","the new curriculum will include Sports as a subject beginning 2011.",""],[1,"235","2","1Student, 1Sports Participation Policy","Under the '1Student, 1Sports' policy, each student is required to take",""]],"170":[[1,"235","4","Private Education Public-Private Partnership Expansion","During the Plan period, private providers will be encouraged to deliver education at all stages from the pre-school to tertiary levels.",""],[1,"235","4","Public-Private Partnership in Education Provision","The Government will implement various modes of public-private partnership in the provision of the",""],[1,"236","6","Trust School Framework","the Government will introduce the Trust School framework for selected existing public schools.",""],[1,"237","1","Trust Schools Programme","Trust Schools are public schools that are managed jointly by private partners and civil service school leaders, under the umbrella of the Ministry of Education.","Ministry of Education"],[1,"237","2","Trust Schools Autonomy and Performance Management Reform","Trust Schools will have extensive decision-making rights over curriculum, finance and human resources to encourage innovation and responsiveness to the needs of their individual school communities.",""]],"171":[[1,"239","4","TEVT Cost-Sharing Financing Arrangement","Therefore, the intention is for costs associated with TEVT to be shared among government, employers, the industry and individual students according to the benefits obtained.",""],[1,"245","3","TEVT Funding Review and Performance-Based Allocation","The current funding approach of TEVT will be reviewed to enhance the effectiveness and efficiency of public TEVT institutions.",""],[1,"245","3","Student Financial Assistance for Skills Certificate Study","The Government will also provide financial assistance to students to study at Malaysian Skills Certificate Level 3 and above at high-performing public TEVT institutions.",""],[1,"245","3","Performance Rating System for TEVT Institutions","Towards this end, a system will be introduced to rate the performance of public and private TEVT institutions.",""],[1,"245","4","TEVT Institution Performance-Based Student Placement Financing","The performance rating of TEVT institutions will be utilised when making decisions for buying places, where the Government finances students to study in private TEVT institutions.",""],[1,"245","6","National Dual Training System for School Dropouts","The National Dual Training System (NDTS) aims to expand the current curricula and provide specialised training to coaches to cater to the needs of school dropouts.",""],[1,"245","7","Workplace Training Expansion in TEVT Curriculum","Therefore, in addition to institutional training, workplace training will be strongly encouraged during the Plan period as part of TEVT curriculum, since it provides:",""]],"172":[[1,"246","8","Graduate Competency Improvement Initiative","Hence, concerted efforts will be undertaken to improve the competency of graduates, as well as enhance the funding cost- effectiveness of higher education through:",""],[1,"246","11","Course Curriculum Upgrading for Academic and Soft Skills Balance","Upgrading course curricula to balance academic content and soft skills;",""],[1,"247","1","Industrial Attachments and Market-Oriented Course Reform","In addition, market orientation of courses will be improved to ease student transition into the labour market and improve overall student employability.",""],[1,"247","1","Public-Private Collaboration in Education Provision","The involvement of the private sector in the provision of education through public-private collaboration will be improved to encourage industry participation in course provision and industrial attachments.",""],[1,"247","2","Standard Policy Framework for Structured Industrial Attachment Programmes","A standard policy framework for structured industrial attachment programmes will be implemented for higher education institutions in collaboration with industry players to improve the effectiveness of such programmes.",""],[1,"247","4","Knowledge Transfer Partnership Programme","the Knowledge Transfer Partnership (KTP) programme will be introduced in 2011 to facilitate collaboration between industry and relevant universities.",""],[1,"247","5","University International Research Collaboration Initiative","Universities will be encouraged to develop strategic collaborations with international research institutions and foreign universities to enhance research and development (R&D) activities, especially in new emerging technologies by:",""],[1,"247","7","University Intellectual Property Management Strengthening","Strengthening management of intellectual property developed in universities to improve the governance of research activities;",""],[1,"248","1","University Centres of Excellence Industrial R&D Collaboration","Strengthening centres of excellence in universities through industrial collaboration in R&D activities to support and accelerate the commercialisation of innovations and new technology.",""],[1,"250","3","Higher Education Curriculum and Programme Review","During the Plan period, higher education institutions will undertake an exercise to review their curricula and courses and seek to align programme and learning outcomes with requirements of industry and employers.",""],[1,"250","5","Malaysian Qualifications Framework Domain Incorporation","Incorporation of domains as stipulated in the Malaysian Qualifications Framework that includes soft skills, such as positive work ethics, communications, teamwork, and decision making and leadership skills.",""],[1,"250","7","Tertiary Curriculum Soft Skills Enhancement","the curriculum of tertiary institutions must place greater emphasis on soft skills development of students.",""],[1,"250","7","My3S Graduate Soft Skills Assessment","The Generic Students' Attributes self-assessment test, also known as the Malaysia Soft Skill Scale or My3S, will be introduced as an instrument to assess graduate competency in soft skills, beginning in July 2010.",""],[1,"251","1","Malaysian Qualifications Framework Implementation and International Benchmarking","continue to play a crucial role in implementing the Malaysian Qualifications Framework as a basis for quality assurance of higher education and as the reference point for the criteria and standards for national qualifications.",""],[1,"251","1","MQA Staff Capacity Building and Foreign Quality Assurance Collaboration","The MQA will also expand its collaboration with foreign quality assurance agencies by signing Memorandums of Arrangement to benchmark standards and help to raise the capabilities of its staff.",""],[1,"258","1","Graduate Employability Bridging Programme","This bridging programme aims to provide recent graduates with specific skills and the right competencies as well as industry-relevant capabilities to improve their employability.",""],[1,"258","2","University-Industry Career Building and Coaching Collaboration","Collaboration on career building and coaching between universities and industry to enhance graduate employability will be encouraged.",""],[1,"258","2","Graduate Employability Management Scheme","The Graduate Employability Management Scheme (GEMS), managed by the Putrajaya Committee for Government-Linked-Company High Perfor- mance, will continue to be implemented and expanded to enhance the employability of unemployed graduates.",""],[1,"259","1","Community College Modular Training Programmes","During the Plan period, the Government will implement a new and innovative approach for community colleges by rolling out modular programmes that allow students to complete multiple short modules at their own pace.",""]],"173":[[1,"250","6","Polytechnic Restructuring and Specialisation Programme","all polytechnics in Malaysia will be restructured to offer courses at diploma and degree levels while phasing out courses at certificate level by the end of the Plan period.",""],[1,"250","6","Premier Polytechnic Upgrade and Applied Research Initiative","Three existing polytechnics will be upgraded to premier polytechnics to undertake applied research through collaboration with the relevant industry to nurture innovation and create home-grown new technologies.",""]],"174":[[1,"253","3","Comprehensive Labour Social Safety Net","This has made the case even more compelling for establishing a comprehensive labour social safety net to support displaced workers.",""],[1,"253","4","Fund for Loss of Employment","Fund for Loss of Employment will be introduced to provide financial assistance for workers who do not get due compensation from their employers upon retrenchment.",""]],"175":[[1,"259","2","Global Talent Attraction and Retention Efforts","Concerted efforts will be undertaken to improve the attractiveness of",""],[1,"259","4","Skilled Foreign Talent Hiring Procedure Simplification","The Government will improve the current procedures for approving the hiring of skilled foreign talent in Malaysia to enhance the flexibility and reduce the complexity, the number of stages and regulatory bodies involved.",""],[1,"259","5","Skilled Foreign Talent Incentive and Employment Condition Reform","To further attract skilled foreign talent, incentives and employment conditions will be improved.",""],[1,"260","1","Flexible Employment Visa for Skilled Foreign Talent","For skilled foreign talent earning more than RM8,000 per month, there will be no time limit for their employment visa, to allow for greater flexibility and mobility.",""],[1,"260","1","Open Visa Scheme for Highly Skilled Foreign Professionals","Open visas will be issued to highly skilled foreign professionals, without the need for the visa to be tied to or conditional upon employment with a particular company or employer.",""],[1,"260","1","Residential Property Access for Skilled Foreign Professionals","They will also be allowed to acquire residential units costings RM250,000 and above.",""],[1,"260","2","Liberalisation of Skilled Professional Entry under AFAS","By 2015, under the ASEAN Framework Agreement on Services (AFAS), Malaysia together with other ASEAN member countries will liberalise the entry of skilled professionals.",""],[1,"261","1","Review of Mandatory Return Requirement for Foreign Graduates","the existing mandatory procedures requiring them to return to their home countries immediately after completing their studies will be reviewed to facilitate their employment in Malaysia, particularly in critical areas.",""],[1,"261","2","International Postgraduate and Post-Doctoral Scholarship Programme","Scholarships will be given to the best students from across the world to pursue postgraduate and post-doctoral studies in Malaysia in fields critical for the nation.",""],[1,"261","3","STPM Top Student Scholarship Programme","During the Plan period, the top 5% of students every year for the Malaysian Higher School Certificate (STPM) will be provided with scholarships to pursue further studies in local universities.",""],[1,"261","3","Final-Year Fee Sponsorship for Overseas Top Students","The Government will also identify top Malaysian students studying in the renowned foreign universities and will provide sponsorship for their final year fees on condition they return to serve.",""],[1,"261","3","Scholarship Return-to-Malaysia Compliance Measures","In addition, steps will be taken to ensure Malaysians studying overseas on scholarships return to Malaysia upon completion of their studies.",""],[1,"261","4","Talent Identification and Engagement of Malaysians Abroad","The Government will undertake consistent efforts to identify talented Malaysians",""],[1,"262","2","Malaysian Diaspora Engagement and Database Initiative","The Malaysian diaspora will be actively engaged to build and strengthen relationships.",""],[1,"262","3","Malaysian Diaspora Recognition Awards and Events","A set of highly regarded awards and events will be created to recognise and celebrate significant achievements by members of the Malaysian diaspora community.",""],[1,"262","3","Malaysian Diaspora Associations Network","Malaysian diaspora associations will be established to provide networking opportunities via both online channels as well as physical chapters in cities with the largest concentrations of Malaysians abroad to provide greater visibility on the activities and opportunities for them;",""],[1,"262","4","Diaspora Dialogue Mechanism","Regular dialogues will be set up between government representatives and the Malaysian diaspora in major cities, where members of the diaspora",""],[1,"262","6","Malaysian Diaspora Investment Promotion","The Government will encourage the Malaysian diaspora to invest in Malaysia.",""],[1,"262","7","Talent Corporation for Global Talent Attraction","a new Talent Corporation (TC) will be established in 2011 under the Prime Minister's Department with the mandate to attract, motivate and retain the talent needed for a high-income economy.","Prime Minister's Department"],[1,"263","1","National Talent Management Initiatives","The TC will develop and drive specific catalytic and innovative national talent management initiatives to attract and develop world-class talent in collaboration with both the public and private sectors.",""],[1,"263","1","Malaysian Diaspora Talent Engagement Initiative","This will include initiatives to engage the Malaysian diaspora, to actively identify and convene high potential Malaysian talent pools, to uncover 'hidden gems' and accelerate the development of top young leaders in Malaysia;",""],[1,"263","2","National Talent Management Coordination and Support Mechanism","The TC will facilitate industry and private sector efforts in creating, motivating and retaining a skilled workforce.",""],[1,"263","3","National Talent Initiative Delivery and Tracking Mechanism","The TC will be responsible for ensuring the delivery of major national initiatives on talent across the human capital development pipeline to develop and retain talent in Malaysia and to address the biggest gaps and bottle-necks in the 'flow' and 'stock' of talent.",""],[1,"263","4","Integrated National Talent Blueprint","The TC, in collaboration with the public and private sectors, will jointly develop an integrated National Talent Blueprint by 2011, which will identify and quantify talent needs of priority economic sectors over time, and develop specific initiatives to accelerate the pipeline of these types of critical talent.",""],[1,"264","2","Integrated Talent Pipeline and Programme Governance Portfolio","Contain a detailed fact base of the talent pipeline for all priority sectors and NKEAs, a quantification of supply and demand gaps in the present and the future, an integrated portfolio of initiatives to ensure delivery and the necessary programme governance.",""],[1,"264","3","Foreign Talent and Diaspora Attraction Strategy","The TC will collaborate with the Immigration Department and Malaysian missions to actively plan and execute strategies to attract foreign talent and the diaspora to Malaysia, especially those with expertise in priority economic sectors","Immigration Department | Malaysian missions"],[1,"264","4","Skilled Foreign Talent Recruitment and Scouting Initiative","In addition to broad initiatives such as conducting road shows and organising career fairs for skilled talent, the Government will also scout, identify, and tap individual skilled foreign talent that can meet specific skills or knowledge shortfalls in Malaysia.",""],[1,"264","5","Talent Attraction and Retention Programme Consolidation","Existing talent attraction and retention programmes such as the Returning Expert Programme and the Brain Gain Programme will be consolidated under the TC and enhanced to ensure better co-ordination, more focus and greater impact.",""],[1,"264","5","Talent Incentive Review and Expansion","The incentives under these programmes will be reviewed and expanded to make them even more attractive to the targeted talent groups overseas.",""],[1,"265","4","Talent Corporation for Strategic Talent Sourcing","The TC will be established with the primary mandate to source and deliver top talent from overseas and within the country, that are most critical for the key economic sectors.",""]],"176":[[1,"269","1","Urban and Rural Quality of Life Improvement","The Government is committed to ensuring a high quality of life in urban and rural areas in line with Malaysia's aspiration to become a developed nation.",""]],"177":[[1,"270","6","Efficient Public Utilities and Services Improvement","Providing efficient public utilities and services.",""]],"178":[[1,"272","5","Urban Conurbation Growth Concentration Strategy","Recognising this, the Government will pursue a strategy of concentrating growth in urban conurbations.",""],[1,"274","7","Second National Physical Plan Finalisation","the second National Physical Plan (NPP) will be finalised by 2010 to set out the strategic direction and priorities of physical development of Peninsular Malaysia.",""],[1,"274","7","State Structural Plans for Sabah and Sarawak","the development strategies for Sabah and Sarawak will be outlined in their respective state structural plans.",""],[1,"277","1","Compact Urban Development Promotion","In order to accommodate growth, compact urban development will be encouraged.",""],[1,"277","2","Compact City Growth Management Mechanisms","the Government will facilitate better use of mechanisms for managing growth such as zoning, urban growth boundaries, growth control regulations and other development incentives.",""],[1,"278","2","Human-Scale City Planning Approach","City planning will promote a human-scale development approach.",""],[1,"278","3","Mixed-Use Neighbourhood Development and Zoning Reform","This will be achieved through encouraging mixed-use developments in neighbourhoods, combining residential, retail and office uses.",""]],"179":[[1,"278","4","Transit-Oriented Development Promotion","Transit-oriented development will be encouraged",""],[1,"279","1","Transit Corridor Development Management","Where there are high capacity rail stations, these areas will be identified as transit corridors, where development will be managed to encourage higher densities with a vibrant mix of uses that will unlock the value of development that comes with increased accessibility.",""],[1,"279","2","Integration of Land Use and Transportation Planning","Integration of land use and transportation plans in shifting towards compact and efficient cities will be an important component of Local Plans.",""],[1,"286","5","Integrated Transport and Land Use Planning","During the Tenth Plan period, the Government will continue its efforts to strengthen its approach to transportation planning, integrating public transport and land use development in all national, regional and local development master plans.",""]],"180":[[1,"275","19","Waste-to-Energy Initiatives","Waste is a resource to be recycled and reused, for example via waste-to-energy initiatives",""]],"181":[[1,"285","7","Transport Industry Regulatory Restructuring","Regulatory restructuring of the transport industry;",""],[1,"285","8","Private Vehicle Demand Management","Managing demand to reduce private vehicle usage.",""],[1,"286","11","Monitoring and Enforcement Regime","Establishing a robust monitoring and enforcement regime.",""],[1,"287","2","National Land Public Transport Master Plan Development and Monitoring","Developing and monitoring the implementation of a 20-year National Land Public Transport Master Plan, along with region- specific master plans to identify macro-level",""],[1,"287","3","Land Public Transport Fund","A land public transport fund, created under the Land Public Transport Bill, 2010, will be operated by SPAD for improving land public transport and providing land public transport services for rural development.",""],[1,"287","7","Central Land Public Transport Planning and Consultation Mechanism","Central planner for land public transport (with administrative integration of trans- port and spatial planning) · SPAD as part of state's one-stop centre · SPAD to be consulted for alternatives to (OSC) new expressways",""],[1,"287","9","Operator Licensing Reform","Move to operator licensing only",""],[1,"287","9","KPI-Based Licensing Framework","KPI-based licensing framework",""],[1,"287","9","Fare Review Mechanism","Regular review of fares in line with competition framework",""],[1,"287","11","Operator Standards Enforcement","Greater enforcement of operator standards in collaboration with other traffic enforcement authorities",""],[1,"287","13","Ring-Fenced Public Transport Improvement Fund","Dedicated fund ring-fenced for public transport improvements",""],[1,"288","2","Public Transport Operating Framework Reform","Establishing a new operating framework for public transport operators starting with the introduction of a fare regime that will enable financial self-sufficiency for private operators while preserving affordability for commuters and ensuring continuous improvements in service standards.",""],[1,"288","4","Expansion Review of SPAD Scope to Sabah and Sarawak","Pending successful implementation in Peninsular Malaysia, the Government will review the potential of expanding SPAD's scope to Sabah and Sarawak.",""],[1,"288","6","Land Public Transport Regulatory Revamp","with the formation of SPAD, the land public transport structure will be revamped to improve regulation of the industry including planning, licensing, fare regulation and enforcement.",""]],"182":[[1,"290","3","Electrified Double-Track Rail Extension Project","The 197-km extension of the electrified double- track project (DTP) from Gemas to Johor Bahru will increase KTM's track capacity by 5 to 10 times and allow for significant reduction in journey times.",""],[1,"290","4","Rail Service Modernisation and Rural Access Enhancement","In the east coast of Peninsular Malaysia and Sabah, rail services will be enhanced by modernisation of facilities and technologies to increase access to rural areas.",""],[1,"290","5","Public Transport Interconnectivity and Access Improvement","Efforts will be directed towards increasing the percentage of one-way journeys completed within one hour and with fewer than four transfers.",""],[1,"290","5","Pedestrian and Transit Station Upgrade Programme","The Government, in collaboration with relevant agencies, will improve the pedestrian experience by increasing the number of bus stops closer to homes, upgrading pedestrian walkways so that they are covered, wide, safe and adequately lit as well as upgrading major rail and bus stations.",""],[1,"290","6","Multimodal Transfer Hub Development","During the Plan period, connectivity across different modes of public transport will be improved through the establishment of multi- modal transfer hubs for services within cities, from suburban areas into cities as well as for intercity travel.",""],[1,"291","1","City Centre Bus Hub Upgrading Programme","the upgrading of 14 Hentian Akhir Bandar (HAB) or city centre bus hubs, two inter-urban transport terminals to facilitate the flow of bus services from satellite cities surrounding the Kuala Lumpur city centre.",""],[1,"291","2","Integrated Cashless Ticketing System","An integrated cashless ticketing system will be introduced across all 16 public transport operators in Greater KL, eliminating the need for multiple tickets across various operators and shortening journey times.",""],[1,"291","2","Public Transport Passenger Information System","Passengers will be provided with easily accessible information on stations and journey schedules to improve the ease of using public transport.",""],[1,"291","2","Bus Stop Scheduling Information Upgrade","Bus stops will be upgraded to display scheduling information for all bus operators and a central website established to display public transport-related information across all modes.",""]],"183":[[1,"291","3","Land Public Transport Regulatory Restructuring","With regulatory restructuring, land public transport operators including taxis will be subjected",""],[1,"291","4","Integrated Transport Information System Upgrade for Public Transport Monitoring","The Integrated Transport Information System (ITIS) in Greater KL will be upgraded into the performance hub for land public transport monitoring and enforcement efforts through the usage of closed-circuit televisions (CCTVs) and global positioning system (GPS) trackers on buses.",""],[1,"291","5","Land Public Transport Performance Monitoring Regime","Key performance indicators (KPIs) for land public transport operators, such as on-time performance, condition of equipment and reliability will be established.",""],[1,"291","5","Heavy Vehicle CBD Entry Restriction Enforcement","The Government will also strengthen enforcement of existing laws restricting the entry of heavy vehicles into the Central Business District (CBD) area during peak hours to reduce congestion through joint enforcement initiatives by SPAD, the Road Transport Department and the traffic police.",""],[1,"332","2","Public Transport Licensing and Operating Framework Restructuring","Restructuring of the public transport licensing and operating framework to be led by the commission for land public transport or SPAD, and supported by major investments in public transport such as the introduction of the mass rapid transit system in Greater KL;",""],[1,"357","8","Land Public Transport Commission Consolidation","The commission for land public transport or SPAD has been established as the single-point of accountability for land public transport planning and regulatory functions.",""]],"184":[[1,"302","2","Housing Maintenance Fund","the Government will establish a Housing Maintenance Fund with an initial funding of RM500 million to assist the residents of both public and private low-cost housing units.",""],[1,"302","2","Tabung Perumahan 1Malaysia Maintenance Support Fund","This is in addition to the fund known as Tabung Perumahan 1Malaysia, established in February 2010 that provides support for the maintenance and major repairs of low-cost private housing in Kuala Lumpur with contributions from the Government and a number of large private corporations.",""],[1,"332","3","Housing Maintenance Fund","Major shifts in housing policies with a new emphasis on the entire life-cycle of housing provision from construction to maintenance, with the introduction of a Housing Maintenance Fund;",""]],"185":[[1,"301","3","Green Building Design Integration in Housing","housing design will need to incorporate Green Building design elements and technology.",""],[1,"302","4","Green Township Guidelines and Rating System","Environmentally friendly townships and neighbourhoods will be encouraged through the introduction of Green Guidelines and a Green Rating System.",""],[1,"302","4","Flagship Green Townships in Putrajaya and Cyberjaya","Putrajaya and Cyberjaya will be the flagship Green Townships.",""],[1,"302","4","Green Building Tax Incentive Review","The Government will review tax incentives, such as tax breaks for buildings and designs that are environmentally friendly, incorporating green design elements like solar panels for heating, rain water harvesting facilities and water conservation features.",""],[1,"302","4","Green Community Spaces in Housing Projects","There will also be focus on creating public community spaces within housing projects that are well-landscaped and equipped with basic",""],[1,"322","4","Green Building Tax Incentives","The Government will also implement tax incentives such as tax breaks for buildings and designs that work harmoniously with nature;",""],[1,"322","5","Green Township Guidelines and Rating Scale Roll-out","The Government will initiate green townships in Putrajaya and Cyberjaya with guidelines and rating scales based on carbon footprint.",""],[1,"327","4","Green Township Guidelines and Rating Scale Initiative","Introduction of guidelines for green townships and rating scales based on carbon footprint baseline and promoting such townships starting with Putrajaya and Cyberjaya",""]],"186":[[1,"304","1","Public Utilities Service Improvement","The provision of essential public utilities in terms of both quality of service and coverage will be strengthened.",""],[1,"332","1","Systematic Restructuring and Investment in Essential Services","the nation has recognised this, and will embark on a systematic restructuring of and investment in the provision of essential services, including:",""],[1,"333","1","World-Class Urban Infrastructure Support","Denser growth in cities will be managed and supported by world-class infrastructure.",""]],"187":[[1,"304","8","Integrated Water Cycle Resource Management Reassessment","Malaysia will reassess the management of its resources across the entire water cycle - from where water is drawn, to how water is treated and supplied to citizens and how wastewater is returned to the environment.",""],[1,"304","9","Long-Term Water Resource Management Strategy","Developing a long-term strategy for water resource management to achieve water security;",""],[1,"305","2","National Water Resources Policy","During the Plan period, the National Water Resources Policy (NWRP) will chart the future course for the sector.",""],[1,"305","3","Integrated Water Resources and River Basin Management Expansion","Other measures to be implemented during the Plan period include expanding the implementation of the Integrated Water Resources Management and Integrated River Basin Management approaches in planning, managing, protecting and rehabilitating water resources.",""],[1,"305","3","Flood Mitigation Programme Financing","The Government will provide RM5 billion for flood mitigation programmes.",""],[1,"305","3","Integrated Flood Management and Preparedness Measures","This includes the application of the Integrated Flood Management approach to manage the risks of flood damage through forecasting and warning facilities as well as the development of disaster preparedness and community awareness programmes and flood hazard maps.",""],[1,"305","3","Water Resources Research and Development Intensification","In addition, research and development efforts will be intensified in area of conservation of water resources to support efforts to develop a sustainable water sector for the national economy.",""]],"188":[[1,"309","5","Electricity Supply Security Measures","Efforts to ensure continued security of electricity supply will focus on a number of areas.",""],[1,"310","1","Alternative Energy Supply Diversification","The development of alternative sources of energy, particularly hydro as well as importation of coal and liquefied natural gas (LNG) by 2015 will improve security of supply.",""],[1,"310","1","Super-Critical Coal Technology Exploration","To further reduce carbon emissions, super-critical coal technology will be explored for new generation investments.",""],[1,"310","1","Nuclear Energy Feasibility and Capacity-Building Programme","Given the scale and scope of this effort, a detailed feasibility study will be carried out together with the necessary training of human capital and awareness campaigns to increase the public's understanding and acceptance of nuclear energy.",""],[1,"310","3","Hydroelectric Power Plant Commissioning","Two hydroelectric plants will be commissioned during the Plan period in Ulu Jelai and Hulu Terengganu with a combined capacity of 622 MW;",""],[1,"310","4","New Power Plant Commissioning in Sabah","Three new power plants will be commissioned with a combined capacity of 700 MW.",""],[1,"310","6","Bakun Hydroelectric Project Commissioning","The 2,400 MW Bakun Hydroelectric Project will be commissioned in stages.",""],[1,"310","7","Transmission and Distribution System Strengthening and Expansion","Transmission and distribution systems will be strengthened and expanded.",""],[1,"310","7","New Electricity Transmission Projects","New transmission projects that will be implemented include overhead lines from Bentong South to Kampung Pandan via Ampang East in Peninsular Malaysia, from the Bakun Hydroelectric Project to Similajau in Sarawak and other transmission projects in Sabah.",""],[1,"310","7","Smart Grid Feasibility Review","The potential of implementing a Smart Grid system will also be reviewed to minimise losses, reduce costs and increase reliability.",""],[1,"311","2","Utility Service Delivery Acceleration","Delivery of services by utilities to new and existing customers will be accelerated through the use of new technologies and performance-based regulations.",""]],"189":[[1,"311","3","Household Broadband Expansion Initiative","To capture this opportunity the Government has set a target of raising household broadband penetration to 75% by the end of 2015.",""],[1,"343","2","Rural Internet Access Centres","Centres providing Internet access will be established as community and business centres in rural communities.",""]],"190":[[1,"312","11","Sanitary Waste Collection System","Sanitary handling with modern trucks and standardised bins for collection",""],[1,"313","4","Waste Collection Service Improvement and Sanitary Handling Upgrade","Collection frequency will increase, for example to twice a week for households and seven times a week for wet markets.",""],[1,"313","4","Service Quality Monitoring Against Specific Targets","the level of service will be monitored against specific targets across all areas.",""],[1,"313","5","Shared Premises Cleaning and Maintenance Programme","Under this effort over 5,600 shared premises including wet markets, parks, food courts and other such facilities will be provided frequent and",""]],"191":[[1,"314","2","Unsanitary Landfill Closure and Rehabilitation Programme","The Government will close and rehabilitate the existing 112 unsanitary landfills across the nation and upgrade some of them to sanitary landfills.",""],[1,"314","2","Waste Treatment and Recovery Facilities Development","In addition, transfer stations, integrated material recovery facilities, sanitary landfills and other disposal and treatment facilities will be built.",""],[1,"314","2","Separate Collection for Bulky, Garden and Recyclable Waste","Separate collection will be done for bulky waste, garden waste and recyclables from the rest of the household solid waste to facilitate recycling anc recovery of waste.",""],[1,"326","11","Solid Waste Management Efficiency Enhancement","The Government will continue efforts to enhance the efficiency and effectiveness of solid waste management, which will also lead to the reduction of GHGs emission.",""],[1,"326","11","Material Recovery Facilities and Thermal Treatment Plants","Among measures that will be undertaken include building material recovery facilities and thermal treatment plants as well as recycling of non-organic waste.",""],[1,"326","11","Organic Waste Segregation and Composting","The segregation of organic material from waste can be turned into compost or used for other purposes.",""],[1,"328","1","Holistic Solid Waste Management through Sanitary Landfills","A holistic management of solid waste through sanitary landfills will help recover the methane produced from the waste and use it to generate energy.",""]],"192":[[1,"318","1","National CCTV Surveillance Network Expansion","The Government is rolling out 496 Closed Circuit Television (CCTV) cameras in hot spot areas across Malaysia.",""],[1,"318","1","CCTV Integration with Police Control Centres","These will be linked to PDRM's control centres so that the police can respond rapidly to incidents.",""],[1,"318","1","Expansion of Existing CCTV Network Connectivity","The possibility of connecting the network of several thousand existing CCTV cameras, many of which are in the transport system, to PDRM control centres will also be explored.",""],[1,"318","3","Safe Cities Programme","The Safe Cities Programme will be given added emphasis.",""],[1,"318","4","Safe City Initiative","Each local programme group will decide on the actions to take based on their local priorities and the funding they have available.",""],[1,"319","3","Pedestrian Walkway Separation and Safety Infrastructure","Separation of pedestrian walkways from motor vehicles lanes through construction of dedicated walkways, bollards, railings or hedging",""],[1,"319","6","Crime Prevention Through Environmental Design","Implement crime prevention through environmental design",""],[1,"319","10","Closed Circuit Television Installation Programme","Installation of Closed Circuit Television (CCTV) in commercial, housing and public places",""],[1,"319","12","Lighting for Residential and Commercial Lanes","Lighting side, front and back lanes of houses and shop houses",""],[1,"319","17","Small Business Activity Generation at Vulnerable Crime Spots","Generate small business activities at vulnerable crime spots",""],[1,"319","18","Housing Area Surveillance Improvement","Improve surveillance in housing areas (through Rukun Tetangga or private security firms)",""],[1,"319","19","Safe City Status Websites","Set up safe city status websites at local authority",""]],"193":[[1,"319","21","Police Station League Table Transparency Initiative","Police performance will be made more transparent through the new Balai or Police Station League Table launched in March 2010, which will show each Balai's performance in reducing crime.",""],[1,"319","23","Police Service Satisfaction and Safety Survey Programme","Surveys to measure satisfaction with the police service as well as to measure the sense of safety of Malaysians will also be conducted periodically.",""],[1,"347","6","Police Station Performance Ranking System","Police stations will be transparently ranked along three dimensions of public satisfaction: response time, ease of making a report and effectiveness in reducing crime;",""]],"194":[[1,"320","4","AFFIRM Framework for Environmental Sustainability","the Government has introduced the AFFIRM framework, which outlines the government's approach towards creating a comprehensive ecosystem for environmental sustainability",""],[1,"321","9","Legislative and Policy Streamlining and Coordination","Streamline and coordinate across existing legislation and policies",""],[1,"321","11","Inter-Ministerial and Cross-Sectoral Adaptation Committee","Establish inter-ministerial and cross-sectoral committee to drive and facilitate implementation of adaptation",""],[1,"322","1","AFFIRM Environmental Sustainability Framework","the Prime Minister introduced the AFFIRM framework of Awareness, Faculty, Finance, Infrastructure, Research and Marketing to develop a complete ecosystem for environmental sustainability.",""],[1,"323","2","Climate Resilient Growth Roadmap","Developing a roadmap for climate resilient growth;",""],[1,"323","4","Climate Change Adaptation Strategy","During the Plan period, Malaysia will adopt a dual strategy in addressing climate change impacts: firstly, adaptation strategies to protect economic growth and development factors from the impact of climate change; and secondly, mitigation strategies to reduce emission of greenhouse gases (GHGs).",""],[1,"323","4","Greenhouse Gas Emissions Mitigation Strategy","During the Plan period, Malaysia will adopt a dual strategy in addressing climate change impacts: firstly, adaptation strategies to protect economic growth and development factors from the impact of climate change; and secondly, mitigation strategies to reduce emission of greenhouse gases (GHGs).",""]],"195":[[1,"321","10","Green Technology Application Roadmaps","Develop roadmaps to guide application of green technologies in various sectors, including power generation, transport and construction",""],[1,"321","13","Green Technology Financing Scheme","Establishment of a Green Technology Financing Scheme (GTFS) with a RM1.5 billion fund to encourage investments in green technology, construction and innovation",""],[1,"322","3","Green Curriculum Integration and Certification System","The Government will also introduce a system for formulation of grading and certification mechanisms for competent personnel in green technology;",""],[1,"322","4","Green Technology Soft Loan Scheme","A green technology soft loan scheme of RM1.5 billion has been launched to provide soft loans to companies that supply and utilise green technology, in which the Government bears 2% of the total interest rate and a guarantee of 60% on the financing amount and banking institutions back the remaining 40%.",""],[1,"322","6","Green Technology Research, Development and Commercialisation Initiative","The Government will enhance research, development and commercialisation efforts in green technology through local research centres and industries.",""],[1,"322","6","International Partnership Promotion for Green Technology","The Government will encourage partnerships with foreign institutions such as universities or multi-national companies;",""],[1,"322","7","National Eco-Labelling Scheme and Standards","Ministry of Energy, Green Technology and Water together with Standard and Industrial Research Institute of Malaysia (SIRIM), will develop a national eco-labelling scheme and standards for our products and services that matches international standards.","Ministry of Energy, Green Technology and Water | Standard and Industrial Research Institute of Malaysia (SIRIM)"]],"196":[[1,"321","12","Pollution Prevention and Control Measures","prevention and control of pollution, strengthening institutional capacity, education and awareness efforts and formulation of action and implementation plans",""],[1,"328","4","Clean Air Action Plan Intensification","The implementation of the Clean Air Action Plan will be intensified.",""],[1,"328","5","Motor Vehicle Emission Standards Enforcement and Upgrading","Stricter enforcement on emission standards will be implemented and emission standards will be further improved in line with global standards;",""],[1,"328","6","Transboundary Haze Pollution Prevention and Peatland Fire Management","In partnership with neighbouring countries, the Government will continue to address transboundary haze pollution while strengthening sustainable peatland management efforts in Malaysia to prevent peatland fires;",""],[1,"328","7","Industrial Emissions Regulation Review and Standards Update","Regulations governing industrial emissions will be reviewed with new emission standards for specificindustries.",""],[1,"328","7","Industrial Self-Regulation and Pollution Control System Programme","Industries will be encouraged to self-regulate with the use of pollution control and monitoring systems and environmental audits;",""]],"197":[[1,"323","7","Climate-Related Hazard Risk Assessment Review","The Government will review the value at risk for communities to develop a clear understanding of the cost-benefit trade-offs involved in averting or reducing the impact of such climate-related hazards.",""],[1,"323","8","Climate Risk Assessment and Prioritization Framework","Developing a robust risk framework to assess and quantify the climate risk faced by the economy and prioritise measures to address those risks;",""],[1,"323","9","Climate-Resilient Infrastructure Investment Decision Frameworks","Implementing policy decision frameworks to ensure that future infrastructure investments are climate resilient;",""],[1,"323","10","Climate Prediction and Modelling Capacity Enhancement","Enhancing capacity in the field of climate prediction and modelling to develop stronger Malaysia-specific and sector-specific knowledge.",""]],"198":[[1,"332","8","Concentrated Spatial Growth Strategy","The Government will move towards an approach of concentrated",""],[1,"333","1","Urban Density, Clustering and Specialisation Strategy","adopting strategies to build density, develop clusters and specialise in high value sectors to exploit increasing returns to scale in cities.",""],[1,"333","1","Urban Public Spaces and Cultural Vibrancy Initiative","with a renewed emphasis on creating attractive public spaces and cultivating arts, culture and leisure activities to support an increasingly cosmopolitan population.",""],[1,"333","1","City-Specific Urban Development Strategies","each city will have strategies tailored to its unique heritage, composition and potential opportunity for growth.",""]],"199":[[1,"338","6","Value-Management Approach for Project Planning and Evaluation","A value-management approach towards planning and evaluation of projects will ensure that every project takes into account holistic life-cycle costs and benefits to ensure that every ringgit is well spent.",""],[1,"361","1","Value-Management Analysis and Life-Cycle Cost Evaluation for Procurement","Implementing value-management analysis and life-cycle cost evaluation for procurement.",""]],"200":[[1,"339","4","Devolution of Powers to Frontline Delivery Agencies","Devolving powers to agencies at the frontline of delivery to increase responsiveness and improve speed of decision-making;",""],[1,"346","2","Empowerment and Decentralisation of Authority","During the Plan period, empowerment and decentralisation of authority will be given renewed focus.",""],[1,"346","3","Devolution of Authority to Frontline Agencies","authority will be devolved to frontline agencies to accelerate decision-making and to enable them respond better to increasing expectations from customers.",""],[1,"359","1","Public Sector Function Transfer and Accountability Reform","Transferring non-core operating functions to private sector players with scale and expertise should improve outcomes and potentially save costs.",""],[1,"359","1","Government Capability and Accountability Strengthening","Steps will also be taken to improve capabilities and accountability in the Government to enable the long-term goal of autonomy for ministries and agencies, in return for the delivery of specific outcomes and adherence to pre-determined standards.",""]],"201":[[1,"339","5","Public Service Competition and Market Mechanisms Reform","Introducing competition and other market mechanisms within public services to encourage innovation and improvement;",""],[1,"341","1","Public Service Process Re-engineering and Streamlining","During the Tenth Plan period, efforts will be intensified and expanded to further facilitate services for people, businesses and trade where efficiencies and response times will be benchmarked with international best practices.",""],[1,"341","1","Cross-Agency Service Interface Redesign","Processes and services across agencies will be re-engineered and streamlined to design interfaces that address customer needs and are simple to use, leveraging on the latest technology.",""],[1,"341","2","Service Delivery Improvement and Expansion Initiative","service delivery will be explored to extend outreach.",""],[1,"341","2","Security and Privacy Safeguards for Digital Services","Due attention will be given to security and privacy to safeguard confidential personal and business data and earn the trust and confidence of the public in using these services.",""]],"202":[[1,"341","5","Citizen Registry System","Through the Citizen Registry System (CRS) the public no longer has to provide personal information separately to different agencies every time they make a public service transaction.",""],[1,"342","1","National Single Identification Number System Expansion","This system replaces the multi-agency number currently in use and will be expanded nationwide by 2015.",""]],"203":[[1,"341","7","Integrated Emergency Response Hotline System","With the introduction of MERS 999, the public will be able to seek emergency assistance from the police, hospitals, Fire Departments, and civil defence through a single emergency number.",""],[1,"341","7","Common Dispatch Centre Emergency Response Acceleration","MERS 999 further enables accelerated response to the location of emergency through common despatch centres.",""]],"204":[[1,"342","6","Trustmark Website Certification Scheme","Trustmark is a certification of recognition for public and private sector websites that will help to increase public confidence and adoption of online transactions.",""],[1,"342","7","e-Tanah Land Administration System Expansion","During the Plan period, e-Tanah services will be extended to other states in Peninsular Malaysia, based on successful implementation in Melaka, Negeri Sembilan and Pulau Pinang.",""],[1,"342","8","Local Authority Revenue and Licensing Digitization","Among the services it offers includes revenue management, tax collection, accounting, complaints management and licensing.",""],[1,"348","2","Local Authority Performance Rating System Expansion","During the Plan period, this system will be extended to local authorities in Sabah and Sarawak.",""]],"205":[[1,"343","6","MyGovXchange Single Business Gateway Enhancement","The existing MyGovXchange will be enhanced as the single gateway for businesses, covering registration, licence application, licence expansion as well as applications for loans and grants from various public agencies.",""],[1,"343","8","SSM Enterprise Services Gateway for Simultaneous Company Registration","the SSM Enterprise Services Gateway will enable simultaneous registration across multiple agencies following the incorporation of a company with SSM.",""],[1,"344","1","Business Entity Information System Expansion","The system will be expanded from five agencies to include all public agencies dealing with business entities.",""]],"206":[[1,"345","5","Public-Private Business Facilitation Task Force","A Special Task Force to Facilitate Business (PEMUDAH) is a consultative forum on issues concerning public service delivery and Malaysia's business environment.",""],[1,"345","6","People-Centric Survey Monitoring and Feedback System","Continuous monitoring of people and business perceptions through regular surveys will be conducted to assess the extent to which government programmes are translated into outcomes that people and business can see, touch and feel.",""],[1,"345","6","Policy Feedback Integration Mechanism","Feedback and ideas on improvement from these surveys will be collated as input in the formulation of government policies, plans and programmes.",""]],"207":[[1,"346","5","Strengthening MIDA Negotiation Authority","MIDA will be empowered with additional decision-making authority in negotiations with investors",""],[1,"346","6","MIDA Repositioning as Malaysian Investment Development Authority","MIDA (formerly known as the Malaysian Industrial Development Authority) will be repositioned as the Malaysian Investment Development Authority",""],[1,"346","7","Investment Promotion and Prioritization by MIDA","MIDA will play a critical role in ensuring investments are directed to priority sectors and geographies and that they support innovation and productivity growth",""],[1,"346","8","MIDA Corporatisation Reform","MIDA will be corporatised to enable the necessary organizational flexibility to attract and retain talent it needs to be internationally competitive",""],[1,"346","9","Enhanced MIDA Negotiation Authority for Targeted Projects","MIDA will be empowered with additional decision-making authority in negotiations with investors for targeted projects",""],[1,"346","10","Central Investment Promotion Agency Designation","MIDA will be designated as the central investment promotion agency for the manufacturing and services sectors (excluding utilities and financial services), to enhance the coordination and cohesion among the various investment promotion bodies in the country",""],[1,"347","2","MIDA Empowerment and Corporatisation Reform","MIDA will be empowered as the central investment promotion agency for the manufacturing and services sector as shown in Chart 7-1.",""]],"208":[[1,"347","3","Performance Competition Among Peer Agencies","Greater competition will be introduced to encourage agencies to learn from best practices, be more responsive to the changing demands of customers and to continuously strive for better performance.",""],[1,"347","8","Demand-Side Funding for Tertiary Education","Introducing demand-side funding in tertiary education.",""],[1,"348","1","Student-Centered Higher Education Funding Reform","a portion of funding will be provided to students rather than institutions of higher learning.",""]],"209":[[1,"355","4","Concentrated Industrial Cluster Development Support","Providing the enablers to support the development of concentrated industrial clusters and supporting ecosystem towards enabling specialisation and economies of scale;",""],[1,"355","5","Innovation Enablers Investment Expansion","Increasing investment into the enablers of innovation, particularly R&D and venture capital funding.",""],[1,"359","4","Co-investment Support for Emerging Specialisations","New government investment will be used to accelerate and facilitate emerging specialisations, especially through co-investments with the industry in terms of skills training, R&D and enabling infrastructure.",""],[1,"359","4","Facilitation Support for National Key Economic Areas","Other potential areas for facilitation support include NKEAs, such as education, healthcare and tourism, to help drive these sectors up the value chain.",""]],"210":[[1,"356","17","Reduction of Government Ownership in Non-Core Companies and Assets","Reducing government ownership of non-core companies and assets by transferring stakes to private sector",""],[1,"356","17","Level Playing Field for Government-Present Industries","Creating a level playing field for industries where government maintains presence",""],[1,"357","4","Divestment of Non-Core State Assets","Systematically reduce its ownership and control of non-core assets.",""],[1,"359","2","Privatisation and Divestment of Non-core Government Assets","During the Plan period, the Government will pursue privatisation and divestments of non- core and non-competitive assets that operate in areas where strategic shareholders or innovative entrepreneurs have the potential to create more value.",""],[1,"359","3","Selected Petronas Subsidiaries Privatization via IPO","the privatisation of selected Petronas subsidiaries via initial public offering.",""],[1,"359","3","Privatization of Ministry of Finance Incorporated Companies","Other divestments, include the privatisation of companies under the Ministry of Finance Incorporated such as Percetakan Nasional Malaysia Berhad, CTRM Aero Composite, Nine Bio Sdn Bhd and Inno Bio Sdn Bhd.",""],[1,"359","3","Transparent Public-Interest Divestment Screening","The Government will ensure that any divestment and privatisation is in the public interest, and will use transparent processes to ensure that potential private sector bidders meet a minimum set of criteria.",""]],"211":[[1,"357","2","Strengthen Policy-Making and Independent Regulatory Role","Strengthen its role as policy-maker and independent regulator;",""],[1,"357","7","Separation of Policy-Making and Regulation","Creating structures to separate policy-making from regulation and specifies clear lines of accountability.",""]],"212":[[1,"361","2","Centralised Government Procurement System","Common items, such as office supplies, Information Communications Technology (ICT) and selected services will be procured centrally to achieve savings across government.",""],[1,"361","2","FELDA-FELCRA-RISDA Shared Services Consortium","FELDA, FELCRA and RISDA have started collaborative efforts through a consortium where selected operational activities in these agencies will be undertaken collectively by the consortium as a central provider of shared services.",""],[1,"361","3","Rubber and Oil Palm Supply and Marketing Consortium","The consortium will also allow for technology sharing and capacity building among these agencies.",""],[1,"361","4","Common Procurement Standards and Policy Reform","Strengthening common procurement standards and policies to ensure that ministries and government agencies have autonomy to make fast procurement decisions within these standards and policies;",""]],"213":[[1,"340","6","Foreign Investment Committee Guidelines Deregulation","Deregulation of the Foreign Investment Committee (FIC) Guidelines enabling greater inflow of private investment.",""],[1,"340","8","Automatic Work Permit Approval for High-Salary Expatriates","Automatic approval for work permit applications by expatriates with salaries of more than RM8,000 per month to increase employment of knowledge workers.",""]],"214":[[1,"362","4","Tax Collection Base Expansion","The Government will broaden the tax collection base.",""],[1,"362","4","Enhanced Tax Compliance Enforcement","Tax collection from individuals and businesses that underpay their taxes will be enhanced through:",""],[1,"362","5","Transfer Pricing and Thin Capitalisation Regulation Enforcement","Tightening and enforcing regulations around specific areas of non-compliance, such as transfer pricing and thin capitalisation;",""],[1,"362","6","Enhanced Taxpayer Identification Tools and Analytics","Enhancing tools and analytics that identify individuals and businesses with a high",""],[1,"362","8","Enforcement Capacity Strengthening Programme","Increasing enforcement capacity and capabilities through additional recruitment, more specialised training and enhanced auditing techniques;",""],[1,"362","9","Targeted Compliance Enforcement Campaigns","Focusing specific enforcement campaigns on segments of individuals and businesses that have low levels of compliance;",""],[1,"362","10","Tax Collection Improvement Measures","Improving the collection of taxes through enhanced collection techniques such as contact strategies, closer corporation with the legal system and other agencies, as well as targeted use of legal remedies;",""],[1,"362","11","Dedicated Court Time for Tax Case Resolution","Improving the time taken to handle and settle tax cases through various options such as allocating specific days in a week of court time dedicated to tax issues.",""]],"215":[[1,"364","1","Fisheries Institutional Function Streamlining","The functions of the Department of Fisheries (DOF) and the Malaysian Fisheries Development Board (LKIM) will be streamlined.",""]],"216":[[1,"364","6","Expansion of MIDA's Investment Promotion Mandate","MIDA will have an expanded mandate as the central investment promotion agency for manufacturing and services with decision- making authority in negotiations with investors;",""],[1,"364","7","InnovationMalaysia Unit","Establishing InnovationMalaysia™.",""]],"217":[[1,"409","1","Industrial Commodities Production and Local Processing Expansion","Increase production and local processing of industrial commodities",""],[1,"412","9","BioNexus Status Companies Target","Achieve targeted number of BioNexus status companies",""]],"218":[[1,"410","8","Kuching International Airport Upgrade","Upgrading of Kuching International Airport",""],[1,"410","9","Airport Upgrading Programme","Upgrading of Alor Setar, Kuala Terengganu, Labuan and Melaka Airports",""]],"219":[[1,"411","12","Off-grid Electricity Generation by Palm Oil Millers","430 MW off-grid electricity generation by palm oil millers",""],[1,"411","13","Energy Efficiency Intensification","Intensify energy efficiency",""]],"220":[[1,"415","5","Private Sector Participation in Training and Hands-on Workforce Development","Greater private sector participation in training and increased supply of work force with hands-on training to meet industrial needs",""],[1,"416","10","National School Teaching and Learning Improvement","Improve teaching and learning methods to enhance quality of national schools",""]],"221":[[1,"432","4","Public Participation in Crime Prevention","Encouraging public participation in combating crimes",""]],"222":[[1,"432","6","Water Services Management Efficiency Improvement","Increase efficiency of water services management",""]],"223":[[1,"439","18","Intensive Skill Training for Single Mothers","Intensive Skill Training for Single Mother (Inkubator Kemahiran Ibu Tunggal)",""],[1,"440","32","Early Childhood Development Programme for Children Aged Four and Below","Early Childhood Development Programme for Children Aged Four and Below",""]],"225":[[1,"364","5","Expanded Poverty Eradication Support for Bottom 40% Households","Expanding the efforts of poverty eradicating agencies to support the bottom 40% of households.","Ministry of Rural and Regional Development | Ministry of Agriculture and Agro-based Industries | Ministry of Housing and Local Government | Ministry of Federal Territories and Urban Well-being"]]}});